msgstr "rtmp:// または rtmps:// のアドレスが設定されていません"

#: blocks/broadcast/ui/LiveStreamWords.qml:92
msgctxt "@info:status a live stream"
msgid "This system has no H.264 encoder that works"
msgstr "このシステムには動作する H.264 エンコーダがありません"

#: blocks/broadcast/ui/LiveStreamWords.qml:95
msgctxt "@info:status a live stream"
msgid "The service refused the stream, or its key"
msgstr "サービスがストリームまたはそのキーを拒否しました"

#: blocks/broadcast/ui/NowPlayingRows.qml:96
msgctxt "@label:listbox"
msgid "Now playing"
msgstr "再生中"

#: blocks/broadcast/ui/NowPlayingRows.qml:120
msgctxt "@info:placeholder"
msgid "Its first line is the title"
msgstr "最初の行がタイトルになります"

#: blocks/broadcast/ui/NowPlayingRows.qml:121
msgctxt "@label:textbox"
msgid "File"
msgstr "ファイル"

#: blocks/broadcast/ui/NowPlayingRows.qml:150
msgctxt "@label:listbox"
msgid "Player"
msgstr "プレーヤー"

#: blocks/broadcast/ui/NowPlayingRows.qml:171
msgctxt "@info how a stream's title picks the media player it follows"
msgid ""
"A player this session's Application blocks capture, or the one playing when "
"they capture none."
msgstr "このセッションの「アプリケーション」ブロックが取り込むプレーヤー、または取り込んでいない場合は再生中のプレーヤーです。"

#: blocks/broadcast/ui/NowPlayingRows.qml:177
msgctxt "@title:window"
msgid "Choose the Now Playing File"
msgstr "タイトルを読み込むファイルを選択"

#: blocks/broadcast/ui/NowPlayingRows.qml:178
msgctxt "@item:inlistbox a file type"
msgid "Text files (*.txt)"
msgstr "テキストファイル (*.txt)"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:17
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid ""
"Rearranges the two sides of a stereo lane: swaps them, folds them into one, "
"copies one side to both, or silences or flips one of them."
msgstr ""
"ステレオレーンの左右を組み替えます: 入れ替える、1 "
"つにまとめる、片側を両側にコピーする、片側を無音にする、片側の位相を反転する、といった処理ができます。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:22
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid ""
"Stereo sound has two sides, left and right, one for each speaker or each ear "
"of your headphones. This block decides what each side plays: its own sound, "
"the other side's, a mix of both, or nothing."
msgstr ""
"ステレオの音には左と右の 2 "
"つの側があり、それぞれ左右のスピーカー、またはヘッドホンの左右の耳に対応します。このブロックは、それぞれの側で何を鳴らすかを決めます: "
"その側の音、反対側の音、両方を混ぜた音、または無音です。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid ""
"You choose one action at a time. The block's tile shows the action, and under"
" it where each side now comes from: L→R means the left side's sound is played"
" on the right."
msgstr ""
"処理は一度に 1 つだけ選べます。ブロックのタイルには選んだ処理が表示され、その下に、それぞれの側の音がどこから来ているかが表示されます: L→R "
"は、左の音を右で鳴らしていることを表します。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid ""
"A change of action fades across in a hundredth of a second, so switching "
"while sound plays makes no click."
msgstr "処理を変更すると 100 分の 1 秒かけてフェードして切り替わるので、再生中に切り替えてもクリックノイズは出ません。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:34
#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsPanel.qml:47
msgctxt "@label:listbox what the Channels block does to the two sides"
msgid "Action"
msgstr "処理"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:36
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid ""
"What the block does to the two sides. Click the list to choose another "
"action; the line under it says what the chosen one does. A new block starts "
"at No change."
msgstr ""
"ブロックが左右に対して行う処理です。一覧をクリックすると別の処理を選べ、その下の行に選んだ処理の内容が表示されます。新しいブロックは「変更なし」から始まります。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:39
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block, one choice of Action"
msgid "No change: both sides pass through as they arrive."
msgstr "変更なし: 左右とも、届いたとおりに通します。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:40
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block, one choice of Action"
msgid "Swap sides: the left side plays on the right and the right on the left."
msgstr "左右を入れ替え: 左の音を右で、右の音を左で鳴らします。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:41
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block, one choice of Action"
msgid ""
"Mono: both sides play the average of the two. A sound in the middle keeps its"
" level, and nothing gets louder than the louder side. Sound panned to one "
"side drops 6 dB, and sound out of phase between the sides cancels. One Ear "
"Mix, in the Hearing group, folds them another way."
msgstr ""
"モノラル: 左右の両方で、2 つの平均を鳴らします。中央にある音はレベルが変わらず、大きいほうの側より大きくなることはありません。片側にパンされた音は 6"
" dB 下がり、左右で逆位相の音は打ち消し合います。「聴覚」グループの「片耳ミックス」は、別の方法で左右をまとめます。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:42
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block, the choices of Action"
msgid ""
"Left to both, or Right to both: one side plays on both, and the other side's "
"sound is left out. For a source that arrives on one side only."
msgstr "左を両方に、または右を両方に: 片側の音を左右の両方で鳴らし、反対側の音は使いません。片側だけに届く音源向けです。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:43
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block, the choices of Action"
msgid ""
"Mute left, or Mute right: that side is silent, and the other plays as it is."
msgstr "左をミュート、または右をミュート: その側を無音にし、反対側はそのまま鳴らします。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:44
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block, the choices of Action"
msgid ""
"Invert left, or Invert right: that side is flipped upside down. It sounds the"
" same on its own, but it puts right a microphone or a cable wired the wrong "
"way round, whose side cancels the other out when the two meet."
msgstr ""
"左の位相を反転、または右の位相を反転: "
"その側の波形を上下逆にします。単独で聞くと同じ音ですが、配線が逆になったマイクやケーブル（左右を合わせると打ち消し合ってしまうもの）を正しく直せます。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:45
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block, one choice of Action"
msgid ""
"Difference: both sides play what differs between them. Whatever sits in the "
"middle, often a voice, drops out, and what is spread to the sides stays."
msgstr "差分: 左右の両方で、左右の違いの部分を鳴らします。中央にある音（多くの場合は声）は消え、左右に広がった音は残ります。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:52
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid ""
"A microphone or an instrument arrives on one side only, and you want to hear "
"it on both."
msgstr "マイクや楽器の音が片側だけに届き、それを両側で聞きたいとき。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:53
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid "Left and right are the wrong way round."
msgstr "左右が逆になっているとき。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:54
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid "You hear with one ear only, and want all of the sound on both sides."
msgstr "片方の耳でしか聞こえず、すべての音を両側で鳴らしたいとき。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:55
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid ""
"You want to check how something sounds on a single speaker, such as a "
"phone's."
msgstr "スマートフォンのスピーカーのように、スピーカー 1 つでどう聞こえるかを確かめたいとき。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:56
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid ""
"A stereo mix sounds hollow and thin in mono, as if part of it were cancelling"
" out."
msgstr "ステレオのミックスをモノラルにすると、一部が打ち消し合っているかのように、うつろで薄い音になるとき。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:63
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid ""
"If one side of a stereo source is only noise or silence, choose Left to both "
"or Right to both rather than Mono. Mono would mix the noise in, or halve the "
"level."
msgstr ""
"ステレオ音源の片側がノイズだけか無音の場合は、「モノラル」ではなく「左を両方に」か「右を両方に」を選んでください。「モノラル」だと、ノイズが混ざるか、レベルが半分になります。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:64
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid ""
"If a stereo source goes thin and quiet in Mono, one of its sides is probably "
"flipped. Put a second Channels block, set to Invert left, before the one set "
"to Mono, and listen whether the sound comes back."
msgstr ""
"ステレオ音源が「モノラル」で薄く小さくなる場合は、おそらく片側の位相が反転しています。「モノラル」に設定したブロックの前に、「左の位相を反転」に設定した "
"2 つ目の「チャンネル」ブロックを置き、音が戻るかどうか聞いてみてください。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsHelp.qml:65
msgctxt "@info help page of the Channels block"
msgid ""
"Difference can take a singer out of many songs, for a karaoke track, but "
"anything else in the middle goes with it, often the bass and the drums."
msgstr "「差分」を使うと、多くの曲から歌声を消してカラオケ用の音源にできますが、中央にある他の音（多くの場合はベースやドラム）も一緒に消えます。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsPanel.qml:59
msgctxt "@label:listbox"
msgid "Action"
msgstr "処理"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:28
msgctxt "@item a Channels action that leaves the two sides alone"
msgid "No change"
msgstr "変更なし"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:30
msgctxt "@item a Channels action"
msgid "Swap sides"
msgstr "左右を入れ替え"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:32
msgctxt "@item a Channels action"
msgid "Mono"
msgstr "モノラル"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:34
msgctxt "@item a Channels action"
msgid "Left to both"
msgstr "左を両方に"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:36
msgctxt "@item a Channels action"
msgid "Right to both"
msgstr "右を両方に"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:38
msgctxt "@item a Channels action"
msgid "Mute left"
msgstr "左をミュート"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:40
msgctxt "@item a Channels action"
msgid "Mute right"
msgstr "右をミュート"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:42
msgctxt "@item a Channels action: flip the polarity of the left side"
msgid "Invert left"
msgstr "左の位相を反転"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:44
msgctxt "@item a Channels action: flip the polarity of the right side"
msgid "Invert right"
msgstr "右の位相を反転"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:46
msgctxt "@item a Channels action: the left side minus the right"
msgid "Difference"
msgstr "差分"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:55
msgctxt "@info where each output side comes from: unchanged"
msgid "L→L · R→R"
msgstr "L→L · R→R"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:57
msgctxt "@info where each output side comes from: swapped"
msgid "R→L · L→R"
msgstr "R→L · L→R"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:59
msgctxt "@info where each output side comes from: the average of both"
msgid "L+R → both"
msgstr "L+R → 両方"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:61
msgctxt "@info where each output side comes from: the left"
msgid "L → both"
msgstr "L → 両方"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:63
msgctxt "@info where each output side comes from: the right"
msgid "R → both"
msgstr "R → 両方"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:65
msgctxt "@info where each output side comes from: left silent"
msgid "L off · R→R"
msgstr "L オフ · R→R"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:67
msgctxt "@info where each output side comes from: right silent"
msgid "L→L · R off"
msgstr "L→L · R オフ"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:69
msgctxt "@info where each output side comes from: left inverted"
msgid "−L→L · R→R"
msgstr "−L→L · R→R"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:71
msgctxt "@info where each output side comes from: right inverted"
msgid "L→L · −R→R"
msgstr "L→L · −R→R"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:73
msgctxt "@info where each output side comes from: left minus right"
msgid "L−R → both"
msgstr "L−R → 両方"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:82
msgctxt "@info what the Channels action does"
msgid "Passes both sides through as they arrive."
msgstr "左右とも、届いたとおりに通します。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:85
msgctxt "@info what the Channels action does"
msgid "Puts the left side on the right and the right on the left."
msgstr "左の音を右に、右の音を左にします。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:88
msgctxt "@info what the Channels action does"
msgid ""
"Averages the two sides and plays the result on both. Sound panned to one side"
" drops 6 dB, and sound out of phase between the sides cancels. One Ear Mix, "
"in the Hearing group, folds them another way."
msgstr ""
"左右を平均し、その結果を両側で鳴らします。片側にパンされた音は 6 dB "
"下がり、左右で逆位相の音は打ち消し合います。「聴覚」グループの「片耳ミックス」は、別の方法で左右をまとめます。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:91
msgctxt "@info what the Channels action does"
msgid "Plays the left side on both, for a source that only arrives on one."
msgstr "左の音を両側で鳴らします。片側だけに届く音源向けです。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:94
msgctxt "@info what the Channels action does"
msgid "Plays the right side on both, for a source that only arrives on one."
msgstr "右の音を両側で鳴らします。片側だけに届く音源向けです。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:97
msgctxt "@info what the Channels action does"
msgid "Silences the left side and leaves the right as it is."
msgstr "左を無音にし、右はそのままにします。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:100
msgctxt "@info what the Channels action does"
msgid "Silences the right side and leaves the left as it is."
msgstr "右を無音にし、左はそのままにします。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:103
msgctxt "@info what the Channels action does"
msgid ""
"Flips the left side upside down, for a cable or microphone wired the wrong "
"way round."
msgstr "左の波形を上下逆にします。配線が逆になったケーブルやマイク向けです。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:106
msgctxt "@info what the Channels action does"
msgid ""
"Flips the right side upside down, for a cable or microphone wired the wrong "
"way round."
msgstr "右の波形を上下逆にします。配線が逆になったケーブルやマイク向けです。"

#: blocks/channels/ui/ChannelsWords.qml:109
msgctxt "@info what the Channels action does"
msgid ""
"Plays what differs between the sides on both. Whatever sits in the middle, "
"often a voice, drops out."
msgstr "左右の違いの部分を両側で鳴らします。中央にある音（多くの場合は声）は消えます。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/CutoffFace.qml:58
msgctxt ""
"@info:tooltip a cutoff filter's settings, 'Cutoff 8.00 kHz, 12 dB per octave'"
msgid "Cutoff %1, %2"
msgstr "カットオフ %1、%2"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/CutoffFace.qml:105
#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/CutoffPanel.qml:71
#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:38
#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:36
msgctxt "@label:slider a cutoff filter's cutoff frequency"
msgid "Cutoff"
msgstr "カットオフ"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/CutoffPanel.qml:61
msgctxt "@label a cutoff filter's cutoff frequency"
msgid "Cutoff:"
msgstr "カットオフ:"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/CutoffPanel.qml:95
#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:40
#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:37
msgctxt "@label:textbox a cutoff frequency to type"
msgid "Cutoff in hertz"
msgstr "カットオフ周波数（Hz）"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/CutoffPanel.qml:123
msgctxt "@label how steeply a filter rolls off"
msgid "Slope:"
msgstr "スロープ:"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:19
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"Takes away the deep sound below a pitch you choose, and lets everything above"
" it pass. Use it to clean rumble, hum from handling and the boom of a room "
"out of a voice."
msgstr ""
"選んだ高さより低い音を取り除き、それより上の音はすべて通します。声から、ゴロゴロという低いノイズ、マイクに触れたときのノイズ、部屋のこもった響きを取り除くのに使います。"

#. i18n: Hz stands for hertz.
#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"Pitch is measured in hertz (Hz): low numbers are deep sounds, high numbers "
"bright ones. The lowest note of a piano is about 27 Hz, and a man's speaking "
"voice has little below about 80 Hz."
msgstr ""
"音の高さはヘルツ（Hz）で測ります。数値が小さいほど低い音、大きいほど明るい音です。ピアノの最低音は約 27 Hz で、男性の話し声には約 80 Hz "
"より下の成分はほとんどありません。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"Sound above the cutoff passes as it is. Below it the sound fades away, more "
"and more the deeper it goes. Right at the cutoff it is already a little "
"quieter, by 3 decibels (dB), to about 70 % of its strength."
msgstr ""
"カットオフより上の音はそのまま通ります。それより下では、低くなるほど音が弱まっていきます。カットオフちょうどの位置でも、すでに 3 "
"デシベル（dB）小さくなり、強さは約 70% になっています。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:27
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"A new block starts at 20 Hz, the bottom of what people can hear, so it "
"changes nothing you would notice until you move the cutoff up."
msgstr "新しいブロックは、人に聞こえる下限である 20 Hz から始まるので、カットオフを上げるまでは、気付くような変化はありません。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:28
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"The cutoff can be moved while sound plays: it sweeps to the new place in a "
"few hundredths of a second rather than jumping. Changing the slope fades from"
" one to the other, so neither makes a click."
msgstr ""
"カットオフは音の再生中にも動かせます。急に跳ぶのではなく、100 "
"分の数秒かけて新しい位置まで滑らかに移ります。スロープを変えると前後の設定がクロスフェードするので、どちらの操作でもクリック音は出ません。"

#. i18n: kHz stands for kilohertz, a thousand hertz.
#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:44
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"The pitch below which sound is taken away, from 20 Hz to 2 kilohertz (kHz), "
"which is 2000 Hz. Drag the slider here or on the block's tile; it gives the "
"low pitches as much room as the high ones."
msgstr ""
"これより低い音が取り除かれる高さで、20 Hz から 2 キロヘルツ（kHz）、つまり 2000 Hz "
"までです。ここかブロックのタイルでスライダーをドラッグしてください。スライダーは、低い音域にも高い音域と同じだけの幅を割り当てています。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:45
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"For an exact number, type it in the box beside the slider and press Enter. A "
"k means thousand, so 1.5k is 1500 Hz. A number outside the range is brought "
"to its nearest end."
msgstr ""
"正確な値にするには、スライダーの横のボックスに数値を入力して Enter キーを押してください。k は 1000 を表すので、1.5k は 1500 Hz"
" です。範囲外の数値は、近い方の端の値になります。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:51
#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:46
msgctxt "@label how steeply a filter rolls off"
msgid "Slope"
msgstr "スロープ"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:57
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"How quickly the sound fades below the cutoff. An octave is a halving of the "
"pitch: from 100 Hz down to 50 Hz, for example."
msgstr ""
"カットオフより下で、音がどれだけ急に弱まるかです。1 オクターブは周波数が半分になることで、たとえば 100 Hz から 50 Hz までです。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:60
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block, one choice of Slope"
msgid ""
"12 dB/oct: gentle. Each octave below the cutoff is 12 dB quieter, about a "
"quarter of the strength. It sounds natural, and is where a new block starts."
msgstr ""
"12 dB/oct: 緩やかです。カットオフから 1 オクターブ下がるごとに 12 dB 小さくなり、強さは約 4 分の 1 "
"になります。自然に聞こえ、新しいブロックはこの設定から始まります。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:61
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block, one choice of Slope"
msgid ""
"24 dB/oct: steep. Each octave below the cutoff is 24 dB quieter, so the "
"rumble goes while the sound just above the cutoff stays."
msgstr ""
"24 dB/oct: 急峻です。カットオフから 1 オクターブ下がるごとに 24 dB "
"小さくなるので、カットオフのすぐ上の音を残したまま、低いゴロゴロ音を消せます。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:68
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"A microphone picks up the rumble of traffic, a fan or an air conditioner."
msgstr "マイクが、車の走行音、ファン、エアコンの低いゴロゴロ音を拾うとき。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:69
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"You hear thumps when somebody touches the microphone or its stand, or bumps "
"the desk."
msgstr "誰かがマイクやスタンドに触れたり、机にぶつかったりしたときに、ドンという音が聞こえるとき。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:70
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid "A voice sounds boomy or muddy, especially close to the microphone."
msgstr "特にマイクに近いときに、声がこもったり濁ったりして聞こえるとき。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:71
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid "Small speakers distort on deep sound they cannot play anyway."
msgstr "小さなスピーカーが、どのみち再生できない低音で音割れするとき。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:78
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"For speech, start at about 80 Hz and raise the cutoff until the voice starts "
"to sound thin, then back off a little."
msgstr "話し声の場合は約 80 Hz から始め、声が薄く聞こえ始めるまでカットオフを上げてから、少し戻してください。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:79
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid "Keep the cutoff low for music: its bass is usually wanted."
msgstr "音楽ではカットオフを低くしておいてください。音楽の低音は、たいてい必要な音です。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:80
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"Put the filter early in the lane, before a compressor or Auto Level, so they "
"do not react to rumble you are going to take away anyway."
msgstr ""
"フィルタはレーンの前の方、コンプレッサーや「オートレベル」より前に置いてください。そうすれば、どのみち取り除く低いノイズに、それらが反応しなくなります。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/HighPassHelp.qml:81
msgctxt "@info help page of the High Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"To take away the high sound instead, such as hiss, use the Low Pass Filter."
msgstr "逆にヒスノイズのような高い音を取り除くには、「ローパスフィルタ」を使ってください。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:17
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"Lets the low and middle sounds through and rolls off everything above a "
"frequency you choose. Use it to take hiss and other high noise out of a "
"source."
msgstr "低音と中音を通し、選んだ周波数より上の音をすべてなだらかに弱めます。音源からヒスノイズなどの高いノイズを取り除くのに使います。"

#. i18n: Hz stands for hertz, kHz for kilohertz.
#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"Every sound is made of frequencies, counted in hertz (Hz): how many times a "
"second the air shakes. Low ones are the bass and the body of a voice; high "
"ones are the hiss, the crispness of an “s” and the sparkle of cymbals. A "
"thousand hertz is a kilohertz (kHz)."
msgstr ""
"どんな音も周波数でできています。周波数はヘルツ（Hz）で数え、空気が 1 "
"秒間に何回振動するかを表します。低い周波数は低音や声の太さ、高い周波数はヒスノイズ、「s」の歯切れ、シンバルのきらめきです。1000 ヘルツが 1 "
"キロヘルツ（kHz）です。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"Below the cutoff, the sound passes as it was. At the cutoff it is already a "
"little quieter, and above it the sound gets quieter and quieter the higher it"
" goes, at the rate the slope sets."
msgstr ""
"カットオフより下の音は、そのまま通ります。カットオフの位置ではすでに少し小さくなっていて、それより上では、スロープで決まる割合で、高くなるほど音が小さくなっていきます。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"A new block starts with the cutoff at 20 kHz, about as high as anybody hears,"
" so it changes nothing until you bring the cutoff down."
msgstr "新しいブロックは、人に聞こえるほぼ上限である 20 kHz のカットオフから始まるので、カットオフを下げるまでは何も変わりません。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"The cutoff glides to a new setting over a few hundredths of a second, so you "
"can drag it while the sound plays and hear it sweep without clicks. The sound"
" is not delayed."
msgstr ""
"カットオフは 100 分の数秒かけて新しい設定へ滑らかに移るので、音の再生中にドラッグしても、クリック音なしに変化を聞けます。音は遅延しません。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:39
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"Where the roll-off starts, from 200 Hz to 20 kHz. Drag the slider, which "
"gives each octave the same room, or type an exact number in the box beside it"
" and press Enter."
msgstr ""
"減衰が始まる位置で、200 Hz〜20 kHz です。どのオクターブにも同じ幅を割り当てたスライダーをドラッグするか、横のボックスに正確な数値を入力して "
"Enter キーを押してください。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:40
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"In the box, 8000, 8k and 8 kHz all mean the same. A number outside the range "
"is brought to its nearest end."
msgstr "ボックスでは、8000、8k、8 kHz はどれも同じ意味です。範囲外の数値は、近い方の端の値になります。"

#. i18n: dB/oct stands for decibels per octave.
#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:53
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"How quickly the sound fades above the cutoff, in decibels (dB) per octave. An"
" octave is a doubling of the frequency, and every 6 dB less is about half the"
" strength."
msgstr ""
"カットオフより上で音がどれだけ急に弱まるかで、1 オクターブあたりのデシベル（dB）で表します。1 オクターブは周波数が 2 倍になることで、6 dB "
"小さくなるごとに強さは約半分になります。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:56
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block, one choice of Slope"
msgid ""
"12 dB/oct: gentle. One octave above the cutoff, the sound has about a quarter"
" of its strength. It sounds natural, and a new block uses it."
msgstr ""
"12 dB/oct: 緩やかです。カットオフの 1 オクターブ上で、音の強さは約 4 分の 1 "
"になります。自然に聞こえ、新しいブロックはこの設定を使います。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:57
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block, one choice of Slope"
msgid ""
"24 dB/oct: steep. One octave above the cutoff, the sound is down to a "
"sixteenth. Use it when the noise sits close above what you want to keep."
msgstr ""
"24 dB/oct: 急峻です。カットオフの 1 オクターブ上で、音は 16 分の 1 になります。残したい音のすぐ上にノイズがある場合に使います。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:60
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid "Changing the slope fades from one to the other, so it makes no click."
msgstr "スロープを変えると前後の設定がクロスフェードするので、クリック音は出ません。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:67
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid "An old recording or a cheap microphone hisses."
msgstr "古い録音や安価なマイクで、サーッというノイズが出るとき。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:68
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"A sound is too sharp or too bright, and you want it duller or further away."
msgstr "音が鋭すぎたり明るすぎたりするので、もっと柔らかく、または遠くに聞こえるようにしたいとき。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:69
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid "You want a sound to be muffled on purpose, as if heard through a wall."
msgstr "壁越しに聞こえるように、わざと音をこもらせたいとき。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:76
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"Start at the top and bring the cutoff down slowly while you listen. Stop as "
"soon as the hiss is gone, before the sound you want gets dull."
msgstr "一番上から始めて、聞きながらカットオフをゆっくり下げてください。ヒスノイズが消えたらすぐ、必要な音がこもる前に止めます。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:77
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"For speech, try a cutoff around 8 kHz first: it takes away much of the hiss "
"and keeps the words clear."
msgstr "話し声の場合は、まず 8 kHz 前後のカットオフを試してください。ヒスノイズの多くを取り除きつつ、言葉ははっきり残ります。"

#: blocks/cutofffilter/ui/LowPassHelp.qml:78
msgctxt "@info help page of the Low Pass Filter block"
msgid ""
"To take away a low rumble instead, use the High Pass Filter. The two together"
" keep only the range in between."
msgstr "逆に低いゴロゴロ音を取り除くには、「ハイパスフィルタ」を使ってください。両方を組み合わせると、その間の帯域だけが残ります。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickFace.qml:85
msgctxt "@label what the number on a Declick tile is"
msgid "threshold"
msgstr "スレッショルド"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickFace.qml:104 blocks/declick/ui/DeclickPanel.qml:57
msgctxt "@label:slider how far a click has to stand out to be taken out"
msgid "Threshold"
msgstr "スレッショルド"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:17
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"Takes clicks and pops out of the sound, and fills each gap with what most "
"likely was there. Use it on a record's crackle, a crackling cable or a stream"
" that drops out for an instant."
msgstr ""
"音からクリックやポップノイズを取り除き、それぞれの隙間を、本来あったと思われる音で埋めます。レコードのパチパチという音、接触の悪いケーブルの雑音、一瞬途切れるストリームなどに使います。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:22
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"Music and speech change smoothly from one moment to the next, so the block "
"can guess, at every moment, what comes next from what came before. A click "
"cannot be guessed: it appears from nowhere. Where the sound suddenly differs "
"from the guess by much more than usual, the block takes it for a click."
msgstr ""
"音楽や話し声は瞬間ごとに滑らかに変化するので、ブロックはそれまでの音から、次に来る音を常に予測できます。クリックは予測できません: "
"どこからともなく現れるからです。音が予測から急に普段よりずっと大きく外れたところを、ブロックはクリックと見なします。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"It also finds a dropout: a few moments of complete silence in the middle of "
"sound, as when a digital stream loses a little of itself."
msgstr "音の途切れ（ドロップアウト）も見つけます: デジタルストリームの一部が欠けたときのように、音の途中でほんの一瞬だけ完全な無音になるものです。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"Each click is cut out and the gap filled in from the sound on both sides of "
"it, so it fits in with what is around it. A click up to three thousandths of "
"a second long is mended this way. A longer noise, such as a scratch that "
"rumbles, is not a click to this block."
msgstr ""
"クリックはそれぞれ切り取られ、その隙間は前後の音から埋められるので、周りの音と自然につながります。この方法で修復できるのは、長さ 1000 分の 3 "
"秒までのクリックです。ゴロゴロと鳴る傷のような長いノイズは、このブロックではクリックとして扱いません。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"The left and the right side are mended each on its own. Sound with no clicks "
"in it passes through unchanged."
msgstr "左と右は、それぞれ別々に修復されます。クリックを含まない音は、そのまま通ります。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"To have sound on both sides of every click, the block works on a fiftieth of "
"a second at a time, and holds the sound back by about a sixtieth of a second."
" Reverblabr keeps the other lanes in step with that delay."
msgstr ""
"すべてのクリックの前後に音があるように、ブロックは一度に 50 分の 1 秒ずつ処理し、音を約 60 分の 1 秒遅らせます。Reverblabr "
"は、他のレーンをこの遅延に合わせます。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:27
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"While the session runs, the settings show how many clicks the block has taken"
" out since it started."
msgstr "セッションの実行中は、開始してからブロックが取り除いたクリックの数が設定に表示されます。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:37 blocks/declick/ui/DeclickPanel.qml:81
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Threshold"
msgstr "スレッショルド"

#. i18n: dB stands for decibels.
#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:40
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"How much a sound has to stand out from the guess before it counts as a click,"
" in decibels (dB), from 0 to 20 dB. A new block starts at 3 dB."
msgstr ""
"音が予測からどれだけ外れたらクリックと見なすかを、デシベル（dB）で、0〜20 dB の範囲で設定します。新しいブロックは 3 dB から始まります。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:41
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"Lower is more sensitive: the block finds fainter clicks, but now and then it "
"also takes the sharp start of a note for one, and changes it a little. Higher"
" is less sensitive: only the loudest clicks are taken out."
msgstr ""
"低くすると感度が上がります: かすかなクリックも見つけますが、ときどき音の鋭い出だしもクリックと見なし、少し変えてしまいます。高くすると感度が下がります:"
" 最も大きなクリックだけが取り除かれます。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:42
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid "A change takes effect at once, while the sound plays."
msgstr "変更は、音の再生中でもすぐに反映されます。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:49
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"You are recording or listening to a vinyl record, and its crackle bothers "
"you."
msgstr "アナログレコードを録音または再生していて、パチパチという音が気になるとき。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:50
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid "A loose cable or a dirty connector adds pops to a microphone."
msgstr "緩んだケーブルや汚れたコネクターのせいで、マイクの音にポップノイズが入るとき。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:51
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"A stream or a call drops out for a moment now and then, and each dropout "
"ticks."
msgstr "ストリームや通話がときどき一瞬途切れ、そのたびにプチッという音がするとき。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:58
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"Start at 3 dB. If clicks are still there, lower the threshold a step at a "
"time until they go."
msgstr "まずは 3 dB で始めてください。クリックが残る場合は、消えるまでスレッショルドを少しずつ下げてください。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:59
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"If sharp sounds such as a drum or a plucked string lose a little of their "
"edge, raise the threshold again."
msgstr "ドラムや弦をはじく音など、鋭い音の歯切れが少し失われる場合は、スレッショルドを上げ直してください。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:60
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"Watch the count of clicks taken out on a quiet passage. If it keeps climbing "
"where you hear no clicks, the threshold is too low."
msgstr "静かな部分で、取り除いたクリックの数を見てください。クリックが聞こえないのに数が増え続ける場合は、スレッショルドが低すぎます。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickHelp.qml:61
msgctxt "@info help page of the Declick block"
msgid ""
"Put the block early in the lane, before the blocks that change the sound, so "
"that it hears the clicks as they arrived."
msgstr "このブロックはレーンの前のほう、音を変えるブロックより前に置いてください。そうすれば、届いたままの状態でクリックを聞き取れます。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickPanel.qml:102
msgctxt "@label the low end of the Declick threshold"
msgid "More sensitive"
msgstr "高感度"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickPanel.qml:109
msgctxt "@label the high end of the Declick threshold"
msgid "Less sensitive"
msgstr "低感度"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickPanel.qml:125
msgctxt "@info what the Declick block does"
msgid ""
"Takes out clicks and pops, from a record's crackle to a digital dropout, and "
"fills in what was underneath from the sound either side. Lower the threshold "
"to catch fainter clicks."
msgstr ""
"レコードのパチパチという音からデジタルの途切れまで、クリックやポップノイズを取り除き、その下にあった音を前後の音から埋めます。かすかなクリックも捉えるには、スレッショルドを下げてください。"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickWords.qml:16
msgctxt "@info a Declick threshold in decibels, '3.0 dB'"
msgid "%1 dB"
msgstr "%1 dB"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickWords.qml:22
msgctxt "@info a running Declick that has found nothing yet"
msgid "No clicks taken out yet"
msgstr "除去したクリック: まだなし"

#: blocks/declick/ui/DeclickWords.qml:24
msgctxt "@info how many clicks a Declick has taken out since it started"
msgid "%1 click taken out"
msgid_plural "%1 clicks taken out"
msgstr[0] "除去したクリック: %1 個"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumFace.qml:45
msgctxt ""
"@info:tooltip a Dehum block's settings with Auto on, 'Hum followed from 50.0 "
"Hz, 30 dB down'"
msgid "Hum followed from %1, %2"
msgstr "ハムを %1 から追従、%2"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumFace.qml:47
msgctxt "@info:tooltip a Dehum block's settings, 'Hum at 50.0 Hz, 30 dB down'"
msgid "Hum at %1, %2"
msgstr "ハム %1、%2"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumFace.qml:148
msgctxt ""
"@label:slider a Dehum block's base frequency, followed automatically, short"
msgid "Base (auto)"
msgstr "基本（自動）"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumFace.qml:149
msgctxt "@label:slider a Dehum block's base frequency, short"
msgid "Base"
msgstr "基本"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumFace.qml:161 blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:63
#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumPanel.qml:175
msgctxt "@label:slider how much a Dehum block takes out"
msgid "Amount"
msgstr "除去量"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:17
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"Takes out the low hum that mains electricity leaves in a recording, and the "
"buzz of its overtones above it, while the rest of the sound stays as it was."
msgstr "電源の電気が録音に残す低いハムと、その上に重なる倍音のブーンという音を取り除き、それ以外の音はそのまま残します。"

#. i18n: Hz stands for hertz; the sentence explains it.
#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"The electricity in the wall changes direction 50 or 60 times a second, "
"depending on the country. A badly earthed cable, a guitar amplifier or a "
"cheap power supply can let that into the sound as a deep, steady hum at 50 or"
" 60 hertz (Hz), which means vibrations a second."
msgstr ""
"コンセントの電気は、国によって 1 秒間に 50 回または 60 "
"回向きが変わります。アースが不十分なケーブル、ギターアンプ、安価な電源などを通じて、それが 50 または 60 "
"ヘルツ（Hz）の低く一定したハムとして音に入り込むことがあります。ヘルツとは 1 秒あたりの振動の回数のことです。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"A hum is rarely alone. It comes with overtones, called harmonics, at two, "
"three, four times its frequency and more, which make it sound like a buzz."
msgstr ""
"ハムが単独で現れることはまれです。周波数の 2 倍、3 倍、4 "
"倍、さらにその上に、倍音（ハーモニクス）と呼ばれる音を伴い、それがブーンという音に聞こえさせます。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"The block cuts a very narrow notch out of the sound at the hum's frequency "
"and at each harmonic, up to the tenth. The lowest notch is only 2 Hz wide, "
"and the tenth about 6 Hz, so a voice or an instrument between them is left "
"almost exactly as it was."
msgstr ""
"ブロックは、ハムの周波数と、10 番目までの各倍音の位置で、音からごく狭い切り込み（ノッチ）を切り取ります。最も低いノッチの幅はわずか 2 Hz、10 "
"番目でも約 6 Hz なので、その間にある声や楽器はほぼ元のまま残ります。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"A change of any setting glides in over three hundredths of a second, so "
"nothing clicks. The block adds no delay."
msgstr "どの設定の変更も 100 分の 3 秒かけて滑らかに反映されるので、クリック音は出ません。ブロックによる遅延はありません。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:36 blocks/dehum/ui/DehumPanel.qml:72
msgctxt "@label which mains frequency a Dehum block takes out"
msgid "Mains"
msgstr "電源周波数"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:38
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"Sets the base frequency to 50 Hz or 60 Hz in one press. Most of the world "
"uses 50 Hz; North America and some other countries use 60 Hz. A new block "
"starts at 50 Hz."
msgstr ""
"1 回押すだけで基本周波数を 50 Hz または 60 Hz に設定します。世界のほとんどの地域は 50 Hz で、北米などの一部の国は 60 Hz "
"です。新しいブロックは 50 Hz から始まります。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:44 blocks/dehum/ui/DehumPanel.qml:108
msgctxt "@label:slider a Dehum block's base frequency"
msgid "Base frequency"
msgstr "基本周波数"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:46
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"The hum's own frequency, from 48 to 62 Hz in tenths of a hertz. Every notch "
"is placed from it: the harmonics are at whole multiples of it."
msgstr ""
"ハムそのものの周波数で、48〜62 Hz の範囲を 0.1 Hz 単位で設定します。すべてのノッチはこれを基準に配置されます: "
"倍音はこの整数倍の位置にあります。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:47
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"Use it when the hum is a little off 50 or 60 Hz, as with a generator, or with"
" a tape that plays a little fast or slow."
msgstr "発電機の場合や、テープの再生速度が少し速いか遅い場合など、ハムが 50 Hz や 60 Hz から少しずれているときに使います。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:53 blocks/dehum/ui/DehumPanel.qml:137
msgctxt "@option:check"
msgid "Follow a drifting hum automatically"
msgstr "ずれるハムに自動で追従"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:55
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"With Auto on, the block listens for the hum while the session runs and moves "
"the notches with it when its frequency wanders. It starts looking at the base"
" frequency, and checks what it finds against the second and third harmonics, "
"so a note in the music does not lead it away."
msgstr ""
"「自動」がオンのとき、ブロックはセッションの実行中にハムを聞き取り、その周波数がずれるとノッチを一緒に動かします。探し始めるのは基本周波数からで、見つけたものを"
" 2 番目と 3 番目の倍音と照らし合わせるので、音楽の音につられて外れることはありません。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:56
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"The line under the switch says what it is doing: which frequency it is "
"following, to a hundredth of a hertz, or that it hears no hum and holds the "
"notches where they were."
msgstr ""
"スイッチの下の行に動作の状態が表示されます: 追従している周波数（0.01 Hz 単位）か、ハムが聞こえないためノッチを元の位置に保っていることです。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:57
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"With Auto on, the notches are a little wider, to keep hold of a hum on the "
"move. It is off for a new block."
msgstr "「自動」がオンのときは、動くハムを捉え続けるために、ノッチが少し広くなります。新しいブロックではオフです。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:65
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"How deep the notches go, from 0 to 10. Each step is 6 dB deeper, and the line"
" under the slider says how far the hum is turned down: 30 dB at 5, where a "
"new block starts, and 60 dB at 10."
msgstr ""
"ノッチの深さで、0〜10 です。1 段階ごとに 6 dB 深くなり、スライダーの下の行にハムをどれだけ下げているかが表示されます: "
"5（新しいブロックの初期値）で 30 dB、10 で 60 dB です。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:66
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid "At 0 the line says Off, and the sound passes through untouched."
msgstr "0 では行に「オフ」と表示され、音はそのまま通過します。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:72 blocks/dehum/ui/DehumPanel.qml:215
msgctxt "@label:spinbox"
msgid "Harmonics"
msgstr "倍音"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:74
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"How many notches there are, counting the base frequency as the first: from 1,"
" the hum alone, to 10, the hum and nine harmonics above it. A new block takes"
" out all ten."
msgstr ""
"ノッチの数で、基本周波数を 1 つ目として数えます: 1（ハムのみ）から 10（ハムとその上の 9 つの倍音）までです。新しいブロックは 10 "
"個すべてを取り除きます。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:81
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"A recording or a microphone has a low hum you can hear in the quiet parts."
msgstr "録音やマイクに、静かな部分で聞こえる低いハムがあるとき。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:82
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid "An electric guitar or a turntable buzzes through its amplifier."
msgstr "エレキギターやターンテーブルが、アンプを通すとブーンと鳴るとき。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:83
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"You are digitising old tapes, and their hum moves up and down with the speed "
"of the tape."
msgstr "古いテープをデジタル化していて、テープの速度に合わせてハムが上下するとき。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:90
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"Try 50 Hz first, then 60 Hz. The right one makes the hum disappear; the wrong"
" one leaves it."
msgstr "まず 50 Hz、次に 60 Hz を試してください。正しいほうではハムが消え、間違ったほうでは残ります。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:91
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"Turn Amount only as high as you need. Deep notches are harmless to most "
"sound, but a low bass note that falls exactly on one can lose a little."
msgstr ""
"「除去量」は必要な分だけ上げてください。深いノッチはほとんどの音には無害ですが、ちょうどノッチの位置に重なる低音は少し失われることがあります。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:92
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"If the deep hum is gone but some of the buzz above it is left, the hum is "
"probably a little off its frequency, and the higher harmonics miss their "
"notches. Turn on Auto, or move the base frequency slowly until the buzz goes."
msgstr ""
"低いハムは消えたのに、その上のブーンという音が少し残る場合は、ハムの周波数が少しずれていて、高い倍音がノッチから外れている可能性があります。「自動」をオンにするか、ブーンという音が消えるまで基本周波数をゆっくり動かしてください。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumHelp.qml:93
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dehum block"
msgid ""
"Fewer harmonics leave more of the sound alone. If the buzz is gone at 4 or 5,"
" you do not need the rest."
msgstr "倍音の数を減らすほど、音に手を加える部分が少なくなります。4 か 5 でブーンという音が消えるなら、残りは必要ありません。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumPanel.qml:68
msgctxt "@label which mains frequency a Dehum block takes out"
msgid "Mains:"
msgstr "電源周波数:"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumPanel.qml:96
msgctxt "@label:slider a Dehum block's base frequency"
msgid "Base:"
msgstr "基本:"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumPanel.qml:135
msgctxt "@label a Dehum block's Auto setting"
msgid "Auto:"
msgstr "自動:"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumPanel.qml:136
msgctxt "@option:check a Dehum block follows a hum whose frequency drifts"
msgid "Follow a drifting hum"
msgstr "ずれるハムに追従"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumPanel.qml:163
msgctxt "@label:slider how much a Dehum block takes out"
msgid "Amount:"
msgstr "除去量:"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumPanel.qml:212
msgctxt "@label:spinbox how many harmonics of the hum a Dehum block takes out"
msgid "Harmonics:"
msgstr "倍音:"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumPanel.qml:229
msgctxt "@info"
msgid ""
"Takes the hum of the mains supply out of the sound, and the whine of its "
"harmonics above it, leaving what lies between them alone."
msgstr "電源のハムと、その上に重なる倍音の甲高いうなりを音から取り除き、その間にある音はそのまま残します。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumWords.qml:15
msgctxt "@info a mains hum's base frequency"
msgid "%1 Hz"
msgstr "%1 Hz"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumWords.qml:20
msgctxt "@info a hum's base frequency as a Dehum block follows it"
msgid "%1 Hz"
msgstr "%1 Hz"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumWords.qml:27
msgctxt "@info a Dehum block with Auto on, before its session runs"
msgid "While it runs, it follows the hum, starting from Base."
msgstr "実行中は「基本」から始めてハムに追従します。"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumWords.qml:29
msgctxt "@info a Dehum block locked onto a hum; %1 is its frequency"
msgid "Following the hum at %1"
msgstr "%1 のハムに追従中"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumWords.qml:30
msgctxt ""
"@info a Dehum block with Auto on and no hum to follow; %1 is where it holds"
msgid "No hum to follow: holding at %1"
msgstr "追従するハムなし: %1 で保持"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumWords.qml:35
msgctxt "@item a mains supply's frequency"
msgid "%1 Hz"
msgstr "%1 Hz"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumWords.qml:46
msgctxt "@info a Dehum block that takes nothing out"
msgid "Off"
msgstr "オフ"

#: blocks/dehum/ui/DehumWords.qml:47
msgctxt "@info how deep a Dehum block's notches go"
msgid "%1 dB down"
msgstr "%1 dB 低減"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:20
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"Learns what a background noise sounds like, such as a fan, a hiss, or the "
"buzzing and ticking a sound card picks up from the computer, and then takes "
"that noise out of everything that follows."
msgstr ""
"ファンの音、サーという音、サウンドカードがコンピュータから拾うブーンやチリチリという音など、背景ノイズの音を学習し、それ以降のすべての音からそのノイズを取り除きます。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"The block first has to hear the noise on its own. Press Learn Noise while "
"only the noise plays: the block listens for ten seconds. At every pitch, from"
" the lowest to the highest, it remembers how loud the noise gets, not only "
"how loud it usually is, so a noise that ticks, crackles or comes and goes is "
"learned with its loudest moments. While it listens, the sound passes through "
"as it is."
msgstr ""
"ブロックはまず、ノイズだけを聞く必要があります。ノイズだけが鳴っている状態で「ノイズを学習」を押すと、ブロックが 10 "
"秒間聞き取ります。最も低い音から最も高い音まで、あらゆる高さについて、ノイズの普段の大きさだけでなく最大の大きさも覚えるので、カチカチ、パチパチと鳴ったり、出たり消えたりするノイズも、最も大きい瞬間まで含めて学習されます。聞き取りの間、音はそのまま通ります。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"From then on, it splits the sound into many narrow bands of pitch, about a "
"thousand of them, in groups of an octave. A group that holds nothing louder "
"than the learned noise is turned down as a whole, so the noise's own ticks "
"cannot get through. In a group where something else is going on, such as a "
"voice or music, the bands where it rises above the noise pass, and the others"
" are turned down."
msgstr ""
"その後は、音を約 1000 本の細い帯域に分け、それを 1 "
"オクターブごとのグループにまとめます。学習したノイズより大きい音を含まないグループは、まとめて音量を下げるので、ノイズ自体のカチカチという音も通りません。声や音楽など他の音があるグループでは、その音がノイズを上回る帯域は通し、それ以外の帯域は下げます。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:27
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"A computer's noise often grows when the computer works harder. When the whole"
" noise becomes a little louder, the block follows it, by up to ten decibels, "
"and never lower than what it learned."
msgstr ""
"コンピュータのノイズは、コンピュータの負荷が上がると大きくなることがよくあります。ノイズ全体が少し大きくなると、ブロックは最大 10 "
"デシベルまでそれに追従します。学習した値より低くなることはありません。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:28
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"The line at the top says where the block stands: Learning, with how far it "
"has got; Active, with how many seconds of noise it learned; or Inactive, when"
" it has learned nothing yet and lets the sound through unchanged."
msgstr ""
"上の行には、ブロックの状態が表示されます: "
"「学習中」（進み具合とともに）、「アクティブ」（学習したノイズの秒数とともに）、またはまだ何も学習しておらず、音をそのまま通す「非アクティブ」です。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:29
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"The noise it learned is saved with the session, so it is still there the next"
" time you open it. A noise learned by an earlier version of Reverblabr is not"
" used: the block says Learn the noise again, and lets the sound through until"
" you do."
msgstr ""
"学習したノイズはセッションと一緒に保存されるので、次にセッションを開いたときも残っています。以前のバージョンの Reverblabr "
"で学習したノイズは使われません: ブロックに「ノイズの再学習が必要」と表示され、学習し直すまで音をそのまま通します。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:30
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"The block holds the sound back by about four hundredths of a second, whatever"
" the settings. Reverblabr keeps the other lanes in step with that delay."
msgstr "このブロックは、設定に関係なく音を約 100 分の 4 秒遅らせます。Reverblabr は、他のレーンをこの遅延に合わせます。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:40 blocks/denoise/ui/DenoisePanel.qml:100
msgctxt "@action:button start listening to the noise"
msgid "Learn Noise"
msgstr "ノイズを学習"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:42 blocks/denoise/ui/DenoisePanel.qml:99
msgctxt "@action:button drop the learned noise"
msgid "Forget Noise"
msgstr "ノイズを破棄"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:45
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"Starts listening to the noise. It needs the session running, since it learns "
"from what is playing; while the session is stopped the button waits."
msgstr "ノイズの聞き取りを始めます。再生中の音から学習するので、セッションの実行が必要です。セッションが停止している間、ボタンは待機状態になります。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:46
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"Once a noise is learned, the button says Forget Noise. Press it to drop the "
"noise, for example to learn a different one. The block then lets the sound "
"through unchanged until it learns again."
msgstr ""
"ノイズを学習すると、ボタンが「ノイズを破棄」に変わります。別のノイズを学習したいときなどに押すと、ノイズを破棄します。その後、ブロックは再び学習するまで音をそのまま通します。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:52 blocks/denoise/ui/DenoisePanel.qml:143
#: blocks/speechdenoise/ui/SpeechDenoiseHelp.qml:39
#: blocks/speechdenoise/ui/SpeechDenoisePanel.qml:103
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Noise reduction"
msgstr "ノイズ低減量"

#. i18n: dB stands for decibels.
#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:55
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"How far the block turns the noise down, in decibels (dB), from 0 to 40 dB. A "
"new block starts at 20 dB."
msgstr "ブロックがノイズをどれだけ下げるかを、デシベル（dB）で、0〜40 dB の範囲で設定します。新しいブロックは 20 dB から始まります。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:56
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"Higher takes out more of the noise. Lower leaves a little of it, which often "
"sounds more natural than none."
msgstr "高くするとノイズをより多く取り除きます。低くするとノイズが少し残りますが、まったくないより自然に聞こえることがよくあります。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:62 blocks/denoise/ui/DenoisePanel.qml:195
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Keep sound above noise by"
msgstr "ノイズに対するマージン"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:64
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"How far above the loudest the learned noise gets a band has to be before the "
"block leaves it alone, from 0 to 20 dB. A new block starts at 3 dB."
msgstr ""
"学習したノイズの最大の大きさより、帯域がどれだけ大きければ、ブロックが手を加えずに残すかを、0〜20 dB の範囲で設定します。新しいブロックは 3 dB"
" から始まります。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:65
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"Raise it if some noise still comes through around a voice. Lower it if quiet "
"parts of the sound you want, such as the end of a word, are being taken away "
"with the noise."
msgstr ""
"声の周りにまだノイズが残る場合は上げてください。言葉の終わりなど、残したい音の小さな部分がノイズと一緒に取り除かれてしまう場合は下げてください。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:72
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"A computer fan or an air conditioner can be heard behind your microphone."
msgstr "マイクの音の後ろに、コンピュータのファンやエアコンの音が聞こえるとき。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:73
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid "An old recording or a cheap sound card has a steady hiss."
msgstr "古い録音や安価なサウンドカードに、一定のサーというノイズがあるとき。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:74
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"A sound card buzzes or ticks with what the computer is doing, and you hear it"
" whenever the sound you play stops."
msgstr "コンピュータの動作に合わせてサウンドカードがブーンやチリチリと鳴り、再生している音が止まるたびにそれが聞こえるとき。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:75
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"The noise is the same kind all the time, even if it ticks or comes and goes. "
"For noise that keeps changing, such as traffic or people talking, try the "
"Speech Denoise block instead."
msgstr ""
"カチカチと鳴ったり出たり消えたりしても、ノイズの種類がいつも同じとき。交通の音や人の話し声のように変化し続けるノイズには、代わりに「音声ノイズ除去」ブロックを試してください。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:82
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"Learn the noise in the same place, with the same microphone and the same "
"volume as the sound you will clean. Keep quiet while it listens."
msgstr "ノイズは、きれいにしたい音と同じ場所で、同じマイク、同じ音量で学習させてください。聞き取りの間は静かにしてください。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:83
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"For the noise a sound card picks up from the computer, learn it with the "
"computer doing what it usually does. If you turn the sound card's gain, learn"
" the noise again."
msgstr ""
"サウンドカードがコンピュータから拾うノイズは、コンピュータが普段どおりの作業をしている状態で学習させてください。サウンドカードのゲインを変えたら、ノイズを学習し直してください。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:84
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"If the room changes, a different fan, a window opened, press Forget Noise and"
" learn it again."
msgstr "ファンが変わった、窓を開けたなど、部屋の状況が変わったら、「ノイズを破棄」を押して学習し直してください。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:85
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"If what is left sounds watery or twinkly, lower Noise reduction a little."
msgstr "残った音が水っぽく聞こえたり、キラキラした音が混じったりする場合は、「ノイズ低減量」を少し下げてください。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseHelp.qml:86
msgctxt "@info help page of the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"Put the block before anything that turns the sound up or down, so it hears "
"the noise at the level it learned it."
msgstr "音量を上げ下げするものより前に、このブロックを置いてください。そうすれば、学習したときと同じレベルでノイズを聞けます。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoisePanel.qml:58
msgctxt "@info a level in decibels, '20.0 dB'"
msgid "%1 dB"
msgstr "%1 dB"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoisePanel.qml:106
msgctxt "@info:tooltip"
msgid "Run the session, with only the noise playing, to learn it"
msgstr "ノイズだけを再生した状態でセッションを実行すると、ノイズを学習できます"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoisePanel.qml:120
msgctxt "@label:slider how far a Denoise block turns the noise down"
msgid "Noise reduction"
msgstr "ノイズ低減量"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoisePanel.qml:167
msgctxt ""
"@label:slider how far above the learned noise a sound has to be to pass "
"untouched"
msgid "Keep sound above noise by"
msgstr "ノイズに対するマージン"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoisePanel.qml:213
msgctxt "@info how to use the Denoise block"
msgid ""
"Play the noise on its own and press Learn Noise: ten seconds of it are "
"listened to. Then everything that follows has that noise taken out."
msgstr "ノイズだけを再生して「ノイズを学習」を押すと、10 秒間聞き取ります。その後のすべての音から、そのノイズが取り除かれます。"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseState.qml:62
msgctxt "@info a Denoise block listening to the noise"
msgid "Learning"
msgstr "学習中"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseState.qml:63
msgctxt "@info a Denoise block taking a learned noise out"
msgid "Active"
msgstr "アクティブ"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseState.qml:64
msgctxt "@info a Denoise block with no noise learned"
msgid "Inactive"
msgstr "非アクティブ"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseState.qml:67
msgctxt "@info how far a Denoise block is through learning, '40 %'"
msgid "Listening… %1 %"
msgstr "聞き取り中… %1%"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseState.qml:70
msgctxt "@info how much noise a Denoise block learned, '10.0 s noise learned'"
msgid "%1 s noise learned"
msgstr "%1 秒のノイズを学習済み"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseState.qml:74
msgctxt ""
"@info a Denoise block whose saved noise an earlier version learned, and which"
" it does not use"
msgid "Learn the noise again"
msgstr "ノイズの再学習が必要"

#: blocks/denoise/ui/DenoiseState.qml:75
msgctxt "@info a Denoise block with no noise learned"
msgid "No noise learned"
msgstr "ノイズ未学習"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingFace.qml:47
msgctxt ""
"@info the background is turned down by this much now, 'ducking -8.0 dB'"
msgid "ducking %1"
msgstr "ダッキング %1"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingFace.qml:50
msgctxt ""
"@info the background is turned down to this while the main source is heard, "
"'duck to 40 %'"
msgid "duck to %1"
msgstr "%1 まで下げる"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingFace.qml:54
msgctxt ""
"@info:tooltip what a Ducking block does, 'Above -30.0 dB on the main input, "
"the background goes to 40 %'"
msgid "Above %1 on the main input, the background goes to %2"
msgstr "メイン入力が %1 を超えると、背景音は %2 になります"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingFace.qml:122 blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:138
msgctxt "@label:slider how far the Ducking block turns the background down"
msgid "Ducked volume"
msgstr "ダッキング時の音量"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:17
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"Turns background sound, such as music, down while a main sound, usually a "
"voice, is heard, and brings it back up when the voice stops."
msgstr "メインの音（ふつうは声）が聞こえている間、音楽などの背景音を下げ、声が止まると元に戻します。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:22
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"The block has two inputs on its tile: main and background. Wire the voice "
"into main and the music into background. What comes out is the two mixed "
"together."
msgstr ""
"このブロックのタイルには、「メイン」と「背景音」の 2 つの入力があります。声を「メイン」に、音楽を「背景音」に配線してください。出力は、その 2 "
"つを混ぜ合わせたものです。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"The block listens to the main input. While it is louder than the threshold, "
"the background is turned down to the ducked volume; when it falls quiet, the "
"background comes back up. The main input itself always passes through "
"unchanged."
msgstr ""
"このブロックはメイン入力を聞いています。メイン入力がスレッショルドより大きい間は、背景音をダッキング時の音量まで下げ、静かになると背景音を元に戻します。メイン入力そのものは、常にそのまま通ります。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"Whichever side of the main input is louder decides, so a voice on the left or"
" the right ducks the music as surely as one in the middle."
msgstr "メイン入力の左右のうち大きい方で判断するので、左や右に寄った声でも、中央の声と同じように確実に音楽を下げます。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"The line at the top says Ducking while the main input is heard and for the "
"hold after it, and Not ducking otherwise."
msgstr "上部の行には、メイン入力が聞こえている間とその後のホールドの間は「ダッキング中」、それ以外は「ダッキングなし」と表示されます。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid "The block adds no delay."
msgstr "このブロックは遅延を加えません。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:36 blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:112
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Main threshold"
msgstr "メイン入力のスレッショルド"

#. i18n: dB stands for decibels.
#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:39
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"How loud the main input has to be to duck the background, in decibels (dB) "
"below full scale, from −60 dB to 0 dB. Full scale is the loudest a digital "
"signal can be. A new block starts at −30 dB."
msgstr ""
"背景音を下げるには、メイン入力がどれだけ大きくなければならないかで、フルスケールより下のデシベル（dB）で −60 dB〜0 dB "
"です。フルスケールとは、デジタル信号が出せる最大の大きさです。新しいブロックは −30 dB から始まります。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:40
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"Lower makes the block react to quieter sound on the main input; higher makes "
"it wait for louder sound."
msgstr "低くするとメイン入力の小さな音にも反応し、高くするともっと大きな音が来るまで待ちます。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:46 blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:167
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Ducked volume"
msgstr "ダッキング時の音量"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:48
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"How loud the background plays while it is ducked, as a percentage of its full"
" volume, from 0 % to 100 %. The number beside it says the same in decibels. A"
" new block starts at 40 %, about −8 dB."
msgstr ""
"ダッキング中に背景音をどれだけの大きさで鳴らすかで、元の音量に対する割合で 0%〜100% です。横の数値は、同じ値をデシベルで示します。新しいブロックは"
" 40%（約 −8 dB）から始まります。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:49
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"At 0 % the background goes silent while the main input is heard. At 100 % it "
"is not turned down at all."
msgstr "0% では、メイン入力が聞こえている間、背景音は無音になります。100% では、まったく下げません。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:55 blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:191
msgctxt "@title:group how quickly the Ducking block works"
msgid "Timing"
msgstr "タイミング"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:57
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"How quickly the background goes down and comes back. Click the heading to "
"open these settings. A new block starts with times that suit speech over "
"music, so you may never need them."
msgstr ""
"背景音がどれだけ速く下がり、戻るかです。見出しをクリックすると、これらの設定が開きます。新しいブロックは、音楽に声を重ねるのに合った時間で始まるので、変更する必要はないかもしれません。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:63 blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:197
msgctxt "@label:slider how long the background takes to go down"
msgid "Attack"
msgstr "アタック"

#. i18n: ms stands for milliseconds, thousandths of a second.
#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:66
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"How long the background takes to go all the way down once the main input "
"starts, in thousandths of a second (ms), from 5 to 1000 ms. A new block takes"
" 50 ms. Short is quick but can sound abrupt; long is gentle, but the first "
"word may be heard over the music."
msgstr ""
"メイン入力が始まってから、背景音が下がりきるまでの時間で、ミリ秒（ms、1000 分の 1 秒）で 5〜1000 ms です。新しいブロックは 50 ms"
" です。短いとすばやいものの唐突に聞こえることがあり、長いと穏やかですが、最初の言葉が音楽にかぶって聞こえることがあります。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:72 blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:209
msgctxt ""
"@label:slider how long the background stays down after the main input stops"
msgid "Hold"
msgstr "ホールド"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:74
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"How long the background stays down after the main input falls quiet, from 0 "
"to 2000 ms. A new block holds it for 300 ms."
msgstr "メイン入力が静かになってから、背景音が下がったままでいる時間で、0〜2000 ms です。新しいブロックは 300 ms です。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:75
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"The hold bridges the short pauses between words, so the music does not jump "
"up and down in every gap."
msgstr "ホールドは言葉の間の短い合間をつなぐので、すき間ごとに音楽が上下することはありません。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:81 blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:219
msgctxt "@label:slider how long the background takes to come back up"
msgid "Release"
msgstr "リリース"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:83
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"How long the background takes to come all the way back up after the hold, "
"from 10 to 5000 ms. A new block takes 500 ms. Longer brings the music back "
"more gently."
msgstr ""
"ホールドの後、背景音が元の大きさに戻りきるまでの時間で、10〜5000 ms です。新しいブロックは 500 ms "
"です。長くするほど、音楽がより穏やかに戻ります。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:90
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"You talk over music in a stream or a podcast, and want the music to make room"
" for you."
msgstr "配信やポッドキャストで音楽に乗せて話すので、話す間は音楽を控えめにしたいとき。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:91
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"You want a game or a video to get quieter whenever somebody speaks in a call."
msgstr "通話で誰かが話すたびに、ゲームや動画の音を小さくしたいとき。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:92
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid "An announcement should always be heard over the background."
msgstr "アナウンスを常に背景音より聞こえやすくしたいとき。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:99
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"To set the threshold, speak normally and watch the line at the top. Raise the"
" threshold until breathing and background noise on the microphone no longer "
"say Ducking, while your voice still does."
msgstr ""
"スレッショルドを設定するには、普段どおりに話しながら上部の行を見てください。声では「ダッキング中」と表示され、マイクに入る息や背景ノイズでは表示されなくなるまで、スレッショルドを上げます。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:100
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid "If the music pumps up and down while you talk, make Hold longer."
msgstr "話している間に音楽が上下に波打つ場合は、「ホールド」を長くしてください。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:101
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"For background music under a voice, a ducked volume between 20 % and 40 % "
"usually keeps the music present without covering the words."
msgstr "声の後ろで流す音楽なら、ダッキング時の音量を 20%〜40% にすると、たいてい言葉を覆わずに音楽の存在感を保てます。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingHelp.qml:102
msgctxt "@info help page of the Ducking block"
msgid ""
"Put a Volume block before the main input if the voice is too quiet to reach "
"the threshold."
msgstr "声が小さすぎてスレッショルドに届かない場合は、メイン入力の前に「音量」ブロックを置いてください。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:78
msgctxt "@info the Ducking block is turning the background down now"
msgid "Ducking"
msgstr "ダッキング中"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:79
msgctxt "@info the Ducking block is leaving the background alone now"
msgid "Not ducking"
msgstr "ダッキングなし"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:90
msgctxt "@label:slider the level the main input has to reach to duck"
msgid "Main threshold"
msgstr "メイン入力のスレッショルド"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:129
msgctxt "@info what the Ducking block's threshold does"
msgid "The background is turned down while the main input is louder than this."
msgstr "メイン入力がこれより大きい間、背景音が下げられます。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:151
msgctxt "@info a volume and the same in decibels, '40 % · -8.0 dB'"
msgid "%1 · %2"
msgstr "%1 · %2"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:184
msgctxt "@info what the Ducking block's ducked volume does"
msgid "While the main input is heard, the background plays at this volume."
msgstr "メイン入力が聞こえている間、背景音はこの音量で鳴ります。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingPanel.qml:228
msgctxt "@info what the Ducking block's timing does"
msgid ""
"The attack is how long the background takes to go down, the hold how long it "
"stays down after the main input stops, and the release how long it takes to "
"come back."
msgstr "アタックは背景音が下がるまでの時間、ホールドはメイン入力が止まった後に下がったままでいる時間、リリースは元に戻るまでの時間です。"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingWords.qml:26
msgctxt "@info a volume as a percentage of the sound as it arrived"
msgid "%1 %"
msgstr "%1%"

#: blocks/ducking/ui/DuckingWords.qml:34
msgctxt "@info the background is turned all the way down"
msgid "silent"
msgstr "無音"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsFace.qml:151
msgctxt "@info how much the block is holding the sound back, in decibels"
msgid "%1 dB"
msgstr "%1 dB"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsFace.qml:153
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:473
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:1005
msgctxt "@info nothing is running, so there is nothing to report"
msgid "—"
msgstr "—"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsFace.qml:154
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:957
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:971
msgctxt "@label how much the block is holding the sound back"
msgid "Gain reduction"
msgstr "ゲインリダクション"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:19
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"Holds loud sound back and pushes quiet sound down, following a curve you "
"shape by dragging four points. Use it to even out a voice, keep peaks in "
"check, or cut the noise between words."
msgstr ""
"4 "
"つの点をドラッグして形を決めるカーブに従って、大きな音を抑え、小さな音をさらに下げます。声のばらつきをならしたり、ピークを抑えたり、言葉の間のノイズを消したりするのに使います。"

#. i18n: dB stands for decibels.
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"The graph at the top of the settings is the block. Along the bottom is how "
"loud the sound comes in, up the side how loud it goes out, both in decibels "
"(dB). The dashed diagonal line is the main line: on it, sound comes out as it"
" went in. The curve is never above that line, so this block only ever turns "
"sound down."
msgstr ""
"設定の一番上にあるグラフが、このブロックそのものです。横軸は入ってくる音の大きさ、縦軸は出ていく音の大きさで、どちらもデシベル（dB）で表します。破線の対角線が基準線で、この線上では、音は入ったときのまま出ていきます。カーブがこの線より上に来ることはないので、このブロックは音を下げることしかしません。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"At the loud end the curve bends away from the diagonal, so loud moments come "
"out less loud. At the quiet end it can drop away from the diagonal, so noise "
"in the pauses gets quieter or disappears. Between the two the sound is left "
"alone."
msgstr ""
"大きい側ではカーブが対角線から離れて曲がるので、大きな瞬間はそれほど大きくならずに出ていきます。小さい側ではカーブが対角線から下へ離れることがあり、合間のノイズが小さくなったり消えたりします。その間では、音はそのままです。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:27
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"While the session runs, a dot on the curve shows where the sound is right "
"now. The bar beside the curve and the Gain reduction number under it show how"
" much the block is turning the sound down, and In / out shows the level going"
" in and the level coming out."
msgstr ""
"セッションの実行中は、カーブ上の点がいまの音の位置を示します。カーブの横のバーとその下の「ゲインリダクション」の数値は、ブロックが音をどれだけ下げているかを示し、「入力"
" / 出力」は入ってくるレベルと出ていくレベルを示します。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:28
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"Both sides of a stereo lane are turned down together, by the louder of the "
"two, so the sound never shifts to one side."
msgstr "ステレオのレーンでは、左右のうち大きい方に合わせて両方を一緒に下げるので、音が片側に寄ることはありません。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:29
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"A new block holds anything above −26 dB back firmly, and leaves the quiet end"
" alone. The presets at the bottom of the settings give other starting points:"
" Gentle leveling, Voice, Noise gate and Hard limiting, and Default to go "
"back."
msgstr ""
"新しいブロックは −26 dB を超える音をしっかり抑え、小さい側はそのままにします。設定の一番下にあるプリセットで、別の出発点を選べます: "
"「穏やかな均一化」「声」「ノイズゲート」「強いリミッティング」、そして元に戻すための「デフォルト」です。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:38
msgctxt "@title a part of the Dynamics Processor's help page"
msgid "The curve"
msgstr "カーブ"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:40
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"Four points shape the curve, and each moves along one line only. Press near "
"one and drag. While you drag, the point lights up and a box beside it shows "
"the settings it is changing. Point at one to read what it is set to."
msgstr ""
"4 つの点がカーブの形を決め、それぞれ決まった 1 "
"本の線の上だけを動きます。点の近くを押してドラッグしてください。ドラッグ中は点が明るくなり、横のボックスに変更中の設定が表示されます。点にマウスを重ねると、現在の設定値を確認できます。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:43
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block, one point of the curve"
msgid ""
"Cut-off, the point on the bottom edge: moves left and right along the bottom."
" Anything quieter than this point comes out as nothing. Between here and the "
"expander threshold the curve climbs in a straight line, so moving this point "
"to the right makes that line steeper. It sets the Expander ratio, and it "
"cannot reach the next point."
msgstr ""
"カットオフ（下端の点）: "
"下端に沿って左右に動きます。この点より小さい音は、まったく出力されません。ここからエキスパンダースレッショルドまでは、カーブが直線で上がっていくので、この点を右へ動かすほど直線が急になります。この点は「エキスパンダーレシオ」を決め、次の点までは届きません。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:44
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block, one point of the curve"
msgid ""
"Expander threshold, the lower point on the diagonal: moves along the "
"diagonal. It sets where the quiet end starts to drop away, and the Cut-off "
"moves with it, so the line stays as steep as it was. It stops at the "
"Compressor threshold."
msgstr ""
"エキスパンダースレッショルド（対角線上の下の点）: "
"対角線に沿って動きます。小さい側が下がり始める位置を決めます。「カットオフ」も一緒に動くので、直線の傾きは変わりません。「コンプレッサースレッショルド」で止まります。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:45
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block, one point of the curve"
msgid ""
"Compressor threshold, the upper point on the diagonal: moves along the "
"diagonal, as far as +20 dB. It sets where the curve starts to bend, and the "
"Height point moves with it. It stops at the Expander threshold."
msgstr ""
"コンプレッサースレッショルド（対角線上の上の点）: 対角線に沿って +20 dB "
"まで動きます。カーブが曲がり始める位置を決め、「高さ」の点も一緒に動きます。「エキスパンダースレッショルド」で止まります。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:46
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block, one point of the curve"
msgid ""
"Height, the point on the right edge: moves up and down the edge. The curve "
"always bends smoothly from the Compressor threshold to this point, and the "
"point cannot go lower than that threshold. Right down, the curve is flat and "
"nothing louder gets through."
msgstr ""
"高さ（右端の点）: "
"右端に沿って上下に動きます。カーブは常に「コンプレッサースレッショルド」からこの点まで滑らかに曲がり、この点がそのスレッショルドより下がることはありません。一番下まで下げるとカーブは水平になり、それより大きい音は通りません。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:49
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"Each point can also be reached with the Tab key. Any arrow key then moves it "
"along its line, 2 dB a press, or half a decibel with Shift held: right and up"
" towards the loud end, left and down away from it."
msgstr ""
"各点には Tab キーでも移動できます。その後は矢印キーで線に沿って動かせます。1 回押すごとに 2 dB、Shift を押しながらなら 0.5 dB "
"動きます。右と上で大きい側へ、左と下でその反対へ動きます。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:50
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"The Make-up gain is not part of the curve: it changes the sound without "
"moving the line. Every setting the points change is also under Details, as a "
"number."
msgstr "「メイクアップゲイン」はカーブの一部ではなく、線を動かさずに音を変えます。点で変わる設定は、すべて「詳細」の下に数値でも表示されます。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:55
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:1031
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:1049
msgctxt "@action:button every setting written out as a number"
msgid "Details"
msgstr "詳細"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:57
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"Click Details to show every setting of the block as a slider with its number,"
" including the ones the curve does not show. It is closed when the settings "
"open."
msgstr ""
"「詳細」をクリックすると、カーブには表れない設定も含めて、ブロックのすべての設定が数値付きのスライダーで表示されます。設定を開いたときは閉じています。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:63
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:443
msgctxt "@label where the curve starts bending away from the diagonal"
msgid "Threshold"
msgstr "スレッショルド"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:65
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"The level above which the block holds the sound back, from −120 to +20 dB. 0 "
"dB is full scale, the loudest a digital signal can be. A new block starts at "
"−26 dB."
msgstr ""
"これを超えるとブロックが音を抑えるレベルで、−120〜+20 dB です。0 dB "
"はフルスケール、つまりデジタル信号が出せる最大の大きさです。新しいブロックは −26 dB から始まります。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:66
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"The lower the threshold, the more of the sound is held back. It cannot go "
"below the Expander threshold."
msgstr "スレッショルドが低いほど、多くの音が抑えられます。「エキスパンダースレッショルド」より下にはできません。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:72
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:445
msgctxt "@label how high the curve can rise above the threshold"
msgid "Height"
msgstr "高さ"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:74
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"How high the curve can rise above the threshold, however loud the sound gets,"
" from 0 to 40 dB. At 0 dB the block is a hard limiter: nothing comes out "
"louder than the threshold. At a large height the curve bends slowly and stays"
" near the diagonal for longer. A new block starts at 7 dB, which is firm."
msgstr ""
"音がどれほど大きくなっても、カーブがスレッショルドからどこまで上がれるかで、0〜40 dB です。0 dB "
"ではブロックはハードリミッターになり、スレッショルドより大きな音は出ません。高さを大きくすると、カーブはゆっくり曲がり、長く対角線の近くにとどまります。新しいブロックは"
" 7 dB から始まり、これはしっかりした効き方です。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:75
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"The curve only ever approaches this height, so it reaches it near the right "
"edge only when the threshold is far below there, and it stays under the "
"diagonal whatever the height."
msgstr ""
"カーブはこの高さに近づいていくだけなので、右端付近でこの高さに届くのは、スレッショルドがそこよりずっと低い場合だけです。また、高さがいくつでも、カーブは対角線より下にとどまります。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:81
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:447
msgctxt "@label where the expander starts working"
msgid "Expander threshold"
msgstr "エキスパンダースレッショルド"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:83
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"The level below which the quiet end of the curve drops away from the "
"diagonal, from −120 dB up to the Threshold. A new block starts at −80 dB, "
"with an Expander ratio that leaves it alone."
msgstr ""
"これより小さいと、カーブの小さい側が対角線から下へ離れるレベルで、−120 dB から「スレッショルド」まで設定できます。新しいブロックは −80 dB "
"から始まり、「エキスパンダーレシオ」は音に何もしない値になっています。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:89
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:449
msgctxt "@label how steeply the quiet end is pushed down"
msgid "Expander ratio"
msgstr "エキスパンダーレシオ"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:91
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"How steeply the sound below the Expander threshold falls away, from 1:1 to "
"50:1. At 2:1, sound 1 dB below that threshold comes out 2 dB below it. At 1:1"
" nothing falls away, and a new block starts there. A high ratio is a noise "
"gate: the sound stops almost at once below the threshold."
msgstr ""
"「エキスパンダースレッショルド」より小さい音がどれだけ急に下がるかで、1:1〜50:1 です。2:1 では、スレッショルドより 1 dB 小さい音が 2 "
"dB 小さくなって出ていきます。1:1 "
"では何も下がらず、新しいブロックはこの値から始まります。レシオを高くするとノイズゲートになり、スレッショルドを下回るとほぼすぐに音が止まります。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:92
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"Where the line reaches the bottom of the graph, the sound comes out as "
"nothing. Dragging the Cut-off point changes this number."
msgstr "線がグラフの下端に達するところでは、音はまったく出力されません。「カットオフ」の点をドラッグすると、この数値が変わります。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:98
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:451
msgctxt "@label how long the expander stays open"
msgid "Expander hold"
msgstr "エキスパンダーホールド"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:100
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"How long the block waits, after the sound drops below the Expander threshold,"
" before it starts pushing it down: from 0 to 500 milliseconds (ms). It keeps "
"the ends of words from being cut off, and stops sound that hovers around the "
"threshold from fluttering. A new block starts at 0 ms."
msgstr ""
"音が「エキスパンダースレッショルド」を下回ってから、ブロックが音を下げ始めるまでの待ち時間で、0〜500 "
"ミリ秒（ms）です。言葉の終わりが切れるのを防ぎ、スレッショルド付近を行き来する音がばたつくのを抑えます。新しいブロックは 0 ms から始まります。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:106
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:453
msgctxt "@label how fast the block reacts to a sound getting louder"
msgid "Attack"
msgstr "アタック"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:108
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"How quickly the block turns the sound down when it needs to, from 0.1 to 200 "
"ms. A short attack catches sudden peaks; a longer one lets the start of each "
"sound through, which keeps drums and speech crisp. A new block starts at 1 "
"ms."
msgstr ""
"必要なときにブロックがどれだけ速く音を下げるかで、0.1〜200 ms "
"です。アタックが短いと急なピークを捉えられます。長いと各音の出だしが通るので、ドラムや話し声の歯切れが保たれます。新しいブロックは 1 ms "
"から始まります。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:114
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:455
msgctxt "@label how fast the block lets go again"
msgid "Release"
msgstr "リリース"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:116
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"How quickly the block lets the sound come back up afterwards, from 10 to 3000"
" ms. A short release can make the level pump audibly; a long one sounds "
"smoother but keeps quiet parts after a loud one too low for a while. A new "
"block starts at 50 ms."
msgstr ""
"その後、ブロックがどれだけ速く音を元に戻すかで、10〜3000 ms "
"です。リリースが短いと、レベルが波打つように聞こえることがあります。長いと滑らかに聞こえますが、大きな部分の後の小さな部分が、しばらく小さすぎるままになります。新しいブロックは"
" 50 ms から始まります。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:122
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:457
msgctxt "@label gain added after the curve"
msgid "Make-up gain"
msgstr "メイクアップゲイン"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:124
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"Turns the whole sound up or down after the curve, from −40 to +40 dB. Holding"
" loud sound back makes the sound quieter overall, and this brings it back up."
" It does not move the line on the graph. A new block starts at 0 dB."
msgstr ""
"カーブの後で音全体を上げ下げするもので、−40〜+40 dB "
"です。大きな音を抑えると全体が小さくなるので、これで大きさを取り戻します。グラフの線は動きません。新しいブロックは 0 dB から始まります。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:130
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:459
msgctxt "@label what the block follows: the loudest sample or a short average"
msgid "Detector"
msgstr "検出方式"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:132
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"How the block measures the level it compares with the thresholds. A new block"
" uses Peaks."
msgstr "スレッショルドと比べるレベルを、ブロックがどのように測るかです。新しいブロックは「ピーク」を使います。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:135
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block, one choice of Detector"
msgid ""
"Peaks: the highest point of the sound wave over the last few thousandths of a"
" second. It reacts to every peak, so nothing slips past."
msgstr "ピーク: 直近の 1000 分の数秒間における音の波の最も高い点です。すべてのピークに反応するので、何も見逃しません。"

#. i18n: RMS is short for root mean square; the sentence explains it.
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:137
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block, one choice of Detector"
msgid ""
"Average (RMS): an average over the last hundredth of a second, which follows "
"how loud the sound feels more closely. RMS is short for root mean square, a "
"way of averaging."
msgstr ""
"平均（RMS）: 直近 100 分の 1 秒間の平均で、音の感じられる大きさにより近く追従します。RMS "
"は「二乗平均平方根」を表す英語の略で、平均の取り方の一つです。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:144
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"A voice is sometimes too loud and sometimes too quiet, and you want it "
"steadier."
msgstr "声が大きすぎたり小さすぎたりするので、もっと安定させたいとき。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:145
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"Sudden loud sounds, such as laughter or a door, keep making listeners reach "
"for the volume."
msgstr "笑い声やドアの音のような突然の大きな音のせいで、聞く人が何度も音量を調整しなければならないとき。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:146
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"A microphone picks up a fan or traffic between sentences, and you want the "
"pauses quieter."
msgstr "文と文の間にマイクがファンや車の音を拾うので、合間を静かにしたいとき。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:147
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"You want a firm ceiling that the sound never goes past, before a recording or"
" a stream."
msgstr "録音や配信の前に、音が決して超えないしっかりした上限を設けたいとき。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:154
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"Start from a preset close to what you want, Voice for speech or Noise gate "
"for a noisy microphone, and adjust from there."
msgstr "話し声なら「声」、ノイズの多いマイクなら「ノイズゲート」のように、目的に近いプリセットから始めて、そこから調整してください。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:155
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"Watch Gain reduction while the sound plays. A few decibels is gentle; much "
"more than 10 dB, most of the time, is heavy and can be heard."
msgstr ""
"音を流しながら「ゲインリダクション」を見てください。数デシベルなら穏やかです。ほとんどの時間で 10 dB を大きく超えるなら強すぎで、耳でもわかります。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:156
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"After setting the loud end, raise the Make-up gain until the sound is as loud"
" as it was before, so you hear the change in evenness rather than in level."
msgstr ""
"大きい側を設定したら、音が以前と同じ大きさになるまで「メイクアップゲイン」を上げてください。そうすると、音量の変化ではなく、音のそろい方の変化を聞き取れます。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:157
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid ""
"For the pauses, play them only, drag the Cut-off point to the right until the"
" noise goes, and move the Expander threshold just above the noise. If word "
"endings get cut off, lower the threshold a little or lengthen the hold."
msgstr ""
"合間を調整するには、合間の部分だけを再生しながら、ノイズが消えるまで「カットオフ」の点を右へドラッグし、「エキスパンダースレッショルド」をノイズのすぐ上に動かします。言葉の終わりが切れる場合は、スレッショルドを少し下げるか、ホールドを長くしてください。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsHelp.qml:158
msgctxt "@info help page of the Dynamics Processor block"
msgid "Ctrl+Z takes back a whole drag of a point in one step."
msgstr "Ctrl+Z を押すと、点のドラッグ 1 回分をまとめて元に戻せます。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:387
msgctxt ""
"@label:slider a point on the transfer curve: anything quieter comes out as "
"nothing"
msgid "Cut-off"
msgstr "カットオフ"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:389
msgctxt "@label:slider a point on the transfer curve"
msgid "Expander threshold"
msgstr "エキスパンダースレッショルド"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:391
msgctxt "@label:slider a point on the transfer curve"
msgid "Compressor threshold"
msgstr "コンプレッサースレッショルド"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:394
msgctxt ""
"@label:slider a point on the transfer curve: how high the curve can rise"
msgid "Height"
msgstr "高さ"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:412
msgctxt "@info a level in decibels"
msgid "%1 decibels"
msgstr "%1 デシベル"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:420
msgctxt "@label:slider a curve point, its value, and how to move it"
msgid "%1, %2. Arrow keys adjust."
msgstr "%1、%2。矢印キーで調整できます。"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:431
msgctxt "@info how steeply the quiet end falls away"
msgid "%1 to 1"
msgstr "%1 対 1"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:885
msgctxt "@info:whatsthis"
msgid "Gain reduction"
msgstr "ゲインリダクション"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:992
#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:1010
msgctxt "@label the level going in and the level coming out"
msgid "In / out"
msgstr "入力 / 出力"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:1003
msgctxt "@info the level going in and the level coming out"
msgid "%1 / %2"
msgstr "%1 / %2"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:1033
msgctxt "@info the details section is open"
msgid "Open"
msgstr "開いている"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:1034
msgctxt "@info the details section is closed"
msgid "Closed"
msgstr "閉じている"

#: blocks/dynamics/ui/DynamicsPanel.qml:1056
msgctxt "@info how many settings are under Details"
msgid "%1 setting"
msgid_plural "%1 settings"
msgstr[0] "%1 個の設定"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoFace.qml:40
msgctxt ""
"@info:tooltip an Echo's settings, 'Every 350 ms, 40 % feedback, tone 5.00 "
"kHz, 35 % mix'"
msgid "Every %1, %2 feedback, tone %3, %4 mix"
msgstr "間隔 %1、フィードバック %2、トーン %3、ミックス %4"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoFace.qml:93
msgctxt "@label what the number on an Echo tile is"
msgid "echo"
msgstr "エコー"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoFace.qml:110 blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:35
#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoPanel.qml:131
msgctxt "@label:slider the time between an Echo's repeats"
msgid "Time"
msgstr "時間"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:17
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"Repeats the sound a moment later, again and again, each repeat quieter and "
"duller than the one before, mixed in behind the original."
msgstr "少し遅れて音を何度も繰り返し、元の音の後ろに重ねます。繰り返すたびに、前より小さく、こもった音になります。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:22
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"The block keeps a copy of the sound and plays it back after the time you set."
" Part of each repeat is fed back in to be repeated again, so you hear a trail"
" of echoes that fades away."
msgstr ""
"このブロックは音のコピーを保持し、設定した時間の後に再生します。各繰り返しの一部はまた戻されて繰り返されるので、だんだん消えていくエコーの連なりが聞こえます。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"The first repeat sounds like the original. Each one after it loses some of "
"its highest sounds, as an echo off a far wall does, and some of its level, so"
" the trail always dies away in the end."
msgstr ""
"最初の繰り返しは元の音と同じように聞こえます。その後は、遠くの壁から返ってくるエコーのように、繰り返すたびに最も高い音の一部とレベルの一部が失われるので、エコーの連なりは必ず最後には消えていきます。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"The original sound goes straight through with no delay, so the block does not"
" hold the lane back."
msgstr "元の音は遅延なしでそのまま通るので、このブロックがレーンを遅らせることはありません。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"Every setting can be changed while sound plays without a click. A new time "
"fades across from the old echoes to the new ones over a twentieth of a "
"second, rather than bending the pitch."
msgstr ""
"どの設定も、音の再生中にクリックノイズなしで変更できます。時間を変えると、ピッチを曲げるのではなく、20 分の 1 "
"秒かけて古いエコーから新しいエコーへフェードで切り替わります。"

#. i18n: ms stands for milliseconds, s for seconds.
#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:38
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"How long after the sound each repeat comes, from 1 millisecond (ms) to 2 "
"seconds (s). A new block starts at 350 ms, about a third of a second."
msgstr "音から各繰り返しまでの時間で、1 ミリ秒（ms）から 2 秒（s）までです。新しいブロックでは 350 ms（約 3 分の 1 秒）です。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:39
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"Drag the slider here or on the block's tile. It gives short times as much "
"room as long ones, so a short echo is easy to aim at."
msgstr ""
"ここか、ブロックのタイルにあるスライダーをドラッグしてください。短い時間にも長い時間と同じだけの幅を割り当てているので、短いエコーも狙いやすくなっています。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:40
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"Below about 50 ms the repeats are too close to be heard apart, and they "
"colour the sound rather than echo it. From about 100 ms they become separate "
"echoes."
msgstr ""
"約 50 ms より短いと、繰り返しが近すぎて別々には聞こえず、エコーというより音に色付けをします。約 100 ms "
"からは、別々のエコーとして聞こえます。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:46 blocks/echo/ui/EchoPanel.qml:143
msgctxt "@label:slider how much of each repeat an Echo feeds back in"
msgid "Feedback"
msgstr "フィードバック"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:48
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"How much of each repeat is fed back in to be repeated again, from 0 to 95 %. "
"It decides how many repeats you hear."
msgstr "各繰り返しのうち、どれだけを戻してもう一度繰り返すかで、0 から 95% までです。聞こえる繰り返しの回数が決まります。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:49
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"At 0 % there is a single repeat. Higher numbers give a longer trail; even at "
"95 % it fades away in the end. A new block starts at 40 %."
msgstr ""
"0% では繰り返しは 1 回だけです。値を大きくするほど連なりが長くなりますが、95% でも最後には消えていきます。新しいブロックでは 40% です。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:55 blocks/echo/ui/EchoPanel.qml:153
msgctxt "@label:slider how bright an Echo's repeats stay"
msgid "Tone"
msgstr "トーン"

#. i18n: Hz stands for hertz, kHz for kilohertz.
#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:58
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"How bright the repeats stay, from 500 hertz (Hz) to 20 kilohertz (kHz). Each "
"repeat loses the sound above this frequency a little more than the one before"
" it."
msgstr ""
"繰り返しがどれだけ明るさを保つかで、500 ヘルツ（Hz）から 20 "
"キロヘルツ（kHz）までです。繰り返すたびに、この周波数より上の音が前よりも少しずつ多く失われます。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:59
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"A low setting gives dark, soft echoes that stay in the background. A high one"
" keeps them as bright as the original. A new block starts at 5 kHz."
msgstr ""
"低くすると、背景に溶け込む暗く柔らかなエコーになります。高くすると、元の音と同じくらい明るいまま保たれます。新しいブロックでは 5 kHz です。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:65 blocks/echo/ui/EchoPanel.qml:165
msgctxt "@label:slider how loud an Echo's repeats are against the original"
msgid "Mix"
msgstr "ミックス"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:67
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"How loud the echoes are against the original, from 0 to 100 %. At 0 % you "
"hear the original alone, at 50 % the two equally, and at 100 % the echoes "
"alone. A new block starts at 35 %."
msgstr ""
"元の音に対するエコーの大きさで、0 から 100% までです。0% では元の音だけ、50% では両方が同じくらい、100% "
"ではエコーだけが聞こえます。新しいブロックでは 35% です。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:68
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"As the echoes get louder, the original gets quieter by the same share, so the"
" overall level stays about the same."
msgstr "エコーが大きくなるのと同じ割合で元の音が小さくなるので、全体のレベルはほぼ変わりません。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:75
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"You want a voice or an instrument to sound as if it were in a large space, "
"such as a canyon or a stadium."
msgstr "声や楽器を、峡谷やスタジアムのような広い場所にいるように響かせたいとき。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:76
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"A sound effect, a jingle or a single word should stand out with a trail of "
"repeats."
msgstr "効果音やジングル、ひとことの言葉を、繰り返しの連なりで目立たせたいとき。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:77
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"Music sounds flat and dry, and a quiet echo behind it would give it depth."
msgstr "音楽が平板で乾いた感じに聞こえ、後ろに小さなエコーを入れて奥行きを出したいとき。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:84
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"Keep the Mix low, between 15 and 35 %, so the echoes sit behind the sound "
"rather than over it."
msgstr "エコーが音に覆いかぶさらず後ろに収まるよう、「ミックス」は 15〜35% と低めにしてください。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:85
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"Echo on speech makes it harder to follow. For a call or a podcast, use a "
"short time with little feedback, or leave it out."
msgstr "話し声にエコーをかけると聞き取りにくくなります。通話やポッドキャストでは、短い時間と少ないフィードバックにするか、使わないでください。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:86
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid ""
"To make echoes fit the beat of a song, work out the time between two beats: "
"60000 divided by the beats per minute gives it in milliseconds."
msgstr "エコーを曲のビートに合わせるには、ビートの間隔を計算します。60000 を 1 分あたりの拍数で割ると、ミリ秒単位の値になります。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoHelp.qml:87
msgctxt "@info help page of the Echo block"
msgid "If the trail gets muddy, lower the Tone or the Feedback."
msgstr "エコーの連なりが濁ってきたら、「トーン」か「フィードバック」を下げてください。"

#: blocks/echo/ui/EchoPanel.qml:173
msgctxt "@info what the Echo's settings do"
msgid ""
"Feedback sets how many repeats you hear, Tone how quickly they lose their "
"top, and Mix how loud they are against the original."
msgstr "「フィードバック」は聞こえる繰り返しの回数を、「トーン」は高音が失われる速さを、「ミックス」は元の音に対するエコーの大きさを決めます。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerFace.qml:47
msgctxt "@info:tooltip one band of an equaliser, '1 kHz +3.0 dB'"
msgid "%1 %2"
msgstr "%1 %2"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerFace.qml:51
msgctxt "@info:tooltip an equaliser with every band at 0 dB"
msgid "Flat"
msgstr "フラット"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerFace.qml:52
#: blocks/parametriceq/ui/ParametricEqFace.qml:48
msgctxt "@info:tooltip between two bands of an equaliser"
msgid ", "
msgstr "、"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:19
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"Shapes the tone of the sound with ten sliders, each lifting or cutting one "
"range of pitches, from the deepest bass to the highest treble."
msgstr ""
"10 本のスライダーで音色を整えます。それぞれのスライダーが、最も低い低音から最も高い高音までのうち 1 つの音域を持ち上げたり下げたりします。"

#. i18n: Hz stands for hertz, kHz for kilohertz.
#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"Every sound is a mix of low and high pitches. The block splits that range "
"into ten bands and lets you turn each one up or down. The bands are named by "
"the pitch in their middle, in hertz (Hz) and kilohertz (kHz): 31, 63, 125, "
"250 and 500 Hz, then 1, 2, 4, 8 and 16 kHz. Each is twice the one before."
msgstr ""
"どんな音も、低い音と高い音が混ざってできています。このブロックはその範囲を 10 "
"のバンドに分け、それぞれを上げ下げできるようにします。各バンドの名前は中心の周波数で、ヘルツ（Hz）とキロヘルツ（kHz）で表します。31、63、125、250、500"
" Hz、続いて 1、2、4、8、16 kHz です。それぞれが前のバンドの 2 倍になっています。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"Each band is about as wide as the gap to its neighbours, so a band touches "
"the bands beside it a little. Moving several sliders next to each other makes"
" a smooth curve rather than steps."
msgstr ""
"各バンドの幅は隣のバンドとの間隔とほぼ同じなので、隣り合うバンドに少しずつ重なります。隣り合う複数のスライダーを動かすと、段差ではなくなめらかなカーブになります。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:27
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"As a rough guide: the two lowest bands are deep bass and rumble, 125 and 250 "
"Hz are warmth and boom, 500 Hz to 2 kHz is the body of voices and most "
"instruments, 4 kHz is clarity and presence, and 8 and 16 kHz are brightness, "
"air and hiss."
msgstr ""
"おおまかな目安は次のとおりです。最も低い 2 つのバンドは深い低音とうなり、125 Hz と 250 Hz は温かみとこもった響き、500 Hz〜2 "
"kHz は声やほとんどの楽器の芯、4 kHz は明瞭さと存在感、8 kHz と 16 kHz は明るさ、空気感、ヒスノイズです。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:28
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"The block's tile shows the ten bands as ten bars, so you can see the shape at"
" a glance. To change them, open the settings."
msgstr "ブロックのタイルには 10 のバンドが 10 本のバーで表示されるので、形がひと目でわかります。変更するには設定を開いてください。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:29
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"A band at 0 dB changes nothing, and a new block starts with every band there."
" Every change glides in over a fiftieth of a second, so moving a slider while"
" sound plays makes no click."
msgstr ""
"0 dB のバンドは何も変えず、新しいブロックはすべてのバンドが 0 dB の状態で始まります。変更はすべて 50 分の 1 "
"秒かけてなめらかに反映されるので、音の再生中にスライダーを動かしてもクリックノイズは出ません。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:39
#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerPanel.qml:124
msgctxt "@label:group an equaliser's ten band sliders"
msgid "Bands"
msgstr "バンド"

#. i18n: dB stands for decibels.
#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:42
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"Ten upright sliders, one a band, with the band's pitch above it and its "
"setting below it. Each goes from −12 to +12 decibels (dB) in steps of half a "
"decibel: up lifts that band, down cuts it, and the line across the middle is "
"0 dB. The scale on the left is in decibels."
msgstr ""
"バンドごとに 1 本ずつ、計 10 本の縦のスライダーがあり、上にバンドの周波数、下にその設定値が表示されます。どれも −12 から +12 "
"デシベル（dB）まで 0.5 dB 刻みで動き、上げるとそのバンドが持ち上がり、下げると下がります。真ん中を横切る線が 0 dB "
"です。左の目盛りの単位はデシベルです。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:43
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid "Every 6 dB is about twice or half the strength of that band."
msgstr "6 dB ごとに、そのバンドの強さが約 2 倍、または約半分になります。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:49
#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerPanel.qml:246
msgctxt "@label:slider the gain before an equaliser's bands"
msgid "Preamp"
msgstr "プリアンプ"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:51
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"Turns the whole sound up or down before it reaches the bands, from −12 to +12"
" dB in steps of half a decibel. A new block starts at 0 dB."
msgstr "バンドに届く前に、音全体を −12 から +12 dB まで 0.5 dB 刻みで上げ下げします。新しいブロックでは 0 dB です。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:52
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"Lifting bands makes the sound louder, and can push it into clipping, where "
"its loudest moments are cut off and crackle. Lower the preamp by about as "
"much as your biggest lift to make room."
msgstr ""
"バンドを持ち上げると音が大きくなり、クリッピング（最も大きな瞬間が切り取られてバリバリと鳴ること）を起こすことがあります。余裕を作るため、最も大きく持ち上げた分と同じくらいプリアンプを下げてください。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:58
#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerPanel.qml:276
msgctxt "@option:check an equaliser lowers its output by its highest lift"
msgid "Keep level"
msgstr "レベルを維持"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:60
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"Does the preamp's job for you. When it is ticked, the block lowers its output"
" by as much as the highest point of the curve the bands make, whenever that "
"is above 0 dB. Lifting bands then changes the tone without making the loudest"
" part of the sound any louder."
msgstr ""
"プリアンプの役目を自動で果たします。チェックを入れると、バンドが作るカーブの最も高い点が 0 dB "
"を超えるたびに、その分だけブロックの出力を下げます。これでバンドを持ち上げても、音の最も大きな部分が大きくなることなく、音色だけが変わります。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:61
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"Cutting bands changes nothing here: the sound just gets a little quieter. It "
"is off for a new block."
msgstr "バンドを下げた場合は何も変わりません。音が少し小さくなるだけです。新しいブロックではオフです。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:67
#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerPanel.qml:292
msgctxt "@action:button put every band of an equaliser back at 0 dB"
msgid "Flatten"
msgstr "フラットに"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:69
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"Puts all ten bands and the preamp back at 0 dB at once, so the block leaves "
"the tone as it is. Keep level stays as it was. Ctrl+Z takes it back in one "
"step."
msgstr ""
"10 のバンドすべてとプリアンプを一度に 0 dB に戻し、ブロックが音色を変えないようにします。「レベルを維持」はそのままです。Ctrl+Z で 1 "
"回で元に戻せます。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:70
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid "The button can only be pressed when something is not at 0 dB."
msgstr "このボタンは、0 dB でないものがあるときだけ押せます。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:77
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid "Headphones or laptop speakers make music sound thin, boomy or harsh."
msgstr "ヘッドホンやノートパソコンのスピーカーで、音楽が薄っぺらく、ボワついて、またはきつく聞こえるとき。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:78
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid "A voice sounds muddy, muffled or sharp, and you want it clearer."
msgstr "声が濁ったり、こもったり、耳に刺さったりして、もっとはっきりさせたいとき。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:79
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid "A recording has a low rumble or a high hiss you want less of."
msgstr "録音に含まれる低いうなりや高いヒスノイズを減らしたいとき。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:80
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid "Some pitches are hard for you to hear, and you want them lifted."
msgstr "聞き取りにくい音域があり、それを持ち上げたいとき。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:87
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"Start from one of the presets at the bottom of the settings, such as Podcast "
"voice, Rumble cut, Hiss cut or Laptop speakers, and adjust from there. Flat "
"puts everything back."
msgstr ""
"設定の下にあるプリセット（「ポッドキャストの声」「低域ノイズカット」「ヒスカット」「ノートパソコンのスピーカー」など）から始め、そこから調整してください。「フラット」ですべて元に戻ります。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:88
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"To find a band that bothers you, lift it a long way, listen, and then cut it "
"once you know which one it is."
msgstr "気になるバンドを探すには、大きく持ち上げて聞いてみて、どのバンドかがわかったら下げてください。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:89
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"Cut rather than lift where you can: taking away what is too much usually "
"sounds more natural than adding to everything else."
msgstr "できるだけ持ち上げるより下げてください。ほかのすべてを足すより、多すぎる部分を取り除くほうが、ふつうは自然に聞こえます。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:90
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"If a meter after the block keeps reaching the red part at the top, tick Keep "
"level or lower the preamp."
msgstr "ブロックの後のメーターが何度も上の赤い部分に届くときは、「レベルを維持」にチェックを入れるか、プリアンプを下げてください。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerHelp.qml:91
msgctxt "@info help page of the 10-Band EQ block"
msgid ""
"For a change at only one end, the Bass & Treble block is quicker. To aim at a"
" single pitch precisely, use the Parametric EQ."
msgstr ""
"低音側か高音側だけを変えるなら、「低音・高音」ブロックのほうが手軽です。特定の周波数を正確に狙うなら、「パラメトリック EQ」を使ってください。"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerPanel.qml:182
msgctxt "@label:slider an equaliser band, '1 kHz'"
msgid "%1 band"
msgstr "%1 バンド"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerPanel.qml:234
msgctxt "@label:slider the gain before an equaliser's bands"
msgid "Preamp:"
msgstr "プリアンプ:"

#: blocks/equalizer10/ui/EqualizerPanel.qml:279
msgctxt "@info:tooltip"
msgid ""
"Lowers the output by the highest point of the curve, so lifting bands changes"
" the tone without making the sound any louder"
msgstr "カーブの最も高い点の分だけ出力を下げるので、バンドを持ち上げても音は大きくならず、音色だけが変わります"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:18
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Gives the sound the character recorded in a file: the echo of a room or a "
"church, the sound of a speaker cabinet, or a correction that makes a pair of "
"headphones sound more even."
msgstr "ファイルに記録された特性を音に与えます: 部屋や教会の響き、スピーカーキャビネットの音、ヘッドホンの音をより均一にする補正などです。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"An impulse response is a short recording of how a place or a piece of "
"equipment answers a single sharp click: the click itself, then everything it "
"turns into, its echoes and its colour. Many can be found to download, made in"
" real rooms or with real equipment."
msgstr ""
"インパルス応答とは、ある場所や機器が 1 回の鋭いクリック音にどう応えるかを記録した短い録音です: "
"クリック音そのものと、それが変わっていったすべて、つまり反射音や音色です。実際の部屋や機材で作られた多くのインパルス応答をダウンロードできます。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"The block plays every moment of the sound through that answer, so the sound "
"comes out as if it had been made in that room, or played through that "
"equipment."
msgstr "ブロックは音の一瞬一瞬をその応答に通すので、音はその部屋で鳴らしたか、その機器を通して再生したかのように聞こえます。"

#. i18n: FIR stands for finite impulse response, the kind of filter this is.
#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"FIR is short for finite impulse response: a filter built from a recording of "
"that kind."
msgstr "FIR は「有限インパルス応答」の略で、このような録音から作られるフィルタです。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:27
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Without a file, or with one it cannot use, the block passes the sound through"
" unchanged."
msgstr "ファイルがない場合や、使用できないファイルの場合、ブロックは音をそのまま通します。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:37
#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:91
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Pre-gain"
msgstr "プリゲイン"

#. i18n: dB stands for decibels.
#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:40
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Turns the sound down before the impulse response is applied, from 0 dB, "
"unchanged, down to −24 dB. A new block starts at 0 dB."
msgstr "インパルス応答をかける前に音を下げます。0 dB（変化なし）から −24 dB までです。新しいブロックは 0 dB から始まります。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:41
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Turn it down when the result is too loud, or the meter after the block "
"reaches the red: some responses make parts of the sound much stronger."
msgstr "結果の音が大きすぎるときや、ブロックの後のメーターが赤い範囲に届くときは下げてください: 応答によっては、音の一部がかなり強くなります。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:47
#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:113
msgctxt "@label how late a FIR Filter's output is"
msgid "Delay"
msgstr "遅延"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:49
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Not a setting: how late the sound leaves the block. It is always 256 samples,"
" about five thousandths of a second at 48 kHz, whatever the file. While the "
"session runs, the line says it in milliseconds too. Reverblabr keeps the "
"other lanes in step with that delay."
msgstr ""
"設定ではなく、音がブロックから出るまでの遅れを示します。ファイルにかかわらず常に 256 サンプルで、48 kHz では約 1000 分の 5 "
"秒です。セッションの実行中は、この行にミリ秒でも表示されます。Reverblabr はほかのレーンをこの遅延に合わせて揃えます。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:55
#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:135
msgctxt "@title:group the file a FIR Filter applies"
msgid "Impulse Response"
msgstr "インパルス応答"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:57
#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:163
msgctxt "@action:button choose an impulse response file"
msgid "Import File…"
msgstr "ファイルをインポート…"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:58
#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:173
msgctxt "@action:button stop using the impulse response file"
msgid "Remove File"
msgstr "ファイルを外す"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:61
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Import File… chooses the file: a WAV, FLAC or AIFF file with one, two or four"
" channels. The button beside the name, Remove File, stops using it."
msgstr ""
"「ファイルをインポート…」でファイルを選びます: チャンネルが 1、2、4 のいずれかの WAV、FLAC、AIFF "
"ファイルです。名前の横にある「ファイルを外す」ボタンで使用をやめます。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:62
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid "The channels say how the response is used:"
msgstr "チャンネル数によって、応答の使われ方が決まります:"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:65
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the FIR Filter block, the kinds of impulse response"
msgid "One channel, mono: the same response on the left and on the right."
msgstr "1 チャンネル、モノラル: 左右に同じ応答を使います。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:66
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the FIR Filter block, the kinds of impulse response"
msgid ""
"Two channels, stereo: one response for the left side and one for the right."
msgstr "2 チャンネル、ステレオ: 左用と右用にそれぞれ 1 つの応答を使います。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:67
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the FIR Filter block, the kinds of impulse response"
msgid ""
"Four channels, true stereo: how the left reaches the left and the right, and "
"how the right reaches the left and the right. A room recorded this way sounds"
" the most real."
msgstr ""
"4 チャンネル、トゥルーステレオ: 左の音が左右にどう届くか、右の音が左右にどう届くかを表します。この方法で録音された部屋が最も自然に聞こえます。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:70
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"A file made at another sample rate than the session's is converted to it. Up "
"to ten seconds of a response are used; a longer one is faded out at ten "
"seconds."
msgstr ""
"セッションと異なるサンプルレートで作られたファイルは、セッションのサンプルレートに変換されます。応答は最大 10 秒まで使われ、それより長い場合は 10 "
"秒でフェードアウトします。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:71
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"While the session runs, the line under the name says what the block made of "
"the file: mono, stereo or true stereo, and how long it is, in seconds and in "
"taps, one tap being one sample of the response. If the file is missing, is "
"not sound, or has another number of channels, the line says so and the sound "
"passes through unchanged."
msgstr ""
"セッションの実行中は、名前の下の行に、ブロックがファイルをどう解釈したかが表示されます: "
"モノラル、ステレオ、トゥルーステレオのいずれかと、長さ（秒とタップ数。1 タップは応答の 1 "
"サンプル）です。ファイルが見つからない、音声ではない、またはチャンネル数が対応していない場合は、この行にそう表示され、音はそのまま通過します。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:72
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Choosing another file while the sound plays crossfades from the old response "
"to the new one in about two hundredths of a second, so there is no click."
msgstr "音の再生中に別のファイルを選ぶと、古い応答から新しい応答へ約 100 分の 2 秒でクロスフェードするので、クリック音は出ません。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:78
#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:196
msgctxt ""
"@option:check scale the impulse response so noise comes out as loud as it "
"went in"
msgid "Match the input's loudness"
msgstr "入力の音量に合わせる"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:80
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Scales the response so that the sound comes out about as loud as it went in, "
"whatever the file was recorded at. It is on for a new block."
msgstr "ファイルの録音レベルにかかわらず、音が入ったときとほぼ同じ大きさで出るように応答を調整します。新しいブロックではオンです。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:81
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Untick it to use the file at the level it was made at, when its maker set "
"that level on purpose."
msgstr "作成者が意図してレベルを設定したファイルを、作られたときのレベルで使いたい場合は、チェックを外してください。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:87
#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:210
msgctxt ""
"@option:check take the silence off the start and the end of the impulse "
"response"
msgid "Trim silence at both ends"
msgstr "両端の無音を除去"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:89
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Cuts the near silence off the start and the end of the response: anything "
"more than 80 dB quieter than its loudest moment. The start of the sound then "
"comes through as early as it can, and a long silent tail costs nothing. Every"
" channel is trimmed alike, so they stay in step."
msgstr ""
"応答の最初と最後にある、ほぼ無音の部分を切り取ります: 最も大きい瞬間より 80 dB "
"以上小さい部分です。これにより音の始まりができるだけ早く届き、長い無音の末尾も処理の負担になりません。すべてのチャンネルが同じように切り取られるので、ずれは生じません。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:90
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"It is off for a new block, because the silence at the start of a room's "
"response is part of how far away the sound seems."
msgstr "新しいブロックではオフです。部屋の応答の最初にある無音は、音がどれだけ離れて聞こえるかを決める要素の 1 つだからです。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:97
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"You want a voice or an instrument to sound as if it were in a particular "
"hall, studio or church."
msgstr "声や楽器を、特定のホール、スタジオ、教会の中にいるように聞かせたいとき。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:98
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Your headphones have a correction file, and you want everything you listen to"
" through them corrected."
msgstr "ヘッドホン用の補正ファイルがあり、そのヘッドホンで聞くすべての音を補正したいとき。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:99
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"A guitar recorded straight into the computer should sound as if it came "
"through a speaker cabinet."
msgstr "コンピュータに直接録音したギターを、スピーカーキャビネットを通したように聞かせたいとき。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:106
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Put a Peak/RMS meter after the block the first time you try a file, and lower"
" Pre-gain if it reaches the red."
msgstr "初めてファイルを試すときはブロックの後に「ピーク/RMS」メーターを置き、赤い範囲に届く場合は「プリゲイン」を下げてください。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterHelp.qml:107
msgctxt "@info help page of the FIR Filter block"
msgid ""
"Responses longer than a few seconds take more of the computer's work. If the "
"sound starts to break up, try a shorter one."
msgstr "数秒より長い応答は、コンピュータの処理の負担が大きくなります。音が途切れ始めたら、短い応答を試してください。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:67
msgctxt "@label:slider how much a FIR Filter turns its input down first"
msgid "Pre-gain"
msgstr "プリゲイン"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:75
msgctxt "@info a level in decibels, '-6.0 dB'"
msgid "%1 dB"
msgstr "%1 dB"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:125
msgctxt "@info a delay in milliseconds and in samples, '5.3 ms (256 samples)'"
msgid "%1 ms (%2 samples)"
msgstr "%1 ms（%2 サンプル）"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:127
msgctxt "@info a delay in samples"
msgid "%1 samples"
msgstr "%1 サンプル"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:147
msgctxt "@info a FIR Filter with no file chosen"
msgid "No file chosen"
msgstr "ファイル未選択"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:222
msgctxt "@info what a FIR Filter does with a file at another rate"
msgid ""
"WAV, FLAC or AIFF, with one, two or four channels. A file at another sample "
"rate than the session's is resampled."
msgstr ""
"チャンネルが 1、2、4 のいずれかの WAV、FLAC、AIFF です。セッションと異なるサンプルレートのファイルはリサンプリングされます。"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:229
msgctxt "@title:window"
msgid "Choose an Impulse Response"
msgstr "インパルス応答を選択"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:236
msgctxt "@item:inlistbox a kind of file"
msgid "Audio files (*.wav *.flac *.aif *.aiff *.caf *.w64)"
msgstr "音声ファイル (*.wav *.flac *.aif *.aiff *.caf *.w64)"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterPanel.qml:237
msgctxt "@item:inlistbox a kind of file"
msgid "All files (*)"
msgstr "すべてのファイル (*)"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterState.qml:53
msgctxt "@info an impulse response with one channel, used on both sides"
msgid "Mono"
msgstr "モノラル"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterState.qml:54
msgctxt "@info an impulse response with a channel for each side"
msgid "Stereo"
msgstr "ステレオ"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterState.qml:56
msgctxt "@info an impulse response with four channels, each side to each side"
msgid "True stereo"
msgstr "トゥルーステレオ"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterState.qml:61
msgctxt "@info a FIR Filter block with no file chosen"
msgid "No impulse response"
msgstr "インパルス応答なし"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterState.qml:65
msgctxt "@info a FIR Filter block with no file passes the sound through"
msgid "Passes sound through"
msgstr "音をそのまま通過"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterState.qml:69
msgctxt "@info a FIR Filter block's file is missing or not an impulse response"
msgid "Cannot use this file"
msgstr "このファイルは使用できません"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterState.qml:73
msgctxt ""
"@info how long a FIR Filter block's impulse response is, '96,000 taps'"
msgid "%1 tap"
msgid_plural "%1 taps"
msgstr[0] "%1 タップ"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterState.qml:75
msgctxt "@info a FIR Filter block's file, while the session is not running"
msgid "Impulse response"
msgstr "インパルス応答"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterState.qml:80
msgctxt ""
"@info a FIR Filter block's impulse response: its channels, its length in "
"seconds and in taps"
msgid "%2, %3 s, %1 tap"
msgid_plural "%2, %3 s, %1 taps"
msgstr[0] "%2、%3 秒、%1 タップ"

#: blocks/firfilter/ui/FirFilterState.qml:84
msgctxt "@info why a FIR Filter block cannot use a file"
msgid ""
"The file is missing, is not audio, or has other than one, two or four "
"channels. The sound passes through unchanged."
msgstr "ファイルが見つからないか、音声ではないか、チャンネル数が 1、2、4 以外です。音はそのまま通過します。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:21
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Moves high sounds that one ear cannot hear down to a lower range where it "
"can. It brings back the hiss of s, sh and f, which tells \"sit\" from \"fit\""
" and \"cat\" from \"cats\"."
msgstr ""
"片方の耳で聞こえない高い音を、その耳で聞こえる低い帯域に移します。s、sh、f "
"の息がこすれるような音が戻るので、「しち」と「いち」や、英語の「cat」と「cats」を聞き分けやすくなります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Some ears hear nothing in a high range, however loud it is made. Turning that"
" range up does not help. But an important part of speech lives up there: the "
"hissing sounds that tell many words apart."
msgstr ""
"耳によっては、高い帯域の音がどれほど大きくしても聞こえないことがあります。その帯域を持ち上げても役に立ちません。ところが、その帯域には話し声の大切な部分があります。多くの言葉を聞き分ける手がかりになる、息がこすれるような音（摩擦音）です。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:27
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"This block takes the sound of a high range, the range it comes from, and puts"
" it into a lower range the ear still hears, the range it goes into. The moved"
" sound is not the same as the original, but it lets the ear notice that the "
"hiss was there, which makes words easier to tell apart."
msgstr ""
"このブロックは、高い帯域（移動元の帯域）の音を取り出し、耳がまだ聞こえる低い帯域（移動先の帯域）に入れます。移動した音は元の音と同じではありませんが、摩擦音がそこにあったことに耳が気づけるので、言葉を聞き分けやすくなります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:28
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Hertz (Hz) count how high a sound is; a thousand hertz is a kilohertz (kHz). "
"The hiss of an s sits above 4 kHz. Ordinary voices sit much lower."
msgstr ""
"ヘルツ（Hz）は音の高さを表す単位で、1000 ヘルツが 1 キロヘルツ（kHz）です。s の摩擦音は 4 kHz "
"より上にあります。普通の声は、それよりずっと低いところにあります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:29
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Each way of moving sound is called a move. The block can do up to four moves "
"at once, each from a range of its own. A new block has one move ready: sound "
"from 4 to 8 kHz squeezed into 2.5 to 4 kHz, with the high range emptied."
msgstr ""
"音を移す一つひとつのやり方を「移動」と呼びます。このブロックは、それぞれ別の帯域から、最大 4 つの移動を同時に行えます。新しいブロックには、移動が 1 "
"つ用意されています: 4〜8 kHz の音を 2.5〜4 kHz に圧縮し、高い帯域は空にします。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:30
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Every move works on the sound as it comes in, so moves never move each "
"other's sound, and their order does not matter. Where two moves put sound "
"into the same range, it adds up."
msgstr ""
"どの移動も入ってきたままの音に働くので、ある移動が別の移動の音をさらに移すことはなく、移動の順序も関係ありません。2 "
"つの移動が同じ帯域に音を入れる場合、その音は足し合わされます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:31
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"It works on one ear only. The other side passes through unchanged, held back "
"by exactly as long as the block takes, so both ears stay in step. Ear, at the"
" top of the settings, says which ear it is for, and the L (blue) or R (red) "
"on the block's tile shows it."
msgstr ""
"片方の耳だけに働きます。もう片方はそのまま通りますが、ブロックの処理にかかる時間とちょうど同じだけ遅らせるので、両耳の音がずれません。設定の一番上にある「耳」がどちらの耳用かを示し、ブロックのタイルの"
" L（青）または R（赤）でもわかります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:32
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"The block holds the sound back by about 21 thousandths of a second (ms) at "
"the usual rate of 48 kHz, and the other ear waits as long. Delay, at the "
"bottom of the settings, shows the exact figure."
msgstr ""
"一般的なサンプルレートの 48 kHz では、このブロックは音を約 21 "
"ミリ秒（ms）遅らせ、もう片方の耳も同じだけ待ちます。設定の一番下にある「遅延」に正確な値が表示されます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:44
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Left or Right: the ear the block works on. The other side passes through "
"unchanged. The block's tile shows an L (blue) or an R (red) to match."
msgstr ""
"「左」または「右」: ブロックが働く耳です。もう片方はそのまま通ります。ブロックのタイルには、それに合わせて L（青）または R（赤）が表示されます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:45
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"A new block starts on the left ear. When the session already has more blocks "
"of this kind for the left ear than for the right, a new one starts on the "
"right, so the second block you add is ready for the other ear."
msgstr ""
"新しいブロックは左耳から始まります。セッションにこの種類のブロックが、右耳用より左耳用のほうが多くある場合、新しいブロックは右耳から始まります。そのため、2"
" つ目に追加したブロックは、すぐにもう片方の耳に使えます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:46
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Changing it while the session runs fades across to the other side, without a "
"click. One undo puts it back. Loading a preset or putting the block back to "
"its default settings leaves it as it is, so a preset made for one ear can be "
"tried on the other."
msgstr ""
"セッションの実行中に変更すると、クリックノイズなしでもう片方の耳へフェードして切り替わります。「元に戻す」を 1 "
"回行うと元に戻ります。プリセットを読み込んだり、ブロックをデフォルト設定に戻したりしても、この設定は変わりません。そのため、片方の耳用に作ったプリセットをもう片方の耳で試せます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:52
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:266
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:53
msgctxt "@option:radio show the moves as arrows along a frequency axis"
msgid "Arrows"
msgstr "矢印"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:54
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Shows the moves along a line of pitches, low on the left and high on the "
"right. For each move, the shaded range is where the sound comes from and the "
"outlined range is where it goes, with an arrow between them."
msgstr ""
"移動を、音の高さの軸に沿って表示します。左が低い音、右が高い音です。各移動について、塗られた帯域が移動元、枠で囲まれた帯域が移動先で、その間を矢印が結びます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:55
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Click a range to pick its move. Drag the ends of the picked move's two ranges"
" to change them."
msgstr "帯域をクリックすると、その移動を選択します。選択した移動の 2 つの帯域の端をドラッグすると、帯域を変更できます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:56
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"While the session runs, the sound before the block and after it is drawn "
"behind, for this block's ear, so you can see it move. The numbers up the "
"side, in dBFS, are for that sound. The ranges and the arrows use only the "
"frequencies along the bottom."
msgstr ""
"セッションの実行中は、このブロックの耳について、ブロックを通る前と後の音が背後に描かれるので、音が移る様子が見えます。縦軸の数値（dBFS）は、その音のものです。帯域と矢印は、下の周波数の目盛りだけを使います。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:62
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:275
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:63
msgctxt ""
"@option:radio show the moves as a map of frequency in against frequency out"
msgid "Map"
msgstr "マップ"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:64
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Shows where each pitch ends up: the pitch going in runs across, and the pitch"
" coming out runs up, both in hertz. The straight diagonal is sound left where"
" it was. A squeezed move bends away from it, and a copied move adds a line "
"beside it."
msgstr ""
"それぞれの高さの音がどこに移るかを表示します: "
"横軸が入力の高さ、縦軸が出力の高さで、どちらもヘルツ単位です。まっすぐな対角線は、元の場所のままの音です。圧縮する移動はそこから曲がって離れ、コピーする移動はその横に線を"
" 1 本加えます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:70
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:299
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:71
msgctxt "@option:check hear only the sound the moves add"
msgid "Moved sound only"
msgstr "移動した音のみ"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:72
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Plays only the sound the moves add, without the rest. Turn it on while you "
"set a move's Level, to hear exactly what it adds, then turn it off again."
msgstr ""
"移動が加える音だけを再生し、それ以外は再生しません。移動の「レベル」を設定するときにオンにすると、加わる音を正確に聞けます。終わったらオフに戻してください。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:73
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"It is a way of listening, not part of the setting: presets leave it alone."
msgstr "これは聞き方の切り替えで、設定の一部ではありません。プリセットはこれを変更しません。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:79
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:673
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:80
msgctxt "@label the moves of a Frequency Lowering or Raising block"
msgid "Moves"
msgstr "移動"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:81
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"A button for each move in use, Move 1 to Move 4. Click one to pick that move:"
" the settings under the buttons are the picked move's. While the session "
"runs, a move that is moving sound shows a small play sign."
msgstr ""
"使用中の移動ごとのボタン（「移動 1」〜「移動 4」）です。クリックすると、その移動を選択します: "
"ボタンの下の設定は、選択した移動のものです。セッションの実行中は、音を移している移動に小さな再生マークが表示されます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:87
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:709
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:88
msgctxt "@action:button add a move to a Frequency Lowering or Raising block"
msgid "Add a move"
msgstr "移動を追加"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:89
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"The plus button adds a move, with ranges of its own to start from, and picks "
"it. Drag its ranges to where you need them. It cannot be pressed once four "
"moves are in use."
msgstr ""
"プラスボタンを押すと、初期の帯域を持つ移動が追加され、選択されます。帯域を必要な位置までドラッグしてください。移動を 4 つ使っているときは押せません。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:95
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:726
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:96
msgctxt ""
"@action:button take a Frequency Lowering or Raising block's picked move away"
msgid "Remove this move"
msgstr "この移動を削除"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:97
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"The button at the end of the row takes the picked move away. To stop a move "
"only for a moment, switch it off instead."
msgstr "列の最後にあるボタンを押すと、選択した移動が削除されます。一時的に止めたいだけなら、代わりにオフにしてください。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:103
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:743
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:104
msgctxt "@label:checkbox whether the chosen move acts"
msgid "Move on"
msgstr "移動のオン/オフ"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:105
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"The switch beside On. Off, the picked move does nothing, but keeps its "
"settings. Switch it off and on to hear what the move does."
msgstr ""
"「オン」の横にあるスイッチです。オフにすると、選択した移動は何もしなくなりますが、設定は保たれます。オフとオンを切り替えると、その移動の効果を聞き比べられます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:111
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:759
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:113
msgctxt "@label how a Frequency Lowering or Raising move carries sound"
msgid "Method"
msgstr "方式"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:117
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid "How the move carries the sound down:"
msgstr "移動が音をどう下げるかを選びます:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:120
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block, one choice of Method"
msgid ""
"Squeeze fits the whole range the sound comes from into the smaller range it "
"goes into: its bottom lands on the bottom, its top on the top, and everything"
" in between is pressed closer together. Use it where the ear hears nothing at"
" all, and empty the range the sound came from. A new block's first move "
"squeezes."
msgstr ""
"「圧縮」は、移動元の帯域全体を、より狭い移動先の帯域に収めます: "
"下端は下端に、上端は上端に移り、その間はすべて詰められます。耳がまったく聞こえない帯域に使い、移動元の帯域は空にしてください。新しいブロックの最初の移動は「圧縮」です。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:121
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block, one choice of Method"
msgid ""
"Copy down moves every sound down by the same step, so the bottom of the range"
" it comes from lands on the bottom of the range it goes into, and the tones "
"of a voice keep their spacing. Sound that would land above the top of that "
"range is left out. Use it where the ear still hears a little of the high "
"range, and keep the original."
msgstr ""
"「下にコピー」は、すべての音を同じ幅だけ下げます。移動元の帯域の下端が移動先の帯域の下端に移り、声に含まれる音どうしの間隔は保たれます。移動先の帯域の上端より上に来る音は省かれます。耳が高い帯域をまだ少し聞き取れる場合に使い、元の音は残してください。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:127
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:804
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:131
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Range the sound comes from"
msgstr "移動元の帯域"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:129
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"The high range the picked move takes sound from, shown beside From. Drag the "
"two handles of the slider, or the ends of the shaded range on the Arrows "
"view. The ends can be anywhere from 125 Hz to 16 kHz."
msgstr ""
"選択した移動が音を取り出す高い帯域で、「移動元」の横に表示されます。スライダーの 2 つのハンドルか、「矢印」表示で塗られた帯域の端をドラッグします。端は"
" 125 Hz〜16 kHz の間で自由に設定できます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:130
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Set it to the range your ear does not hear. Neither range can be narrower "
"than a sixth of an octave, and the range the sound comes from always stays "
"above the range it goes into."
msgstr ""
"耳が聞こえない帯域に合わせてください。どちらの帯域も 6 分の 1 オクターブより狭くはできず、移動元の帯域は常に移動先の帯域より上にあります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:136
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:848
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:141
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Range the sound goes into"
msgstr "移動先の帯域"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:138
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"The lower range the picked move puts sound into, shown beside Into. Set it to"
" a range your ear still hears well, just below the range the sound comes "
"from."
msgstr "選択した移動が音を入れる低い帯域で、「移動先」の横に表示されます。耳がまだよく聞こえる帯域、つまり移動元の帯域のすぐ下に合わせてください。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:144
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:890
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:149
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Level of the moved sound"
msgstr "移動した音のレベル"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:146
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"How loud the moved sound is, against how loud it was where it came from: from"
" −24 dB to +12 dB, in steps of half a decibel. A new move starts at 0 dB, the"
" same level."
msgstr ""
"移動した音の大きさを、元の場所での大きさを基準に設定します: −24 dB〜+12 dB、0.5 dB 刻みです。新しい移動は 0 "
"dB（同じレベル）から始まります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:147
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Set it so an s is clear but not sharp. Moved sound only helps you hear it on "
"its own."
msgstr "s の音がはっきり聞こえ、しかも耳障りにならないように設定してください。「移動した音のみ」を使うと、その音だけを聞けます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:153
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:920
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:158
msgctxt ""
"@label what becomes of the range a Frequency Lowering or Raising move takes "
"sound from"
msgid "Leave the source"
msgstr "元の帯域の扱い"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:160
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid "What becomes of the high range once its sound has been copied lower:"
msgstr "音を低い帯域へコピーした後、高い帯域をどうするかを選びます:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:163
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block, one choice of Leave the "
"source"
msgid "As it was keeps it unchanged, for an ear that still hears some of it."
msgstr "「そのまま」は、変更せずに残します。その帯域をまだ少し聞き取れる耳向けです。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:164
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block, one choice of Leave the "
"source"
msgid "Quieter turns it down by 12 dB."
msgstr "「小さく」は、12 dB 下げます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:165
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block, one choice of Leave the "
"source"
msgid ""
"Empty takes its sound out. Use it where the ear hears nothing there anyway. A"
" new block's first move empties it."
msgstr ""
"「空にする」は、その帯域の音を取り除きます。その帯域がもともと耳に何も聞こえない場合に使います。新しいブロックの最初の移動は「空にする」です。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:171
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:948
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:176
msgctxt "@label when a Frequency Lowering or Raising move acts"
msgid "Acts"
msgstr "動作"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:177
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid "When the move does its work:"
msgstr "移動がいつ働くかを選びます:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:180
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block, one choice of Acts"
msgid ""
"Always moves everything in the range, all the time. A new move acts always."
msgstr "「常に」は、帯域内のすべての音を常に移します。新しい移動は「常に」です。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:181
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block, one choice of Acts"
msgid ""
"On s, sh, f moves sound only while the high range is louder than everything "
"below it, as it is in a hissing sound. Vowels and most music pass as they "
"came."
msgstr ""
"「s、sh、f のとき」は、摩擦音のように、高い帯域がそれより下のすべてより大きいときだけ音を移します。母音やほとんどの音楽は、そのまま通ります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:187
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:980
#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:192
msgctxt "@label how late a Frequency Lowering or Raising block's sound is"
msgid "Delay"
msgstr "遅延"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:189
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Not a setting: how long the block holds the sound back, in thousandths of a "
"second. It depends only on the session's rate, about 21 ms at 48 kHz. The "
"other ear waits as long, so the two stay in step."
msgstr ""
"設定ではありません: ブロックが音を遅らせる時間を、ミリ秒で示します。セッションのサンプルレートだけで決まり、48 kHz では約 21 ms "
"です。もう片方の耳も同じだけ待つので、両耳の音はずれません。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:196
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"You mix up words that differ only in an s, an f or a sh, such as \"sit\" and "
"\"fit\"."
msgstr "「しち」と「いち」のように、s、f、sh の音だけが違う言葉を聞き間違えるとき。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:197
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid "You miss plurals: \"cat\" and \"cats\" sound the same to you."
msgstr "複数形を聞き逃すとき（英語の「cat」と「cats」が同じに聞こえるなど）。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:198
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"An audiogram shows no response at high pitches, or the Hearing Compensation "
"fit marked high bands where more lift is unlikely to help."
msgstr ""
"オージオグラムで高い音に反応がないとき、または「聴覚補正」のフィッティングで、これ以上持ち上げても効果が見込めない高いバンドに印が付いたとき。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:205
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Put it before Hearing Compensation, so the moved sound gets the lift of the "
"range it lands in."
msgstr "「聴覚補正」の前に置いてください。そうすれば、移動した音にも移動先の帯域の持ち上げが適用されます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:206
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"Start with the first move as it is, listen to speech for a while, then change"
" one thing at a time."
msgstr "まずは最初の移動をそのまま使い、しばらく話し声を聞いてから、一度に 1 つずつ変更してください。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:207
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"If voices sound harsh or lisped, try a lower Level, or choose On s, sh, f."
msgstr "声が耳障りに聞こえたり、舌足らずに聞こえたりする場合は、「レベル」を下げるか、「s、sh、f のとき」を選んでみてください。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:208
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"For the other ear, add a second block of this kind: it starts on the right "
"ear. Set it up for that ear."
msgstr "もう片方の耳には、この種類のブロックをもう 1 つ追加してください: そのブロックは右耳から始まります。その耳に合わせて設定します。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyLoweringHelp.qml:209
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Lowering block"
msgid ""
"For a dip in the middle of your hearing, use this block for the lower half of"
" the dip and Frequency Raising for the upper half, both for the same ear."
msgstr "聴力の中ほどの帯域が落ち込んでいる場合は、落ち込みの下半分にこのブロックを、上半分に「周波数引き上げ」を使います。どちらも同じ耳に使います。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMoveFace.qml:71
msgctxt "@info a Frequency Lowering or Raising tile with no move that acts"
msgid "No moves"
msgstr "移動なし"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMoveFace.qml:93
msgctxt ""
"@info a Frequency Lowering or Raising tile while one of its moves is moving "
"sound"
msgid "moving sound"
msgstr "音を移動中"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMoveFace.qml:98
msgctxt ""
"@info a Frequency Raising tile whose first move gives low sounds their "
"harmonics"
msgid "harmonics added"
msgstr "倍音を追加"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMoveFace.qml:102
msgctxt "@info a Frequency Raising tile whose first move copies sound up"
msgid "copied up"
msgstr "上にコピー"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMoveFace.qml:104
msgctxt "@info a Frequency Raising tile whose first move squeezes sound up"
msgid "squeezed up"
msgstr "上に圧縮"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMoveFace.qml:108
msgctxt "@info a Frequency Lowering tile whose first move copies sound down"
msgid "copied down"
msgstr "下にコピー"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMoveFace.qml:110
msgctxt "@info a Frequency Lowering tile whose first move squeezes sound down"
msgid "squeezed down"
msgstr "下に圧縮"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:330
msgctxt "@label the axis across a map of frequency in against frequency out"
msgid "Frequency in, Hz"
msgstr "入力周波数（Hz）"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:331
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:107
msgctxt "@label the axis of a graph across frequency"
msgid "Frequency, Hz"
msgstr "周波数（Hz）"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:333
msgctxt "@label the axis up a map of frequency in against frequency out"
msgid "Frequency out, Hz"
msgstr "出力周波数（Hz）"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:334
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:766
msgctxt "@label the axis of a graph of level, 0 is full scale"
msgid "Level, dBFS"
msgstr "レベル（dBFS）"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:741
msgctxt "@label:checkbox whether a Frequency Lowering or Raising move acts"
msgid "On:"
msgstr "オン:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:755
msgctxt "@label how a Frequency Lowering or Raising move carries sound"
msgid "Method:"
msgstr "方式:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:788
msgctxt ""
"@label:slider the range a Frequency Lowering or Raising move takes sound from"
msgid "From:"
msgstr "移動元:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:832
msgctxt ""
"@label:slider the range a Frequency Lowering or Raising move puts sound into"
msgid "Into:"
msgstr "移動先:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:878
msgctxt ""
"@label:slider the level of the sound a Frequency Lowering or Raising move "
"adds"
msgid "Level:"
msgstr "レベル:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:917
msgctxt ""
"@label what becomes of the range a Frequency Lowering or Raising move takes "
"sound from"
msgid "Leave the source:"
msgstr "元の帯域の扱い:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:946
msgctxt "@label when a Frequency Lowering or Raising move acts"
msgid "Acts:"
msgstr "動作:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:990
msgctxt "@info a delay in milliseconds, '43 ms'"
msgid "%1 ms"
msgstr "%1 ms"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:1000
msgctxt "@info what the Frequency Raising block does"
msgid ""
"Moves sound from a low or middle range the ear makes no use of into a higher "
"range it hears. Copy up adds a copy two octaves or so higher; Squeeze fits "
"the whole range into another; Add harmonics (experimental) gives each low "
"sound its harmonics higher up, so a voice keeps its pitch. It holds the sound"
" back by about 43 ms, or 85 ms while a move starts below 250 Hz, which takes "
"longer to tell apart. Put it before any block that sets the level of each "
"range."
msgstr ""
"耳が活用できない低い帯域や中ほどの帯域の音を、聞こえる高い帯域に移します。「上にコピー」は 2 "
"オクターブほど高い位置にコピーを加え、「圧縮」は帯域全体を別の帯域に収め、「倍音を追加」（実験的）は低い音それぞれに高い倍音を加えるので、声の高さが保たれます。音は約"
" 43 ms 遅れます。移動が 250 Hz より下から始まる場合は、聞き分けに時間がかかるため約 85 ms "
"遅れます。帯域ごとのレベルを決めるブロックより前に置いてください。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyMovePanel.qml:1002
msgctxt "@info what the Frequency Lowering block does"
msgid ""
"Moves sound from a range the ear makes no use of into a lower range it hears:"
" the hiss of s, sh and f, which tells \"sit\" from \"fit\". Squeeze fits the "
"whole range into a smaller one; Copy down adds a copy lower down. Put it "
"before any block that sets the level of each range, so the moved sound gets "
"the level of where it lands."
msgstr ""
"耳が活用できない帯域の音を、聞こえる低い帯域に移します。たとえば、「しち」と「いち」を聞き分ける s、sh、f "
"の摩擦音です。「圧縮」は帯域全体をより狭い帯域に収め、「下にコピー」は低い位置にコピーを加えます。帯域ごとのレベルを決めるブロックより前に置くと、移動した音に移動先のレベルが適用されます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Moves low or middle sounds that one ear hears poorly up to a higher range "
"where it hears better. Parts of it are experimental."
msgstr "片方の耳で聞こえにくい低い音や中ほどの音を、よく聞こえる高い帯域に移します。一部の機能は実験的なものです。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:28
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Some ears hear the low range faintly or not at all, while higher sounds are "
"fine. This block takes the sound of a low or middle range, the range it comes"
" from, and puts it into a higher range the ear hears, the range it goes into."
" It works like Frequency Lowering, the other way round."
msgstr ""
"耳によっては、高い音は問題なく聞こえるのに、低い帯域がかすかにしか、またはまったく聞こえないことがあります。このブロックは、低い帯域や中ほどの帯域（移動元の帯域）の音を取り出し、耳が聞こえる高い帯域（移動先の帯域）に入れます。「周波数引き下げ」と同じ仕組みで、向きが逆です。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:29
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Hertz (Hz) count how high a sound is; a thousand hertz is a kilohertz (kHz). "
"A deep voice has its lowest tone round 100 Hz."
msgstr ""
"ヘルツ（Hz）は音の高さを表す単位で、1000 ヘルツが 1 キロヘルツ（kHz）です。低い声では、いちばん低い音が 100 Hz 前後にあります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:30
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Each way of moving sound is called a move. The block can do up to four moves "
"at once, each from a range of its own. A new block has one move ready: sound "
"from 250 to 500 Hz copied two octaves up into 1 to 2 kHz, with the original "
"kept. An octave up is twice as high."
msgstr ""
"音を移す一つひとつのやり方を「移動」と呼びます。このブロックは、それぞれ別の帯域から、最大 4 つの移動を同時に行えます。新しいブロックには、移動が 1 "
"つ用意されています: 250〜500 Hz の音を 2 オクターブ上の 1〜2 kHz にコピーし、元の音は残します。1 オクターブ上がると、周波数は 2"
" 倍になります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:31
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Every move works on the sound as it comes in, so moves never move each "
"other's sound, and their order does not matter. Where two moves put sound "
"into the same range, it adds up."
msgstr ""
"どの移動も入ってきたままの音に働くので、ある移動が別の移動の音をさらに移すことはなく、移動の順序も関係ありません。2 "
"つの移動が同じ帯域に音を入れる場合、その音は足し合わされます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:32
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"It works on one ear only. The other side passes through unchanged, held back "
"by exactly as long as the block takes, so both ears stay in step. Ear, at the"
" top of the settings, says which ear it is for, and the L (blue) or R (red) "
"on the block's tile shows it."
msgstr ""
"片方の耳だけに働きます。もう片方はそのまま通りますが、ブロックの処理にかかる時間とちょうど同じだけ遅らせるので、両耳の音がずれません。設定の一番上にある「耳」がどちらの耳用かを示し、ブロックのタイルの"
" L（青）または R（赤）でもわかります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:33
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Low sounds take longer to tell apart, so this block holds the sound back "
"longer than Frequency Lowering: about 43 thousandths of a second (ms) at the "
"usual rate of 48 kHz while every move starts at 250 Hz or above, and about 85"
" ms once a move starts lower. The other ear waits as long. Even 43 ms can be "
"noticed with video, where lips move before you hear the voice, so it is "
"better kept for listening."
msgstr ""
"低い音は聞き分けに時間がかかるため、このブロックは「周波数引き下げ」より長く音を遅らせます。一般的なサンプルレートの 48 kHz では、すべての移動が "
"250 Hz 以上から始まる間は約 43 ミリ秒（ms）、それより下から始まる移動があると約 85 ms です。もう片方の耳も同じだけ待ちます。43 ms"
" でも、声が聞こえる前に唇が動いて見えるので、動画では気づくことがあります。音を聞くだけの用途に向いています。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:45
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Left or Right: the ear the block works on. The other side passes through "
"unchanged. The block's tile shows an L (blue) or an R (red) to match."
msgstr ""
"「左」または「右」: ブロックが働く耳です。もう片方はそのまま通ります。ブロックのタイルには、それに合わせて L（青）または R（赤）が表示されます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:46
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"A new block starts on the left ear. When the session already has more blocks "
"of this kind for the left ear than for the right, a new one starts on the "
"right, so the second block you add is ready for the other ear."
msgstr ""
"新しいブロックは左耳から始まります。セッションにこの種類のブロックが、右耳用より左耳用のほうが多くある場合、新しいブロックは右耳から始まります。そのため、2"
" つ目に追加したブロックは、すぐにもう片方の耳に使えます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:47
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Changing it while the session runs fades across to the other side, without a "
"click. One undo puts it back. Loading a preset or putting the block back to "
"its default settings leaves it as it is, so a preset made for one ear can be "
"tried on the other."
msgstr ""
"セッションの実行中に変更すると、クリックノイズなしでもう片方の耳へフェードして切り替わります。「元に戻す」を 1 "
"回行うと元に戻ります。プリセットを読み込んだり、ブロックをデフォルト設定に戻したりしても、この設定は変わりません。そのため、片方の耳用に作ったプリセットをもう片方の耳で試せます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:55
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Shows the moves along a line of pitches, low on the left and high on the "
"right. For each move, the shaded range is where the sound comes from and the "
"outlined range is where it goes, with an arrow between them."
msgstr ""
"移動を、音の高さの軸に沿って表示します。左が低い音、右が高い音です。各移動について、塗られた帯域が移動元、枠で囲まれた帯域が移動先で、その間を矢印が結びます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:56
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Click a range to pick its move. Drag the ends of the picked move's two ranges"
" to change them."
msgstr "帯域をクリックすると、その移動を選択します。選択した移動の 2 つの帯域の端をドラッグすると、帯域を変更できます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:57
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"While the session runs, the sound before the block and after it is drawn "
"behind, for this block's ear, so you can see it move. The numbers up the "
"side, in dBFS, are for that sound. The ranges and the arrows use only the "
"frequencies along the bottom."
msgstr ""
"セッションの実行中は、このブロックの耳について、ブロックを通る前と後の音が背後に描かれるので、音が移る様子が見えます。縦軸の数値（dBFS）は、その音のものです。帯域と矢印は、下の周波数の目盛りだけを使います。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:65
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Shows where each pitch ends up: the pitch going in runs across, and the pitch"
" coming out runs up, both in hertz. The straight diagonal is sound left where"
" it was. A squeezed move bends away from it, a copied move adds a line beside"
" it, and Add harmonics adds a line for each harmonic."
msgstr ""
"それぞれの高さの音がどこに移るかを表示します: "
"横軸が入力の高さ、縦軸が出力の高さで、どちらもヘルツ単位です。まっすぐな対角線は、元の場所のままの音です。圧縮する移動はそこから曲がって離れ、コピーする移動はその横に線を"
" 1 本加え、「倍音を追加」は倍音ごとに線を 1 本加えます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:73
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Plays only the sound the moves add, without the rest. Turn it on while you "
"set a move's Level, to hear exactly what it adds, then turn it off again."
msgstr ""
"移動が加える音だけを再生し、それ以外は再生しません。移動の「レベル」を設定するときにオンにすると、加わる音を正確に聞けます。終わったらオフに戻してください。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:74
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"It is a way of listening, not part of the setting: presets leave it alone."
msgstr "これは聞き方の切り替えで、設定の一部ではありません。プリセットはこれを変更しません。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:82
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"A button for each move in use, Move 1 to Move 4. Click one to pick that move:"
" the settings under the buttons are the picked move's. While the session "
"runs, a move that is moving sound shows a small play sign."
msgstr ""
"使用中の移動ごとのボタン（「移動 1」〜「移動 4」）です。クリックすると、その移動を選択します: "
"ボタンの下の設定は、選択した移動のものです。セッションの実行中は、音を移している移動に小さな再生マークが表示されます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:90
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"The plus button adds a move, with ranges of its own to start from, and picks "
"it. Drag its ranges to where you need them. It cannot be pressed once four "
"moves are in use."
msgstr ""
"プラスボタンを押すと、初期の帯域を持つ移動が追加され、選択されます。帯域を必要な位置までドラッグしてください。移動を 4 つ使っているときは押せません。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:98
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"The button at the end of the row takes the picked move away. A move taken "
"away no longer counts towards the delay."
msgstr "列の最後にあるボタンを押すと、選択した移動が削除されます。削除した移動は、遅延の計算に含まれなくなります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:106
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"The switch beside On. Off, the picked move does nothing, but keeps its "
"settings. Switch it off and on to hear what the move does."
msgstr ""
"「オン」の横にあるスイッチです。オフにすると、選択した移動は何もしなくなりますが、設定は保たれます。オフとオンを切り替えると、その移動の効果を聞き比べられます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:107
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"A move that is switched off still counts towards the delay, so comparing "
"never moves the ear in time."
msgstr "オフにした移動も遅延の計算に含まれるので、聞き比べても、その耳の音のタイミングがずれることはありません。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:120
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid "How the move carries the sound up:"
msgstr "移動が音をどう上げるかを選びます:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:123
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block, one choice of Method"
msgid ""
"Squeeze fits the whole range the sound comes from into the range it goes "
"into: its bottom lands on the bottom, its top on the top. Use it where the "
"ear hears nothing at all in the low range, and empty the range the sound came"
" from."
msgstr ""
"「圧縮」は、移動元の帯域全体を移動先の帯域に収めます: "
"下端は下端に、上端は上端に移ります。耳が低い帯域をまったく聞き取れない場合に使い、移動元の帯域は空にしてください。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:124
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block, one choice of Method"
msgid ""
"Copy up moves every sound up by the same step, so the bottom of the range it "
"comes from lands on the bottom of the range it goes into, and the tones of a "
"voice keep their spacing. Sound that would land above the top of that range "
"is left out. A new block's first move copies up."
msgstr ""
"「上にコピー」は、すべての音を同じ幅だけ上げます。移動元の帯域の下端が移動先の帯域の下端に移り、声に含まれる音どうしの間隔は保たれます。移動先の帯域の上端より上に来る音は省かれます。新しいブロックの最初の移動は「上にコピー」です。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:125
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block, one choice of Method"
msgid ""
"Add harmonics is experimental. Moving a voice up raises its pitch. Instead, "
"this leaves each low sound where it is and adds its harmonics, the tones at "
"twice its pitch, three times and so on up to sixteen times, wherever they "
"fall in the range the sound goes into. The ear takes the pitch from the "
"harmonics, so the voice still sounds like itself. Not much is known about how"
" well this helps, so trust your ears."
msgstr ""
"「倍音を追加」は実験的な機能です。声を上に移すと、声の高さが上がってしまいます。この方式では、低い音はそれぞれ元の場所に残したまま、その倍音（元の高さの "
"2 倍、3 倍と続き、16 "
"倍までの音）のうち、移動先の帯域に入るものを加えます。耳は倍音から音の高さを感じ取るので、声は本来の声らしく聞こえます。どれほど効果があるかはまだよくわかっていないので、自分の耳で確かめてください。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:133
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"The low range the picked move takes sound from, shown beside From. Drag the "
"two handles of the slider, or the ends of the shaded range on the Arrows "
"view. The ends can be anywhere from 60 Hz to 16 kHz."
msgstr ""
"選択した移動が音を取り出す低い帯域で、「移動元」の横に表示されます。スライダーの 2 つのハンドルか、「矢印」表示で塗られた帯域の端をドラッグします。端は"
" 60 Hz〜16 kHz の間で自由に設定できます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:134
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Set it to the range your ear hears poorly. Neither range can be narrower than"
" a sixth of an octave, and the range the sound comes from always stays below "
"the range it goes into."
msgstr ""
"耳が聞こえにくい帯域に合わせてください。どちらの帯域も 6 分の 1 オクターブより狭くはできず、移動元の帯域は常に移動先の帯域より下にあります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:135
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"When a move starts below 250 Hz, the delay grows from about 43 ms to about 85"
" ms. If that happens while the session runs, the sound fades out, stays quiet"
" for about as long as the new delay, and fades back in: a short gap, not a "
"click."
msgstr ""
"移動が 250 Hz より下から始まると、遅延は約 43 ms から約 85 ms "
"に増えます。セッションの実行中にそうなると、音はフェードアウトし、新しい遅延とほぼ同じ時間だけ無音になってから、フェードインします。クリックノイズではなく、短い途切れになります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:143
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"The higher range the picked move puts sound into, shown beside Into. Set it "
"to a range your ear hears well."
msgstr "選択した移動が音を入れる高い帯域で、「移動先」の横に表示されます。耳がよく聞こえる帯域に合わせてください。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:151
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"How loud the moved sound is, against how loud it was where it came from: from"
" −24 dB to +12 dB, in steps of half a decibel. A new move starts at 0 dB, the"
" same level."
msgstr ""
"移動した音の大きさを、元の場所での大きさを基準に設定します: −24 dB〜+12 dB、0.5 dB 刻みです。新しい移動は 0 "
"dB（同じレベル）から始まります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:152
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid "Moved sound only helps you hear it on its own."
msgstr "「移動した音のみ」を使うと、その音だけを聞けます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:165
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid "What becomes of the low range once its sound has been carried up:"
msgstr "音を高い帯域へ移した後、低い帯域をどうするかを選びます:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:168
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Frequency Raising block, one choice of Leave the "
"source"
msgid ""
"As it was keeps it unchanged, for an ear that still hears some of it. A new "
"block's first move keeps it."
msgstr "「そのまま」は、変更せずに残します。その帯域をまだ少し聞き取れる耳向けです。新しいブロックの最初の移動は「そのまま」です。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:169
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Frequency Raising block, one choice of Leave the "
"source"
msgid "Quieter turns it down by 12 dB."
msgstr "「小さく」は、12 dB 下げます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:170
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Frequency Raising block, one choice of Leave the "
"source"
msgid ""
"Empty takes its sound out. Use it where the ear hears nothing there anyway."
msgstr "「空にする」は、その帯域の音を取り除きます。その帯域がもともと耳に何も聞こえない場合に使います。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:182
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid "When the move does its work:"
msgstr "移動がいつ働くかを選びます:"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:185
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block, one choice of Acts"
msgid ""
"Always moves everything in the range, all the time. A new move acts always."
msgstr "「常に」は、帯域内のすべての音を常に移します。新しい移動は「常に」です。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:186
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block, one choice of Acts"
msgid ""
"On low sounds moves sound only while the low range is louder than everything "
"above it, as it is with a deep voice or a hum. Sound that is mostly higher "
"passes as it came."
msgstr ""
"「低い音のとき」は、低い声やハムノイズのように、低い帯域がそれより上のすべてより大きいときだけ音を移します。主に高い音でできた音は、そのまま通ります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:194
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Not a setting: how long the block holds the sound back with its moves as they"
" are, in thousandths of a second. It grows as soon as a move's range the "
"sound comes from reaches below 250 Hz, even before the session runs, so you "
"know what you will get."
msgstr ""
"設定ではありません: 現在の移動の設定で、ブロックが音を遅らせる時間をミリ秒で示します。移動元の帯域が 250 Hz "
"より下に及ぶと、セッションを実行する前でもすぐに値が増えるので、実際の遅延を前もって確認できます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:201
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"One ear hears deep voices and low sounds faintly, or not at all, while higher"
" sounds are clear."
msgstr "片方の耳で、高い音ははっきり聞こえるのに、低い声や低い音がかすかにしか、またはまったく聞こえないとき。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:202
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Your hearing has a dip in the middle: use this block together with Frequency "
"Lowering."
msgstr "聴力の中ほどの帯域が落ち込んでいるとき。このブロックを「周波数引き下げ」と組み合わせて使います。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:203
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid "You listen to speech or music, and a small delay does not matter."
msgstr "話し声や音楽を聞くだけで、少しの遅延が問題にならないとき。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:210
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Put it before Hearing Compensation, so the moved sound gets the lift of the "
"range it lands in."
msgstr "「聴覚補正」の前に置いてください。そうすれば、移動した音にも移動先の帯域の持ち上げが適用されます。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:211
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"Keep the ranges at 250 Hz or above if you can: the delay stays at about 43 "
"ms."
msgstr "できれば帯域は 250 Hz 以上にしてください: 遅延が約 43 ms のままになります。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:212
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"For a dip from 1 to 4 kHz, for example: Frequency Lowering squeezes 1 to 2 "
"kHz into 500 Hz to 1 kHz, and this block squeezes 2 to 4 kHz into 4 to 8 kHz,"
" both for the same ear. Split like this, their order does not matter."
msgstr ""
"たとえば 1〜4 kHz が落ち込んでいる場合: 「周波数引き下げ」で 1〜2 kHz を 500 Hz〜1 kHz に圧縮し、このブロックで 2〜4 "
"kHz を 4〜8 kHz に圧縮します。どちらも同じ耳に使います。このように分ければ、2 つのブロックの順序は関係ありません。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:213
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"If the ranges of the two blocks overlap, the second block moves what the "
"first has already moved. Put first the move you want the other to work on."
msgstr ""
"2 つのブロックの帯域が重なる場合、後のブロックは、前のブロックがすでに移した音をさらに移します。もう一方に処理させたい移動のほうを先に置いてください。"

#: blocks/frequencymove/ui/FrequencyRaisingHelp.qml:214
msgctxt "@info help page of the Frequency Raising block"
msgid ""
"For the other ear, add a second block of this kind: it starts on the right "
"ear. Set it up for that ear."
msgstr "もう片方の耳には、この種類のブロックをもう 1 つ追加してください: そのブロックは右耳から始まります。その耳に合わせて設定します。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingBands.qml:231
msgctxt "@item a band's ceiling that holds nothing back"
msgid "no limit"
msgstr "制限なし"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingBands.qml:232
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1430
#: blocks/outputdevice/ui/OutputDevicePanel.qml:199
msgctxt "@item a level, 0 is full scale"
msgid "%1 dBFS"
msgstr "%1 dBFS"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:21
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Makes quiet sounds easier to hear for one ear that hears some pitches "
"faintly. It lifts soft sound a lot and loud sound only a little, so speech "
"comes up without loud moments becoming too much."
msgstr ""
"一部の音域が聞こえにくい片方の耳のために、小さな音を聞き取りやすくします。小さな音は大きく、大きな音は少しだけ持ち上げるので、大きな音がうるさくなりすぎることなく、話し声が聞き取りやすくなります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Many people with partial hearing loss hear low voices well and high voices "
"poorly, or miss one range in the middle. Turning everything up does not help "
"much: the parts you already hear become too loud before the faint parts are "
"clear."
msgstr ""
"ある程度の難聴がある人の多くは、低い声はよく聞こえても高い声は聞こえにくかったり、中ほどの一部の音域が聞き取れなかったりします。すべてを大きくしても、あまり効果はありません。かすかな部分がはっきり聞こえるようになる前に、もともと聞こえている部分が大きくなりすぎてしまうからです。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:27
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"This block splits the sound into sixteen bands, from deep sounds at 100 Hz to"
" very high ones at 16 kHz, and gives each band its own amount of help. Hertz "
"(Hz) count how high a sound is: a man's speaking voice is round 100 to 150 "
"Hz, and the hiss of an s is above 4000 Hz, that is 4 kHz."
msgstr ""
"このブロックは、100 Hz の低い音から 16 kHz のとても高い音までを 16 "
"のバンドに分け、バンドごとに補正の量を変えます。ヘルツ（Hz）は音の高さを表す単位です。男性の話し声はおよそ 100〜150 Hz で、s の擦れる音は "
"4000 Hz、つまり 4 kHz より上にあります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:28
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"In every band the help depends on how loud the sound is at that moment. Soft "
"sound gets the most lift, loud sound the least. Each band also has a ceiling,"
" a level nothing in that band goes above."
msgstr ""
"どのバンドでも、補正の量はその瞬間の音の大きさによって変わります。小さな音ほど大きく持ち上げ、大きな音ほど持ち上げる量は少なくなります。各バンドには上限もあり、そのバンドの音がそれを超えることはありません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:29
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"It works on one ear only. The other side of the sound passes through "
"unchanged, held back by exactly as long as the block takes, so both ears stay"
" in step. Ear, at the top of the settings, says which ear it is for, and the "
"L (blue) or R (red) on the block's tile shows it."
msgstr ""
"片方の耳にだけ働きます。もう片方の音はそのまま通りますが、このブロックの処理にかかるのとちょうど同じ時間だけ遅らせるので、左右の耳でずれは生じません。どちらの耳用かは設定の一番上の「耳」で決まり、ブロックのタイルの"
" L（青）または R（赤）で示されます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:30
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"The block holds the sound back by about six thousandths of a second, far too "
"little to notice."
msgstr "このブロックは音を約 1000 分の 6 秒遅らせますが、気づかないほどわずかです。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:31
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"When the block starts, its lift comes in gently over one second, so the first"
" sound is never a sudden jump in volume."
msgstr "ブロックが動き始めると、持ち上げは 1 秒かけて徐々に効いてくるので、最初の音で急に音量が跳ね上がることはありません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:32
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"At the very end a limiter is always at work. It keeps the sound under the "
"Output ceiling, including the peaks that fall between the digital samples."
msgstr "最後には常にリミッターが働いています。デジタルのサンプルとサンプルの間に生じるピークも含めて、音を「出力の上限」より下に保ちます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:33
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"A new block has every gain at 0 dB, so it changes nothing until you set it. "
"Set it by hand, or let it start from your audiogram, the chart from a hearing"
" test."
msgstr ""
"新しいブロックではすべてのゲインが 0 dB "
"なので、設定するまで何も変わりません。手動で設定するか、オージオグラム（聴力検査の結果の図）から始めてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:34
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Reverblabr is not a medical device. It shapes sound for listening and does "
"not replace an audiologist or a hearing aid. If your hearing has changed, "
"have it checked."
msgstr ""
"Reverblabr "
"は医療機器ではありません。聞きやすいように音を整えるものであり、聴覚の専門家や補聴器の代わりにはなりません。聞こえ方が変わったと感じたら、検査を受けてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:46
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Left or Right: the ear the block works on. The other side passes through "
"unchanged. The block's tile shows an L (blue) or an R (red) to match."
msgstr ""
"「左」または「右」: このブロックが働く耳です。もう片方はそのまま通ります。ブロックのタイルには、それに合わせて L（青）または R（赤）が表示されます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:47
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"A new block starts on the left ear. When the session already has more blocks "
"of this kind for the left ear than for the right, a new one starts on the "
"right, so the second block you add is ready for the other ear."
msgstr ""
"新しいブロックは左耳で始まります。セッションにこの種類のブロックが、右耳用より左耳用のほうが多くある場合は、新しいブロックは右耳で始まります。そのため、2"
" つ目に追加したブロックはそのままもう一方の耳に使えます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:48
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Changing it while the session runs fades across to the other side, without a "
"click. One undo puts it back. Loading a preset or putting the block back to "
"its default settings leaves it as it is, so a preset made for one ear can be "
"tried on the other."
msgstr ""
"セッションの実行中にこれを変えると、クリックノイズなしでもう一方の側へフェードで切り替わります。「元に戻す」1 "
"回で戻ります。プリセットを読み込んだりブロックをデフォルト設定に戻したりしてもこの設定は変わらないので、片方の耳用に作ったプリセットをもう一方の耳で試せます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:54
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:57
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:635
msgctxt "@option:radio a view of gain against frequency"
msgid "Gain"
msgstr "ゲイン"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:56
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Shows how much each band lifts the sound, from low pitches on the left to "
"high ones on the right. Up is more lift, in decibels (dB), from −20 dB to +60"
" dB. 0 dB leaves the sound as it is; every 6 dB more roughly doubles the "
"strength of the sound."
msgstr ""
"各バンドが音をどれだけ持ち上げるかを、左の低い音から右の高い音まで表示します。上に行くほど持ち上げが大きく、単位はデシベル（dB）で、−20 dB から "
"+60 dB までです。0 dB では音はそのままで、6 dB 増えるごとに音の強さがおよそ 2 倍になります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:57
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"The four curves are the Soft, Average and Loud gains and the Ceiling, in the "
"block's colour. The one you picked under the view choice has a handle on each"
" band: drag a handle up or down to change that band. Click a handle to see "
"the band's settings as numbers under the view."
msgstr ""
"4 "
"本のカーブは、「小さな音」「普通の音」「大きな音」のゲインと「上限」で、ブロックの色で描かれます。表示の切り替えの下で選んだカーブには、バンドごとにハンドルがあります。ハンドルを上下にドラッグすると、そのバンドが変わります。ハンドルをクリックすると、そのバンドの設定が表示の下に数値で示されます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:58
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"While the session runs, a dark line shows the lift each band is giving right "
"now, moving between the Soft and Loud curves as the sound gets quieter or "
"louder. The sound itself is drawn faintly behind it, on a scale of its own, "
"as the line under the view says: 0 dBFS at the top, −100 dBFS at the bottom. "
"The gain numbers do not apply to it."
msgstr ""
"セッションの実行中は、各バンドが今どれだけ持ち上げているかを濃い線が示し、音が小さくなったり大きくなったりするにつれて「小さな音」と「大きな音」のカーブの間を動きます。その後ろには音そのものが独自の目盛りで薄く描かれます。表示の下の行にあるとおり、上端が"
" 0 dBFS、下端が −100 dBFS です。ゲインの数値はこれには当てはまりません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:59
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"When the session has a second block of this kind for the other ear, its "
"Average curve is drawn as a faint dashed line, to compare the two ears."
msgstr ""
"セッションにもう一方の耳用の同じ種類のブロックがあるときは、両耳を比べられるように、そのブロックの「普通の音」のカーブが薄い破線で描かれます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:65
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:69
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:634
msgctxt "@option:radio a view of levels against frequency"
msgid "Levels"
msgstr "レベル"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:67
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Shows where the sound sits against this ear's hearing, from very quiet at the"
" bottom to the loudest possible at the top."
msgstr "この耳の聞こえに対して音がどこにあるかを、下のとても小さな音から上の最も大きな音まで表示します。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:68
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"The numbers are digital level, in dBFS, from −100 at the bottom to 0 at the "
"top, where digital sound is at its loudest. The thick dark line is the "
"quietest level the ear hears, from the audiogram. Levels typed in dB HL are "
"drawn 85 dB lower, a fixed figure that does not measure your sound system, "
"and the line under the view says so. The dashed line is each band's ceiling. "
"While the session runs, the grey area is the sound coming in, and the "
"coloured line the sound going out, in bands a tenth of an octave wide."
msgstr ""
"数値はデジタルのレベルで、単位は dBFS です。下端が −100、上端が 0 で、0 "
"はデジタルの音が最も大きくなるところです。太く濃い線は、オージオグラムから得た、この耳に聞こえる最も小さなレベルです。dB HL で入力したレベルは 85"
" dB "
"低く描かれます。これは決まった値で、お使いの再生環境を測ったものではなく、表示の下の行にもそう示されます。破線は各バンドの上限です。セッションの実行中は、灰色の部分が入ってくる音、色の付いた線が出ていく音で、1/10"
" オクターブ幅の帯域ごとに表示されます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:69
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"The aim is to see the sound going out rise above the dark line, where the ear"
" can hear it, and stay under the dashed one."
msgstr "出ていく音が、濃い線（これより上なら耳に聞こえます）を上回り、かつ破線を下回っている状態を目指してください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:70
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"A ceiling above 0 dBFS holds nothing back, so it has no place on this scale: "
"the words on the graph say so, and how many bands it applies to."
msgstr ""
"0 dBFS より上の上限は何も制限しないので、この目盛りには表示されません。グラフ上の文字で、その旨と、それが何個のバンドに当てはまるかが示されます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:76
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:80
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:641
msgctxt "@option:radio the gain for soft sound"
msgid "Soft"
msgstr "小さな音"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:78
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"The lift for soft sound in a band: a quiet voice, a whisper, the end of a "
"word. Soft here means 15 dB quieter than ordinary speech."
msgstr ""
"バンド内の小さな音（静かな声、ささやき、言葉の終わりなど）に対する持ち上げ量です。ここでいう小さな音とは、普通の話し声より 15 dB "
"小さい音のことです。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:79
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"This is usually the largest of the three gains, because soft sound is what a "
"weak ear misses first."
msgstr "聞こえの弱い耳がまず聞き逃すのは小さな音なので、ふつうは 3 つのゲインの中でこれが最も大きくなります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:85
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:89
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:643
msgctxt "@option:radio the gain for sound of average loudness"
msgid "Average"
msgstr "普通の音"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:87
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"The lift for sound as loud as ordinary conversation. It is the curve the view"
" starts with, and the one to set first."
msgstr "普通の会話くらいの大きさの音に対する持ち上げ量です。表示で最初に選ばれているカーブで、最初に設定するのもこのカーブです。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:93
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:97
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:645
msgctxt "@option:radio the gain for loud sound"
msgid "Loud"
msgstr "大きな音"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:95
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"The lift for loud sound in a band, 15 dB louder than ordinary speech: a "
"raised voice, a door, a loud part of music. Keep it lower than Average, so "
"loud sound does not become uncomfortable."
msgstr ""
"バンド内の大きな音（普通の話し声より 15 dB "
"大きい音。張り上げた声、ドアの音、音楽の大きな部分など）に対する持ち上げ量です。大きな音が不快にならないよう、「普通の音」より低くしておいてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:96
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Between those three levels the lift changes smoothly. Each gain can be set "
"from −30 dB to +60 dB; a negative gain turns a band down, for a range that "
"sounds too sharp."
msgstr ""
"この 3 つのレベルの間では、持ち上げ量はなめらかに変わります。各ゲインは −30 dB から +60 dB "
"まで設定できます。マイナスのゲインはそのバンドを下げるので、耳に刺さるように聞こえる音域に使えます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:102
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:106
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:647
msgctxt "@option:radio the highest level a band may put out"
msgid "Ceiling"
msgstr "上限"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:104
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"The loudest a band may become, however much it is lifted. Set it just below "
"the level where sound in that range starts to feel too loud for you."
msgstr "どれだけ持ち上げても、バンドがこれより大きくなることはありません。その音域の音がうるさく感じ始めるレベルのすぐ下に設定してください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:105
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"It reads in dBFS, the level of the band's own sound, where 0 is full scale; "
"above that it reads no limit, which is where a new block starts. On the Gain "
"view the ceiling is drawn as the most lift a loud sound may have under it."
msgstr ""
"値は dBFS（そのバンド自身の音のレベル。0 "
"がフルスケール）で示されます。それより上では「制限なし」と表示され、新しいブロックはこの状態から始まります。「ゲイン」表示では、上限は、その下で大きな音に許される最大の持ち上げ量として描かれます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:113
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Press and hold it to hear the sound without this block. Let go and the block "
"is back. Use it to judge whether a change really helps."
msgstr "押し続けている間、このブロックを通さない音が聞こえます。離すとブロックが戻ります。変更が本当に役立っているかを判断するのに使ってください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:119
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:148
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1365
msgctxt "@label how quickly the gain follows the sound"
msgid "Speed"
msgstr "速度"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:121
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid "How quickly the lift follows the sound as it gets louder or quieter."
msgstr "音が大きくなったり小さくなったりするとき、持ち上げ量がどれだけ速く追従するかです。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:124
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block, one choice of Speed"
msgid ""
"Syllabic follows speech syllable by syllable: it reacts within five "
"thousandths of a second and lets go within seven hundredths. It brings up "
"soft consonants best."
msgstr ""
"「音節単位」は話し声を音節ごとに追いかけます。1000 分の 5 秒以内に反応し、100 分の 7 秒以内に戻ります。小さな子音を最もよく持ち上げます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:125
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block, one choice of Speed"
msgid ""
"Slow follows the scene rather than each sound, letting go over a second and a"
" half. It keeps the shape of music better."
msgstr "「ゆっくり」は個々の音ではなく場面全体を追い、1.5 秒かけて戻ります。音楽の形をよりよく保ちます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:126
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block, one choice of Speed"
msgid ""
"Adaptive works slowly most of the time, and switches to the quick way when a "
"sound jumps 8 dB or more above what came before, such as a door slamming. It "
"catches the sudden sound at once and is back soon after. A new block uses "
"Adaptive."
msgstr ""
"「適応型」はふだんはゆっくり働き、ドアがバタンと閉まるときのように音が直前より 8 dB "
"以上急に大きくなると、速い動きに切り替わります。突然の音をすぐに捉え、その後すぐに元に戻ります。新しいブロックでは「適応型」が使われます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:132
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:161
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1377
msgctxt "@label a gain over every band"
msgid "Loudness"
msgstr "全体の音量"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:134
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Turns every band up or down together, from −30 dB to +30 dB, without changing"
" the shape you set. Use it to set the overall level by ear. A new block "
"starts at 0 dB."
msgstr ""
"設定した形を変えずに、すべてのバンドをまとめて −30 dB から +30 dB "
"の範囲で上げ下げします。耳で聞きながら全体のレベルを決めるのに使ってください。新しいブロックでは 0 dB です。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:140
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:169
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1391
msgctxt "@label below this level soft sound is not lifted"
msgid "Noise floor"
msgstr "ノイズフロア"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:142
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Below this level the lift fades away, a decibel less for every decibel "
"quieter. It keeps the block from bringing up the hiss of a recording or the "
"hum of a room in the pauses."
msgstr ""
"このレベルより下では持ち上げ量が減っていき、1 デシベル小さくなるごとに 1 "
"デシベルずつ少なくなります。これにより、音の途切れた間に録音のヒスノイズや部屋のハムノイズが持ち上げられるのを防ぎます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:143
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"It goes from −100 dB to −40 dB below full scale, the loudest a digital signal"
" can be, and starts at −75 dB. If you hear hiss rise in the pauses, raise it "
"a little."
msgstr ""
"範囲は、フルスケール（デジタル信号の最大の大きさ）を基準に −100 dB から −40 dB までで、最初は −75 dB "
"です。音の途切れた間にヒスノイズが大きくなるのが聞こえたら、少し上げてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:149
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:178
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1413
msgctxt "@label the most gain any band is given"
msgid "Most gain"
msgstr "最大ゲイン"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:151
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"The most lift any band is ever given, whatever the other settings ask for: "
"from 0 dB to 60 dB, and 50 dB for a new block. Lower it if a band ever gets "
"far too loud. Fit from Audiogram keeps every band under it too."
msgstr ""
"ほかの設定がどうであっても、どのバンドにもこれ以上の持ち上げは行いません。範囲は 0 dB から 60 dB までで、新しいブロックでは 50 dB "
"です。大きくなりすぎるバンドがあれば下げてください。「オージオグラムから設定」でも、すべてのバンドがこの値以下に保たれます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:152
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"It sits under Limits, which are digital limits: they work on numbers inside "
"the computer. How loud that is at your ear depends on your volume, your sound"
" card and your headphones, which Reverblabr can't know."
msgstr ""
"これは「制限」の中にあります。「制限」はデジタルの制限で、コンピュータ内部の数値に対して働きます。それが耳元でどれだけの大きさになるかは、音量やサウンドカード、ヘッドホンによって決まり、Reverblabr"
" にはわかりません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:158
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:187
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1428
msgctxt "@label the level nothing goes above"
msgid "Output ceiling"
msgstr "出力の上限"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:160
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"The limiter at the very end: nothing leaves the block louder than this. It "
"goes from −24 dBFS to −1 dBFS, where 0 dBFS is full scale, and starts at −1 "
"dBFS."
msgstr ""
"最後にあるリミッターです。これより大きな音はブロックから出ません。範囲は −24 dBFS から −1 dBFS まで（0 dBFS "
"がフルスケール）で、最初は −1 dBFS です。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:161
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"It cannot be switched off. Lower it to take sudden sounds down, especially "
"with headphones."
msgstr "オフにはできません。特にヘッドホンを使うときは、下げると突然の大きな音を抑えられます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:168
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:197
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1402
#: blocks/outputdevice/ui/OutputDeviceHelp.qml:64
#: blocks/outputdevice/ui/OutputDevicePanel.qml:179
msgctxt "@title:group the digital limits of a block"
msgid "Limits"
msgstr "制限"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:170
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Lowering a limit works at once, by dragging, with the keys or by typing. "
"Raising one takes one more step: press Raise…, or type a higher number, and "
"confirm it. The sound then rises slowly to the new limit, about 12 dB each "
"second. A preset that would raise a limit asks first as well."
msgstr ""
"制限を下げるのは、ドラッグでもキーでも数値の入力でも、すぐに反映されます。上げるときはもう 1 "
"段階必要で、「上げる…」を押すか、より大きな数値を入力してから確認します。その後、音は 1 秒に約 12 dB "
"ずつ、新しい制限までゆっくり上がります。制限を上げることになるプリセットも、同じように先に確認を求めます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:176
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:205
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1382
msgctxt "@action:button take Loudness past the line, which asks first"
msgid "Go Further…"
msgstr "さらに上げる…"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:178
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Loudness stops where the band that has come up the most reaches +10 dB. Past "
"that it takes one more step, which this button opens. It shows at the stop."
msgstr ""
"「全体の音量」は、最も持ち上げられたバンドが +10 dB に達したところで止まります。それを超えるにはもう 1 "
"段階必要で、このボタンでそれを開きます。ボタンは止まった位置に表示されます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:184
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:213
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1610
msgctxt "@action:button take the other ear's block's band settings"
msgid "Copy from the Other Ear"
msgstr "もう一方の耳からコピー"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:186
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Takes every band's settings from the session's other Hearing Compensation 16 "
"block, the one for the other ear, as a starting point. The button can only be"
" pressed when there is such a block. Its limits come too, and a copy that "
"would raise one asks first. One undo takes the copy back."
msgstr ""
"セッション内のもう 1 つの「聴覚補正 "
"16」ブロック（もう一方の耳用）から、すべてのバンドの設定を出発点として取り込みます。このボタンは、そのようなブロックがあるときだけ押せます。制限もコピーされ、制限を上げることになるコピーは先に確認を求めます。「元に戻す」1"
" 回でコピーを取り消せます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:191
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:220
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1451
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1478
msgctxt "@title:group the quietest levels one ear hears, at each frequency"
msgid "Audiogram"
msgstr "オージオグラム"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:193
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"An audiogram is the chart a hearing test gives you: for each pitch, the "
"quietest level the ear heard. If you have one for this ear, type it in here "
"and the block can set its bands from it. Click the heading to open it."
msgstr ""
"オージオグラムは聴力検査で渡される図で、周波数ごとに、耳が聞き取れた最も小さなレベルを示します。この耳のオージオグラムがあればここに入力してください。ブロックがそれをもとにバンドを設定できます。見出しをクリックすると開きます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:194
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"It has a line for each of the eleven pitches a hearing test usually checks, "
"from 125 Hz to 8000 Hz. On each line, choose what was found:"
msgstr ""
"聴力検査で通常調べる 125 Hz から 8000 Hz までの 11 の周波数ごとに 1 行ずつあります。各行で、検査の結果を選んでください:"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:197
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block, one choice of an "
"audiogram line"
msgid ""
"The first choice, a dash, means nothing was measured at this pitch. The block"
" works it out from the pitches either side."
msgstr "最初の選択肢（ダッシュ）は、この周波数では何も測定されなかったことを表します。ブロックは両隣の周波数から値を割り出します。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:198
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block, one choice of an "
"audiogram line"
msgid "Heard: type the quietest level heard into the box next to it."
msgstr "「聞こえた」: 聞こえた最も小さなレベルを隣の欄に入力します。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:199
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block, one choice of an "
"audiogram line"
msgid ""
"No response: nothing was heard, even at the loudest level tried. Type that "
"level into the box."
msgstr "「反応なし」: 試した最大のレベルでも何も聞こえなかったことを表します。そのレベルを欄に入力します。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:202
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"The number boxes take levels from −140 to 140. The levels you type are kept "
"with the block. They draw the dark line of the Levels view, and set the bands"
" when you press Fit from Audiogram."
msgstr ""
"数値欄には −140 から 140 "
"までのレベルを入力できます。入力したレベルはブロックに保存されます。これらは「レベル」表示の濃い線になり、「オージオグラムから設定」を押すとバンドの設定に使われます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:208
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:237
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1460
msgctxt "@label what the audiogram's levels are measured in"
msgid "Measured in"
msgstr "測定単位"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:210
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"What the audiogram's numbers mean. dB HL, decibels hearing level, is what a "
"hearing test writes on its chart: 0 is what a young ear with good hearing "
"just hears. Choose it for an audiogram from a test; a new block uses it."
msgstr ""
"オージオグラムの数値が何を表すかです。dB HL（聴力レベルのデシベル）は聴力検査の図に書かれる単位で、0 "
"は聴力のよい若い人の耳がかろうじて聞き取れる大きさです。検査で得たオージオグラムにはこれを選んでください。新しいブロックではこれが使われます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:211
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"dBFS is for levels measured as digital levels through the very headphones you"
" listen with. Such numbers mean nothing with other headphones."
msgstr ""
"dBFS は、実際に聞くときに使うそのヘッドホンを通して、デジタルのレベルとして測ったレベル用です。そうした数値は、別のヘッドホンでは意味がありません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:217
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:246
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1558
msgctxt "@option:check a 'too loud' level was measured at this frequency"
msgid "Too loud given"
msgstr "不快レベルあり"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:219
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Tick it on a line where the test also found the level at which sound becomes "
"too loud, and type that level in the box beside it. The fit then puts the "
"ceiling there 5 dB below it. Where none is given, the fit takes 100 dB HL, a "
"level most people find uncomfortable."
msgstr ""
"検査で、音がうるさすぎると感じるレベル（不快レベル）も測った行では、これにチェックを入れ、そのレベルを隣の欄に入力してください。すると設定時に、その周波数の上限がそのレベルの"
" 5 dB 下になります。指定がない場合は、ほとんどの人が不快に感じる 100 dB HL が使われます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:225
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:254
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1599
msgctxt "@action:button"
msgid "Fit from Audiogram"
msgstr "オージオグラムから設定"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:227
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Sets every band's Soft, Average and Loud gains and its Ceiling from the "
"audiogram, in one step, following a published fitting rule. One undo takes it"
" all back."
msgstr ""
"公開されている処方式に従って、オージオグラムから各バンドの「小さな音」「普通の音」「大きな音」のゲインと「上限」を一度に設定します。「元に戻す」1 "
"回ですべて元に戻ります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:228
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"The lift for ordinary speech is never more than the ear has lost at that "
"pitch, and no band gets more than Most gain, nor more than 50 dB however high"
" Most gain is."
msgstr ""
"普通の話し声に対する持ち上げ量が、その周波数で耳が失った聴力を超えることはありません。また、どのバンドも「最大ゲイン」を超えず、「最大ゲイン」をどれだけ高くしても"
" 50 dB を超えることはありません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:229
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"A band may be marked with a warning sign: where the audiogram says no "
"response, or where the ear would need more than that. More lift is unlikely "
"to help there. Frequency Lowering can move that sound to a range the ear does"
" hear."
msgstr ""
"オージオグラムが「反応なし」のバンドや、耳がそれ以上の持ち上げを必要とするバンドには、警告マークが付くことがあります。そこではさらに持ち上げても、あまり効果は期待できません。「周波数引き下げ」を使えば、その音を耳に聞こえる音域へ移せます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:230
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid "Treat the result as a starting point, and adjust by ear."
msgstr "結果は出発点と考え、耳で聞きながら調整してください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:237
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"You follow voices on television or in a video call less well than you used "
"to."
msgstr "テレビやビデオ通話の声が、以前より聞き取りにくくなったとき。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:238
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid "You can hear that someone is talking, but not make out the words."
msgstr "誰かが話しているのはわかるのに、言葉が聞き取れないとき。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:239
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"One ear hears worse than the other, and you want to help that ear on its own."
msgstr "片方の耳がもう一方より聞こえにくく、その耳だけを補いたいとき。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:240
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid "You have an audiogram and want to listen with the sound shaped to it."
msgstr "オージオグラムがあり、それに合わせて整えた音で聞きたいとき。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:247
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Be careful with loud sound. Start with the volume low, especially with "
"headphones, and raise it slowly."
msgstr "大きな音には注意してください。特にヘッドホンでは、音量を低くして始め、ゆっくり上げてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:248
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Start from your audiogram if you have one, then listen to speech you know "
"well and change one thing at a time."
msgstr "オージオグラムがあればそこから始め、聞き慣れた話し声を聞きながら、一度に 1 つずつ変えてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:249
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Without an audiogram, start with the Average curve: lift the bands where "
"voices sound dull or muffled, a few decibels at a time."
msgstr ""
"オージオグラムがない場合は、「普通の音」のカーブから始めてください。声がこもったり、ぼやけたりして聞こえるバンドを、数デシベルずつ持ち上げます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:250
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"If everything sounds too loud, turn Loudness down rather than lowering every "
"band."
msgstr "すべてが大きすぎるときは、バンドを 1 つずつ下げるのではなく「全体の音量」を下げてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:251
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"For the other ear, add a second block of this kind: it starts on the right "
"ear. Copy from the Other Ear gives it a starting point."
msgstr "もう一方の耳には、この種類のブロックをもう 1 つ追加してください。右耳で始まります。「もう一方の耳からコピー」で出発点を作れます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:252
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"Put a Frequency Lowering or Raising block before this one, so the moved sound"
" gets the lift of the range it lands in."
msgstr "「周波数引き下げ」または「周波数引き上げ」ブロックをこのブロックの前に置くと、移された音に、移った先の音域の持ち上げがかかります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation16Help.qml:253
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 16 block"
msgid ""
"When sixteen bands are not fine enough for a steep slope or a narrow dip in "
"your hearing, try Hearing Compensation 64."
msgstr "聴力の急な傾きや狭い落ち込みに対して 16 のバンドでは細かさが足りないときは、「聴覚補正 64」を試してください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Makes quiet sounds easier to hear for one ear that hears some pitches "
"faintly. It lifts soft sound a lot and loud sound only a little, so speech "
"comes up without loud moments becoming too much."
msgstr ""
"一部の音域が聞こえにくい片方の耳のために、小さな音を聞き取りやすくします。小さな音は大きく、大きな音は少しだけ持ち上げるので、大きな音がうるさくなりすぎることなく、話し声が聞き取りやすくなります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:28
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Many people with partial hearing loss hear low voices well and high voices "
"poorly, or miss one range in the middle. Turning everything up does not help "
"much: the parts you already hear become too loud before the faint parts are "
"clear."
msgstr ""
"ある程度の難聴がある人の多くは、低い声はよく聞こえても高い声は聞こえにくかったり、中ほどの一部の音域が聞き取れなかったりします。すべてを大きくしても、あまり効果はありません。かすかな部分がはっきり聞こえるようになる前に、もともと聞こえている部分が大きくなりすぎてしまうからです。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:29
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"This block splits the sound into sixty-four narrow bands, from deep sounds at"
" 100 Hz to very high ones at 16 kHz, and gives each band its own amount of "
"help. That is fine enough for a steep slope or a narrow dip in your hearing. "
"Hertz (Hz) count how high a sound is: a man's speaking voice is round 100 to "
"150 Hz, and the hiss of an s is above 4000 Hz, that is 4 kHz."
msgstr ""
"このブロックは、100 Hz の低い音から 16 kHz のとても高い音までを 64 "
"の狭いバンドに分け、バンドごとに補正の量を変えます。聴力の急な傾きや狭い落ち込みにも合わせられる細かさです。ヘルツ（Hz）は音の高さを表す単位です。男性の話し声はおよそ"
" 100〜150 Hz で、s の擦れる音は 4000 Hz、つまり 4 kHz より上にあります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:30
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"You do not set sixty-four bands one by one. You place points, up to 24 of "
"them, and the bands follow smooth curves through the points. Between two "
"points a curve never goes higher or lower than the two points themselves, so "
"a dip is as deep as you set it and no deeper. Below the lowest point and "
"above the highest, the bands take that point's settings."
msgstr ""
"64 のバンドを 1 つずつ設定する必要はありません。最大 24 個の点を置くと、バンドはそれらの点を通るなめらかなカーブに従います。2 "
"つの点の間で、カーブがその 2 "
"点より高くなったり低くなったりすることはないので、落ち込みは設定したとおりの深さになり、それ以上深くはなりません。最も低い点より下と最も高い点より上のバンドは、その点の設定になります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:31
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"In every band the help depends on how loud the sound is at that moment. Soft "
"sound gets the most lift, loud sound the least. Each band also has a ceiling,"
" a level nothing in that band goes above."
msgstr ""
"どのバンドでも、補正の量はその瞬間の音の大きさによって変わります。小さな音ほど大きく持ち上げ、大きな音ほど持ち上げる量は少なくなります。各バンドには上限もあり、そのバンドの音がそれを超えることはありません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:32
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"It works on one ear only. The other side of the sound passes through "
"unchanged, held back by exactly as long as the block takes, so both ears stay"
" in step. Ear, at the top of the settings, says which ear it is for, and the "
"L (blue) or R (red) on the block's tile shows it."
msgstr ""
"片方の耳にだけ働きます。もう片方の音はそのまま通りますが、このブロックの処理にかかるのとちょうど同じ時間だけ遅らせるので、左右の耳でずれは生じません。どちらの耳用かは設定の一番上の「耳」で決まり、ブロックのタイルの"
" L（青）または R（赤）で示されます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:33
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"The block holds the sound back by about six thousandths of a second, far too "
"little to notice."
msgstr "このブロックは音を約 1000 分の 6 秒遅らせますが、気づかないほどわずかです。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:34
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"When the block starts, its lift comes in gently over one second, so the first"
" sound is never a sudden jump in volume."
msgstr "ブロックが動き始めると、持ち上げは 1 秒かけて徐々に効いてくるので、最初の音で急に音量が跳ね上がることはありません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:35
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"At the very end a limiter is always at work. It keeps the sound under the "
"Output ceiling, including the peaks that fall between the digital samples."
msgstr "最後には常にリミッターが働いています。デジタルのサンプルとサンプルの間に生じるピークも含めて、音を「出力の上限」より下に保ちます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:36
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"A new block has six points, at 250 Hz, 500 Hz, 1 kHz, 2 kHz, 4 kHz and 8 kHz,"
" where an audiogram has its main lines. All their gains are at 0 dB, so it "
"changes nothing until you set it. Set it by hand, or let it start from your "
"audiogram, the chart from a hearing test."
msgstr ""
"新しいブロックには、オージオグラムの主な周波数にあたる 250 Hz、500 Hz、1 kHz、2 kHz、4 kHz、8 kHz の 6 "
"つの点があります。どのゲインも 0 dB なので、設定するまで何も変わりません。手動で設定するか、オージオグラム（聴力検査の結果の図）から始めてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:37
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Reverblabr is not a medical device. It shapes sound for listening and does "
"not replace an audiologist or a hearing aid. If your hearing has changed, "
"have it checked."
msgstr ""
"Reverblabr "
"は医療機器ではありません。聞きやすいように音を整えるものであり、聴覚の専門家や補聴器の代わりにはなりません。聞こえ方が変わったと感じたら、検査を受けてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:49
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Left or Right: the ear the block works on. The other side passes through "
"unchanged. The block's tile shows an L (blue) or an R (red) to match."
msgstr ""
"「左」または「右」: このブロックが働く耳です。もう片方はそのまま通ります。ブロックのタイルには、それに合わせて L（青）または R（赤）が表示されます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:50
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"A new block starts on the left ear. When the session already has more blocks "
"of this kind for the left ear than for the right, a new one starts on the "
"right, so the second block you add is ready for the other ear."
msgstr ""
"新しいブロックは左耳で始まります。セッションにこの種類のブロックが、右耳用より左耳用のほうが多くある場合は、新しいブロックは右耳で始まります。そのため、2"
" つ目に追加したブロックはそのままもう一方の耳に使えます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:51
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Changing it while the session runs fades across to the other side, without a "
"click. One undo puts it back. Loading a preset or putting the block back to "
"its default settings leaves it as it is, so a preset made for one ear can be "
"tried on the other."
msgstr ""
"セッションの実行中にこれを変えると、クリックノイズなしでもう一方の側へフェードで切り替わります。「元に戻す」1 "
"回で戻ります。プリセットを読み込んだりブロックをデフォルト設定に戻したりしてもこの設定は変わらないので、片方の耳用に作ったプリセットをもう一方の耳で試せます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:59
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Shows how much each band lifts the sound, from low pitches on the left to "
"high ones on the right. Up is more lift, in decibels (dB), from −20 dB to +60"
" dB. 0 dB leaves the sound as it is; every 6 dB more roughly doubles the "
"strength of the sound."
msgstr ""
"各バンドが音をどれだけ持ち上げるかを、左の低い音から右の高い音まで表示します。上に行くほど持ち上げが大きく、単位はデシベル（dB）で、−20 dB から "
"+60 dB までです。0 dB では音はそのままで、6 dB 増えるごとに音の強さがおよそ 2 倍になります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:60
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"The four curves are the Soft, Average and Loud gains and the Ceiling, in the "
"block's colour. The one you picked under the view choice has a handle on each"
" point. Drag a handle up or down to change that curve at the point, or "
"sideways to move the point to another pitch. Click a handle to see the "
"point's settings as numbers under the view."
msgstr ""
"4 "
"本のカーブは、「小さな音」「普通の音」「大きな音」のゲインと「上限」で、ブロックの色で描かれます。表示の切り替えの下で選んだカーブには、点ごとにハンドルがあります。ハンドルを上下にドラッグするとその点でのカーブが変わり、左右にドラッグすると点が別の周波数に移ります。ハンドルをクリックすると、その点の設定が表示の下に数値で示されます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:61
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Double-click an empty spot to add a point there. It is placed on the curves "
"as they are, so nothing changes until you move it."
msgstr "何もないところをダブルクリックすると、そこに点を追加できます。点は今のカーブの上に置かれるので、動かすまで何も変わりません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:62
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"While the session runs, a dark line shows the lift each band is giving right "
"now, moving between the Soft and Loud curves as the sound gets quieter or "
"louder. The sound itself is drawn faintly behind it, on a scale of its own, "
"as the line under the view says: 0 dBFS at the top, −100 dBFS at the bottom. "
"The gain numbers do not apply to it."
msgstr ""
"セッションの実行中は、各バンドが今どれだけ持ち上げているかを濃い線が示し、音が小さくなったり大きくなったりするにつれて「小さな音」と「大きな音」のカーブの間を動きます。その後ろには音そのものが独自の目盛りで薄く描かれます。表示の下の行にあるとおり、上端が"
" 0 dBFS、下端が −100 dBFS です。ゲインの数値はこれには当てはまりません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:63
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"When the session has a second block of this kind for the other ear, its "
"Average curve is drawn as a faint dashed line, to compare the two ears."
msgstr ""
"セッションにもう一方の耳用の同じ種類のブロックがあるときは、両耳を比べられるように、そのブロックの「普通の音」のカーブが薄い破線で描かれます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:71
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Shows where the sound sits against this ear's hearing, from very quiet at the"
" bottom to the loudest possible at the top."
msgstr "この耳の聞こえに対して音がどこにあるかを、下のとても小さな音から上の最も大きな音まで表示します。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:72
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"The numbers are digital level, in dBFS, from −100 at the bottom to 0 at the "
"top, where digital sound is at its loudest. The thick dark line is the "
"quietest level the ear hears, from the audiogram. Levels typed in dB HL are "
"drawn 85 dB lower, a fixed figure that does not measure your sound system, "
"and the line under the view says so. The dashed line is each band's ceiling. "
"While the session runs, the grey area is the sound coming in, and the "
"coloured line the sound going out, in bands a tenth of an octave wide."
msgstr ""
"数値はデジタルのレベルで、単位は dBFS です。下端が −100、上端が 0 で、0 "
"はデジタルの音が最も大きくなるところです。太く濃い線は、オージオグラムから得た、この耳に聞こえる最も小さなレベルです。dB HL で入力したレベルは 85"
" dB "
"低く描かれます。これは決まった値で、お使いの再生環境を測ったものではなく、表示の下の行にもそう示されます。破線は各バンドの上限です。セッションの実行中は、灰色の部分が入ってくる音、色の付いた線が出ていく音で、1/10"
" オクターブ幅の帯域ごとに表示されます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:73
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"The aim is to see the sound going out rise above the dark line, where the ear"
" can hear it, and stay under the dashed one."
msgstr "出ていく音が、濃い線（これより上なら耳に聞こえます）を上回り、かつ破線を下回っている状態を目指してください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:74
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"A ceiling above 0 dBFS holds nothing back, so it has no place on this scale: "
"the words on the graph say so, and how many bands it applies to."
msgstr ""
"0 dBFS より上の上限は何も制限しないので、この目盛りには表示されません。グラフ上の文字で、その旨と、それが何個のバンドに当てはまるかが示されます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:82
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"The lift for soft sound at a point: a quiet voice, a whisper, the end of a "
"word. Soft here means 15 dB quieter than ordinary speech."
msgstr ""
"その点での小さな音（静かな声、ささやき、言葉の終わりなど）に対する持ち上げ量です。ここでいう小さな音とは、普通の話し声より 15 dB "
"小さい音のことです。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:83
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"This is usually the largest of the three gains, because soft sound is what a "
"weak ear misses first."
msgstr "聞こえの弱い耳がまず聞き逃すのは小さな音なので、ふつうは 3 つのゲインの中でこれが最も大きくなります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:91
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"The lift for sound as loud as ordinary conversation. It is the curve the view"
" starts with, and the one to set first."
msgstr "普通の会話くらいの大きさの音に対する持ち上げ量です。表示で最初に選ばれているカーブで、最初に設定するのもこのカーブです。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:99
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"The lift for loud sound at a point, 15 dB louder than ordinary speech: a "
"raised voice, a door, a loud part of music. Keep it lower than Average, so "
"loud sound does not become uncomfortable."
msgstr ""
"その点での大きな音（普通の話し声より 15 dB "
"大きい音。張り上げた声、ドアの音、音楽の大きな部分など）に対する持ち上げ量です。大きな音が不快にならないよう、「普通の音」より低くしておいてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:100
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Between those three levels the lift changes smoothly. Each gain can be set "
"from −30 dB to +60 dB; a negative gain turns a band down, for a range that "
"sounds too sharp."
msgstr ""
"この 3 つのレベルの間では、持ち上げ量はなめらかに変わります。各ゲインは −30 dB から +60 dB "
"まで設定できます。マイナスのゲインはそのバンドを下げるので、耳に刺さるように聞こえる音域に使えます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:108
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"The loudest the bands near a point may become, however much they are lifted. "
"Set it just below the level where sound in that range starts to feel too loud"
" for you."
msgstr ""
"どれだけ持ち上げても、点の近くのバンドがこれより大きくなることはありません。その音域の音がうるさく感じ始めるレベルのすぐ下に設定してください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:109
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"It reads in dBFS, the level of the band's own sound, where 0 is full scale; "
"above that it reads no limit, which is where a new block starts. On the Gain "
"view the ceiling is drawn as the most lift a loud sound may have under it."
msgstr ""
"値は dBFS（そのバンド自身の音のレベル。0 "
"がフルスケール）で示されます。それより上では「制限なし」と表示され、新しいブロックはこの状態から始まります。「ゲイン」表示では、上限は、その下で大きな音に許される最大の持ち上げ量として描かれます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:117
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Press and hold it to hear the sound without this block. Let go and the block "
"is back. Use it to judge whether a change really helps."
msgstr "押し続けている間、このブロックを通さない音が聞こえます。離すとブロックが戻ります。変更が本当に役立っているかを判断するのに使ってください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:123
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:655
msgctxt "@label where a control point is"
msgid "Frequency"
msgstr "周波数"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:125
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Where the chosen point is, from 100 Hz to 16 kHz. It is shown with the "
"point's Soft, Average, Loud and Ceiling when you click its handle. Move its "
"slider, or drag the handle sideways."
msgstr ""
"選んだ点の位置で、100 Hz から 16 kHz "
"までです。ハンドルをクリックすると、その点の「小さな音」「普通の音」「大きな音」「上限」と一緒に表示されます。スライダーを動かすか、ハンドルを左右にドラッグしてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:131
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1119
msgctxt "@action:button put a new control point on the curves"
msgid "Add Point"
msgstr "点を追加"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:133
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Puts a new point in the middle of the widest gap between the points, on the "
"curves as they are, so the sound stays as it was until you move it. The point"
" is chosen, ready to set. A double click on an empty spot of the view does "
"the same at that spot, and one undo takes either back."
msgstr ""
"点どうしの間隔が最も広いところの真ん中に、今のカーブの上に新しい点を置くので、動かすまで音は変わりません。追加した点は選択された状態になり、すぐに設定できます。表示の何もないところをダブルクリックしても、その位置で同じことができます。どちらも「元に戻す」1"
" 回で取り消せます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:134
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"A block holds 24 points. With all of them in use the button is greyed out "
"until you remove one."
msgstr "1 つのブロックに置ける点は 24 個までです。すべて使っているときは、どれかを削除するまでボタンは灰色になり、押せません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:140
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1136
msgctxt "@action:button take a control point out of the curves"
msgid "Remove Point"
msgstr "点を削除"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:142
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Takes the chosen point away. The curves then run straight on between the "
"points either side of it."
msgstr "選んだ点を取り除きます。カーブは、その両隣の点の間をそのままつなぐようになります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:150
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid "How quickly the lift follows the sound as it gets louder or quieter."
msgstr "音が大きくなったり小さくなったりするとき、持ち上げ量がどれだけ速く追従するかです。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:153
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block, one choice of Speed"
msgid ""
"Syllabic follows speech syllable by syllable: it reacts within five "
"thousandths of a second and lets go within seven hundredths. It brings up "
"soft consonants best."
msgstr ""
"「音節単位」は話し声を音節ごとに追いかけます。1000 分の 5 秒以内に反応し、100 分の 7 秒以内に戻ります。小さな子音を最もよく持ち上げます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:154
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block, one choice of Speed"
msgid ""
"Slow follows the scene rather than each sound, letting go over a second and a"
" half. It keeps the shape of music better."
msgstr "「ゆっくり」は個々の音ではなく場面全体を追い、1.5 秒かけて戻ります。音楽の形をよりよく保ちます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:155
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block, one choice of Speed"
msgid ""
"Adaptive works slowly most of the time, and switches to the quick way when a "
"sound jumps 8 dB or more above what came before, such as a door slamming. It "
"catches the sudden sound at once and is back soon after. A new block uses "
"Adaptive."
msgstr ""
"「適応型」はふだんはゆっくり働き、ドアがバタンと閉まるときのように音が直前より 8 dB "
"以上急に大きくなると、速い動きに切り替わります。突然の音をすぐに捉え、その後すぐに元に戻ります。新しいブロックでは「適応型」が使われます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:163
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Turns every band up or down together, from −30 dB to +30 dB, without changing"
" the shape you set. Use it to set the overall level by ear. A new block "
"starts at 0 dB."
msgstr ""
"設定した形を変えずに、すべてのバンドをまとめて −30 dB から +30 dB "
"の範囲で上げ下げします。耳で聞きながら全体のレベルを決めるのに使ってください。新しいブロックでは 0 dB です。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:171
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Below this level the lift fades away, a decibel less for every decibel "
"quieter. It keeps the block from bringing up the hiss of a recording or the "
"hum of a room in the pauses."
msgstr ""
"このレベルより下では持ち上げ量が減っていき、1 デシベル小さくなるごとに 1 "
"デシベルずつ少なくなります。これにより、音の途切れた間に録音のヒスノイズや部屋のハムノイズが持ち上げられるのを防ぎます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:172
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"It goes from −100 dB to −40 dB below full scale, the loudest a digital signal"
" can be, and starts at −75 dB. If you hear hiss rise in the pauses, raise it "
"a little."
msgstr ""
"範囲は、フルスケール（デジタル信号の最大の大きさ）を基準に −100 dB から −40 dB までで、最初は −75 dB "
"です。音の途切れた間にヒスノイズが大きくなるのが聞こえたら、少し上げてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:180
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"The most lift any band is ever given, whatever the other settings ask for: "
"from 0 dB to 60 dB, and 50 dB for a new block. Lower it if a band ever gets "
"far too loud. Fit from Audiogram keeps every band under it too."
msgstr ""
"ほかの設定がどうであっても、どのバンドにもこれ以上の持ち上げは行いません。範囲は 0 dB から 60 dB までで、新しいブロックでは 50 dB "
"です。大きくなりすぎるバンドがあれば下げてください。「オージオグラムから設定」でも、すべてのバンドがこの値以下に保たれます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:181
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"It sits under Limits, which are digital limits: they work on numbers inside "
"the computer. How loud that is at your ear depends on your volume, your sound"
" card and your headphones, which Reverblabr can't know."
msgstr ""
"これは「制限」の中にあります。「制限」はデジタルの制限で、コンピュータ内部の数値に対して働きます。それが耳元でどれだけの大きさになるかは、音量やサウンドカード、ヘッドホンによって決まり、Reverblabr"
" にはわかりません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:189
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"The limiter at the very end: nothing leaves the block louder than this. It "
"goes from −24 dBFS to −1 dBFS, where 0 dBFS is full scale, and starts at −1 "
"dBFS."
msgstr ""
"最後にあるリミッターです。これより大きな音はブロックから出ません。範囲は −24 dBFS から −1 dBFS まで（0 dBFS "
"がフルスケール）で、最初は −1 dBFS です。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:190
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"It cannot be switched off. Lower it to take sudden sounds down, especially "
"with headphones."
msgstr "オフにはできません。特にヘッドホンを使うときは、下げると突然の大きな音を抑えられます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:199
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Lowering a limit works at once, by dragging, with the keys or by typing. "
"Raising one takes one more step: press Raise…, or type a higher number, and "
"confirm it. The sound then rises slowly to the new limit, about 12 dB each "
"second. A preset that would raise a limit asks first as well."
msgstr ""
"制限を下げるのは、ドラッグでもキーでも数値の入力でも、すぐに反映されます。上げるときはもう 1 "
"段階必要で、「上げる…」を押すか、より大きな数値を入力してから確認します。その後、音は 1 秒に約 12 dB "
"ずつ、新しい制限までゆっくり上がります。制限を上げることになるプリセットも、同じように先に確認を求めます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:207
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Loudness stops where the band that has come up the most reaches +10 dB. Past "
"that it takes one more step, which this button opens. It shows at the stop."
msgstr ""
"「全体の音量」は、最も持ち上げられたバンドが +10 dB に達したところで止まります。それを超えるにはもう 1 "
"段階必要で、このボタンでそれを開きます。ボタンは止まった位置に表示されます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:215
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Takes every point from the session's other Hearing Compensation 64 block, the"
" one for the other ear, as a starting point. The button can only be pressed "
"when there is such a block. Its limits come too, and a copy that would raise "
"one asks first. One undo takes the copy back."
msgstr ""
"セッション内のもう 1 つの「聴覚補正 "
"64」ブロック（もう一方の耳用）から、すべての点を出発点として取り込みます。このボタンは、そのようなブロックがあるときだけ押せます。制限もコピーされ、制限を上げることになるコピーは先に確認を求めます。「元に戻す」1"
" 回でコピーを取り消せます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:222
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"An audiogram is the chart a hearing test gives you: for each pitch, the "
"quietest level the ear heard. If you have one for this ear, type it in here "
"and the block can set its bands from it. Click the heading to open it."
msgstr ""
"オージオグラムは聴力検査で渡される図で、周波数ごとに、耳が聞き取れた最も小さなレベルを示します。この耳のオージオグラムがあればここに入力してください。ブロックがそれをもとにバンドを設定できます。見出しをクリックすると開きます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:223
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"It has a line for each of the eleven pitches a hearing test usually checks, "
"from 125 Hz to 8000 Hz. On each line, choose what was found:"
msgstr ""
"聴力検査で通常調べる 125 Hz から 8000 Hz までの 11 の周波数ごとに 1 行ずつあります。各行で、検査の結果を選んでください:"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:226
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block, one choice of an "
"audiogram line"
msgid ""
"The first choice, a dash, means nothing was measured at this pitch. The block"
" works it out from the pitches either side."
msgstr "最初の選択肢（ダッシュ）は、この周波数では何も測定されなかったことを表します。ブロックは両隣の周波数から値を割り出します。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:227
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block, one choice of an "
"audiogram line"
msgid "Heard: type the quietest level heard into the box next to it."
msgstr "「聞こえた」: 聞こえた最も小さなレベルを隣の欄に入力します。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:228
msgctxt ""
"@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block, one choice of an "
"audiogram line"
msgid ""
"No response: nothing was heard, even at the loudest level tried. Type that "
"level into the box."
msgstr "「反応なし」: 試した最大のレベルでも何も聞こえなかったことを表します。そのレベルを欄に入力します。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:231
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"The number boxes take levels from −140 to 140. The levels you type are kept "
"with the block. They draw the dark line of the Levels view, and set the bands"
" when you press Fit from Audiogram."
msgstr ""
"数値欄には −140 から 140 "
"までのレベルを入力できます。入力したレベルはブロックに保存されます。これらは「レベル」表示の濃い線になり、「オージオグラムから設定」を押すとバンドの設定に使われます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:239
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"What the audiogram's numbers mean. dB HL, decibels hearing level, is what a "
"hearing test writes on its chart: 0 is what a young ear with good hearing "
"just hears. Choose it for an audiogram from a test; a new block uses it."
msgstr ""
"オージオグラムの数値が何を表すかです。dB HL（聴力レベルのデシベル）は聴力検査の図に書かれる単位で、0 "
"は聴力のよい若い人の耳がかろうじて聞き取れる大きさです。検査で得たオージオグラムにはこれを選んでください。新しいブロックではこれが使われます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:240
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"dBFS is for levels measured as digital levels through the very headphones you"
" listen with. Such numbers mean nothing with other headphones."
msgstr ""
"dBFS は、実際に聞くときに使うそのヘッドホンを通して、デジタルのレベルとして測ったレベル用です。そうした数値は、別のヘッドホンでは意味がありません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:248
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Tick it on a line where the test also found the level at which sound becomes "
"too loud, and type that level in the box beside it. The fit then puts the "
"ceiling there 5 dB below it. Where none is given, the fit takes 100 dB HL, a "
"level most people find uncomfortable."
msgstr ""
"検査で、音がうるさすぎると感じるレベル（不快レベル）も測った行では、これにチェックを入れ、そのレベルを隣の欄に入力してください。すると設定時に、その周波数の上限がそのレベルの"
" 5 dB 下になります。指定がない場合は、ほとんどの人が不快に感じる 100 dB HL が使われます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:256
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Sets the points from the audiogram, in one step, following a published "
"fitting rule. It places a point at each pitch the audiogram has a level for, "
"sets its Soft, Average and Loud gains and its Ceiling, and takes away every "
"other point. One undo takes it all back."
msgstr ""
"公開されている処方式に従って、オージオグラムから点を一度に設定します。オージオグラムにレベルがある周波数ごとに点を置き、その「小さな音」「普通の音」「大きな音」のゲインと「上限」を設定して、ほかの点はすべて取り除きます。「元に戻す」1"
" 回ですべて元に戻ります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:257
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"The lift for ordinary speech is never more than the ear has lost at that "
"pitch, and no point gets more than Most gain, nor more than 50 dB however "
"high Most gain is."
msgstr ""
"普通の話し声に対する持ち上げ量が、その周波数で耳が失った聴力を超えることはありません。また、どの点も「最大ゲイン」を超えず、「最大ゲイン」をどれだけ高くしても"
" 50 dB を超えることはありません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:258
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"A point may be marked with a warning sign: where the audiogram says no "
"response, or where the ear would need more than that. More lift is unlikely "
"to help there. Frequency Lowering can move that sound to a range the ear does"
" hear."
msgstr ""
"オージオグラムが「反応なし」の点や、耳がそれ以上の持ち上げを必要とする点には、警告マークが付くことがあります。そこではさらに持ち上げても、あまり効果は期待できません。「周波数引き下げ」を使えば、その音を耳に聞こえる音域へ移せます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:259
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid "Treat the result as a starting point, and adjust by ear."
msgstr "結果は出発点と考え、耳で聞きながら調整してください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:266
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"You follow voices on television or in a video call less well than you used "
"to."
msgstr "テレビやビデオ通話の声が、以前より聞き取りにくくなったとき。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:267
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid "You can hear that someone is talking, but not make out the words."
msgstr "誰かが話しているのはわかるのに、言葉が聞き取れないとき。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:268
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"One ear hears worse than the other, and you want to help that ear on its own."
msgstr "片方の耳がもう一方より聞こえにくく、その耳だけを補いたいとき。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:269
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Your hearing drops steeply from one pitch to the next, or has a narrow dip, "
"that sixteen bands cannot follow."
msgstr "聴力が周波数によって急に落ち込んでいたり、狭い範囲だけ落ち込んでいたりして、16 のバンドでは追いきれないとき。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:270
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid "You have an audiogram and want to listen with the sound shaped to it."
msgstr "オージオグラムがあり、それに合わせて整えた音で聞きたいとき。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:277
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Be careful with loud sound. Start with the volume low, especially with "
"headphones, and raise it slowly."
msgstr "大きな音には注意してください。特にヘッドホンでは、音量を低くして始め、ゆっくり上げてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:278
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Start from your audiogram if you have one, then listen to speech you know "
"well and change one thing at a time."
msgstr "オージオグラムがあればそこから始め、聞き慣れた話し声を聞きながら、一度に 1 つずつ変えてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:279
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Without an audiogram, start with the Average curve: lift the bands where "
"voices sound dull or muffled, a few decibels at a time."
msgstr ""
"オージオグラムがない場合は、「普通の音」のカーブから始めてください。声がこもったり、ぼやけたりして聞こえるバンドを、数デシベルずつ持ち上げます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:280
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"If everything sounds too loud, turn Loudness down rather than lowering every "
"band."
msgstr "すべてが大きすぎるときは、バンドを 1 つずつ下げるのではなく「全体の音量」を下げてください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:281
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"For the other ear, add a second block of this kind: it starts on the right "
"ear. Copy from the Other Ear gives it a starting point."
msgstr "もう一方の耳には、この種類のブロックをもう 1 つ追加してください。右耳で始まります。「もう一方の耳からコピー」で出発点を作れます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:282
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Put a Frequency Lowering or Raising block before this one, so the moved sound"
" gets the lift of the range it lands in."
msgstr "「周波数引き下げ」または「周波数引き上げ」ブロックをこのブロックの前に置くと、移された音に、移った先の音域の持ち上げがかかります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:283
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"Use few points. A point at each pitch of your audiogram is usually enough; "
"add one only where you hear that the sound needs it."
msgstr "点は少なめにしてください。ふつうはオージオグラムの周波数ごとに 1 つあれば十分です。聞いてみて必要だと感じたところにだけ追加してください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensation64Help.qml:284
msgctxt "@info help page of the Hearing Compensation 64 block"
msgid ""
"If your hearing changes gently from low to high, Hearing Compensation 16 is "
"simpler to set by hand."
msgstr "聴力が低い音から高い音へゆるやかに変化しているなら、「聴覚補正 16」のほうが手動で設定しやすくなります。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationFace.qml:40
msgctxt "@info:tooltip a Hearing Compensation block that lifts nothing"
msgid "Flat: nothing lifted"
msgstr "フラット: 持ち上げなし"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationFace.qml:42
msgctxt ""
"@info:tooltip the most a Hearing Compensation block lifts soft sound, '+24.0 "
"dB'"
msgid "Soft sound lifted by up to %1"
msgstr "小さな音を最大 %1 持ち上げ"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationFace.qml:43
msgctxt "@item a gain in decibels"
msgid "+%1 dB"
msgstr "+%1 dB"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:108
msgctxt "@label unit of a change of level"
msgid "dB"
msgstr "dB"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:109
#: blocks/outputdevice/ui/OutputDevicePanel.qml:198
msgctxt "@label unit of a level, 0 is full scale"
msgid "dBFS"
msgstr "dBFS"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:120
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:613
#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1415
msgctxt "@item a gain in decibels"
msgid "%1 dB"
msgstr "%1 dB"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:402
msgctxt "@info under the levels view of a block, an audiogram typed in dBFS"
msgid "Dark line: the quietest level heard, from the audiogram."
msgstr "濃い線: オージオグラムから得た、聞こえる最も小さなレベル。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:404
msgctxt ""
"@info under the levels view of a block, an audiogram typed in dB HL, '85 dB'"
msgid ""
"Dark line: the quietest level heard, from the audiogram, drawn %1 dB below "
"what was typed. That is a fixed figure, not a measure of your sound system."
msgstr ""
"濃い線: オージオグラムから得た、聞こえる最も小さなレベル。入力した値より %1 dB "
"低く描かれています。これは決まった値で、お使いの再生環境を測ったものではありません。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:416
msgctxt "@info the levels view of a block, while its session is stopped"
msgid "The sound is drawn while the session runs."
msgstr "音はセッションの実行中に描かれます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:420
msgctxt ""
"@info the levels view of a block, while another block's card is analysed"
msgid "Not showing live sound: another card has it."
msgstr "リアルタイムの音は表示されていません: 別の設定パネルが使用中です。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:617
msgctxt "@item a frequency in kilohertz"
msgid "%1 kHz"
msgstr "%1 kHz"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:618
msgctxt "@item a frequency in hertz"
msgid "%1 Hz"
msgstr "%1 Hz"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:663
msgctxt "@info what a Hearing Compensation block does"
msgid ""
"Lifts soft sound for one ear, band by band, and holds loud sound under a "
"ceiling."
msgstr "片耳のために、小さな音をバンドごとに持ち上げ、大きな音は上限より下に抑えます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:765
msgctxt "@label the axis of a graph of gain"
msgid "Gain, dB"
msgstr "ゲイン（dB）"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:941
msgctxt "@label the dashed line on the levels view"
msgid "Ceiling"
msgstr "上限"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:945
msgctxt "@info no band's ceiling is on the levels view's scale"
msgid "Ceiling above 0 dBFS: no limit"
msgstr "上限が 0 dBFS より上: 制限なし"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:947
msgctxt "@info bands whose ceiling is above the levels view's scale"
msgid "Ceiling: no limit in %1 band"
msgid_plural "Ceiling: no limit in %1 bands"
msgstr[0] "上限: %1 個のバンドで制限なし"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1013
msgctxt "@info a band's handle, 'Average at 1.0 kHz: +12.0 dB'"
msgid "%1 at %2: %3"
msgstr "%2 の%1: %3"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1073
msgctxt ""
"@info under the gain view of a block, while the sound is drawn behind the "
"curves"
msgid ""
"Grey: the sound, on a scale of its own, not the gain axis: 0 dBFS at the top,"
" −100 dBFS at the bottom."
msgstr "灰色: 音（ゲインの軸ではなく独自の目盛り。上端が 0 dBFS、下端が −100 dBFS）。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1086
msgctxt "@info under the levels view of a block"
msgid ""
"Grey: sound in. Coloured line: sound out. Dashed: ceiling. Sound in bands a "
"tenth of an octave wide."
msgstr "灰色: 入ってくる音。色付きの線: 出ていく音。破線: 上限。音は 1/10 オクターブ幅の帯域ごとに表示。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1099
msgctxt "@info bands where the fit asked for more than the block may give"
msgid ""
"In the marked band more gain is unlikely to help. Frequency Lowering can move"
" the sound to where it is heard."
msgid_plural ""
"In the %1 marked bands more gain is unlikely to help. Frequency Lowering can "
"move the sound to where it is heard."
msgstr[0] "印の付いた %1 個のバンドでは、ゲインを上げても効果はあまり期待できません。「周波数引き下げ」を使えば、音を聞こえる音域へ移せます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1168
msgctxt "@info why Add Point cannot be pressed, '24 points'"
msgid "A block holds %1 points. Remove one to add another."
msgstr "1 つのブロックに置ける点は %1 個までです。追加するには、どれかを削除してください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1212
msgctxt ""
"@title a control point of a Hearing Compensation block, 'Point at 890 Hz'"
msgid "Point at %1"
msgstr "%1 の点"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1214
msgctxt "@title a band of a Hearing Compensation block, 'Band 5 at 890 Hz'"
msgid "Band %1 at %2"
msgstr "バンド %1（%2）"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1224
msgctxt "@info how a band compresses: '2.0:1 above -40 dBFS'"
msgid "Compresses %1:1 above %2 dBFS"
msgstr "%2 dBFS より上を %1:1 で圧縮"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1248
msgctxt "@label the axis across a band's input/output curve"
msgid "In, dBFS"
msgstr "入力（dBFS）"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1249
msgctxt "@label the axis up a band's input/output curve"
msgid "Out, dBFS"
msgstr "出力（dBFS）"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1383
msgctxt "@info said at the end of a slider"
msgid "Loudness stops here. To go on, use Go Further."
msgstr "「全体の音量」はここで止まります。さらに上げるには「さらに上げる」を使ってください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1384
msgctxt "@info the question over a number, 'Loudness is +10 dB'"
msgid "Loudness is %1. Take it to:"
msgstr "「全体の音量」は現在 %1 です。新しい値:"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1403
#: blocks/outputdevice/ui/OutputDevicePanel.qml:180
msgctxt "@info what the limits are not"
msgid "Digital, not at your ear"
msgstr "耳元の音量ではなくデジタルの値"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1416
msgctxt "@info said at the end of a slider"
msgid "Most gain stops here. To raise it, use Raise."
msgstr "「最大ゲイン」はここで止まります。さらに上げるには「上げる」を使ってください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1417
msgctxt "@info the question over a number"
msgid "Most gain is %1 dB. Raise it to:"
msgstr "「最大ゲイン」は現在 %1 dB です。新しい値:"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1431
msgctxt "@info said at the end of a slider"
msgid "Output ceiling stops here. To raise it, use Raise."
msgstr "「出力の上限」はここで止まります。さらに上げるには「上げる」を使ってください。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1432
msgctxt "@info the question over a number"
msgid "Output ceiling is %1 dBFS. Raise it to:"
msgstr "「出力の上限」は現在 %1 dBFS です。新しい値:"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1516
msgctxt ""
"@label:listbox what one ear heard at a frequency of an audiogram, '1 kHz, "
"left ear'"
msgid "Audiogram at %1, %2"
msgstr "%1、%2のオージオグラム"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1541
msgctxt ""
"@label:spinbox the quietest level one ear heard at a frequency, '1 kHz, left "
"ear'"
msgid "Heard at, %1, %2"
msgstr "%1、%2で聞こえたレベル"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1560
msgctxt ""
"@option:check a 'too loud' level was measured for one ear at a frequency, '1 "
"kHz, left ear'"
msgid "Too loud given, %1, %2"
msgstr "%1、%2の不快レベルあり"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1591
msgctxt ""
"@label:spinbox the level at which sound becomes too loud for one ear, '1 kHz,"
" left ear'"
msgid "Too loud at, %1, %2"
msgstr "%1、%2の不快レベル"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1619
msgctxt "@title:window"
msgid "Copy from the Other Ear"
msgstr "もう一方の耳からコピー"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1620
msgctxt "@info"
msgid ""
"The other ear's limits are higher than this ear's. The copy raises them."
msgstr "もう一方の耳の制限はこの耳より高くなっています。コピーすると制限が引き上げられます。"

#: blocks/hearingcompensation/ui/HearingCompensationPanel.qml:1624
msgctxt "@action:button copy, which raises a limit"
msgid "Raise and Copy"
msgstr "制限を上げてコピー"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:18
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"Brings in the sound of a microphone, an audio interface or anything else the "
"computer can record from."
msgstr "マイク、オーディオインターフェースなど、コンピュータで録音できるあらゆるものの音を取り込みます。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"Choose a device, and the block starts a lane with what it hears. Put the "
"blocks that clean up or change the sound after it."
msgstr "デバイスを選ぶと、ブロックはそのデバイスが拾う音でレーンを始めます。音をきれいにしたり変えたりするブロックは、この後に置いてください。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"A microphone with one channel is heard on both sides, left and right, at the "
"level it was recorded at. A stereo device keeps its two sides. A device with "
"more channels is folded into two."
msgstr ""
"1 "
"チャンネルのマイクの音は、録音されたときのレベルのまま左右両方から聞こえます。ステレオのデバイスは左右をそのまま保ちます。それより多くのチャンネルを持つデバイスは、2"
" チャンネルにまとめられます。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"The block has no volume of its own. How loud the device records is set in the"
" system's sound settings, where every program sees the same level."
msgstr ""
"このブロック自体には音量の設定はありません。デバイスの録音レベルはシステムのサウンド設定で決まり、そこではすべてのプログラムに同じレベルが適用されます。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"If the device is unplugged, the block goes quiet and a warning says so. It "
"comes back by itself when the device does."
msgstr "デバイスを取り外すと、ブロックは無音になり、その旨の警告が表示されます。デバイスが戻れば、自動的に元に戻ります。"

#. i18n: A2DP and HSP/HFP are the names of a wireless headset's profiles, the
#. same in every language.
#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:28
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"A wireless headset only has a microphone in its headset profile (HSP/HFP). "
"The system usually switches to it by itself when something records from the "
"headset. If the headset stays on its playback profile (A2DP), the block hears"
" nothing, and after a few seconds a message says so. Switch the profile in "
"the system's sound settings."
msgstr ""
"ワイヤレスヘッドセットのマイクは、ヘッドセットプロファイル（HSP/HFP）でしか使えません。ヘッドセットから録音しようとすると、ふつうはシステムが自動的にこのプロファイルに切り替えます。ヘッドセットが再生用のプロファイル（A2DP）のままだとブロックには何も聞こえず、数秒後にその旨のメッセージが表示されます。システムのサウンド設定でプロファイルを切り替えてください。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:41
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid "What the block records from. The list has the devices plugged in now:"
msgstr "ブロックの録音元です。一覧には、今接続されているデバイスが表示されます:"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:44
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block, a choice of Audio device"
msgid ""
"Default input: whatever your desktop records from. When you change that in "
"the system's settings, or plug in a headset it switches to, the block "
"follows. This is what a new block uses."
msgstr ""
"「デフォルトの入力」: "
"デスクトップが録音に使っているデバイスです。システムの設定でそれを変えたり、自動で切り替わるヘッドセットを接続したりすると、ブロックもそれに従います。新しいブロックではこれが使われます。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:45
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block, a choice of Audio device"
msgid ""
"A device by name: that device, whatever the desktop's choice is. Choose one "
"to keep the block on the same microphone."
msgstr "デバイス名: デスクトップでの選択に関係なく、そのデバイスを使います。ブロックを常に同じマイクにしておきたいときに選んでください。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:46
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block, a choice of Audio device"
msgid ""
"Virtual devices, at the end of the list: outputs with no hardware behind "
"them, such as the ones you make in Reverblabr, that other programs play into."
" Choose one to bring what they play into the session."
msgstr ""
"仮想デバイス（一覧の最後）: Reverblabr "
"で作るもののように、背後にハードウェアのない出力で、ほかのプログラムがそこに音を再生します。それらが再生する音をセッションに取り込みたいときに選んでください。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:49
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"A device the block was set to that is not plugged in stays in the list, "
"marked unavailable, so opening the settings never moves the block to another "
"device."
msgstr ""
"ブロックに設定されたデバイスが接続されていなくても、「利用不可」と表示されて一覧に残るので、設定を開いただけでブロックが別のデバイスに切り替わることはありません。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:56
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"Click the heading to choose which of the device's channels make the left and "
"the right side. Most devices never need it."
msgstr "見出しをクリックすると、デバイスのどのチャンネルを左右に使うかを選べます。ほとんどのデバイスでは必要ありません。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:65
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"Which of the device's channels the left side and the right side of the lane "
"come from. The lists show the channels by the names the device gives them, "
"such as FL and FR for front left and front right, or AUX0, AUX1 and so on."
msgstr ""
"レーンの左右それぞれが、デバイスのどのチャンネルから来るかです。一覧には、デバイスが付けた名前でチャンネルが表示されます。たとえば前方左と前方右を表す "
"FL と FR、あるいは AUX0、AUX1 などです。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:66
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"Default, what a new block uses, leaves it to the block, as described above. A"
" channel you choose goes to its side whole, and nowhere else: microphone 3 of"
" an audio interface on the left, for example, and microphone 4 on the right."
msgstr ""
"「デフォルト」（新しいブロックの設定）では、上で説明したとおりブロックに任せます。選んだチャンネルは、丸ごとその側にだけ送られます。たとえば、オーディオインターフェースのマイク"
" 3 を左に、マイク 4 を右に、といった具合です。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:67
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"Once you choose a channel for one side, the other side is silent until you "
"choose one for it too."
msgstr "片側のチャンネルを選ぶと、もう片側にもチャンネルを選ぶまで、そちらは無音になります。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:74
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"You want to record your voice, or send it through blocks that make it "
"clearer, before it reaches a call or a stream."
msgstr "自分の声を録音したいとき、または通話や配信に届く前に、声を聞き取りやすくするブロックに通したいとき。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:75
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"You have an audio interface with several inputs and want two particular ones."
msgstr "複数の入力があるオーディオインターフェースで、特定の 2 つを使いたいとき。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:76
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"Other programs play into a virtual output, and you want that sound in the "
"session."
msgstr "ほかのプログラムが仮想出力に再生している音を、セッションに取り込みたいとき。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:83
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"Put a Peak/RMS meter after the block and speak, to check that the sound "
"arrives and how loud it is."
msgstr "ブロックの後に「ピーク/RMS」メーターを置いて話してみると、音が届いているか、どれくらいの大きさかを確かめられます。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:84
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"If the level is too low or too high, change it in the system's sound settings"
" first, rather than with a Volume block later."
msgstr "レベルが低すぎたり高すぎたりするときは、後から「音量」ブロックで調整するのではなく、まずシステムのサウンド設定で変えてください。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDeviceHelp.qml:85
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Device block"
msgid ""
"If you send the lane to your own speakers, use headphones, or the microphone "
"hears the speakers and the sound feeds back."
msgstr "レーンを自分のスピーカーに送る場合はヘッドホンを使ってください。そうしないと、マイクがスピーカーの音を拾ってハウリングが起きます。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDevicePanel.qml:69
msgctxt "@info the chosen input is not plugged in"
msgid ""
"This input is not there at the moment. It comes back on its own when the "
"device does."
msgstr "この入力は現在ありません。デバイスが戻れば自動的に元に戻ります。"

#: blocks/inputdevice/ui/InputDevicePanel.qml:83
msgctxt ""
"@info %1 is a wireless headset; A2DP and HSP/HFP are the names of its two "
"kinds of profile"
msgid ""
"%1 is on its playback profile (A2DP), which has no microphone, so nothing is "
"being recorded. Switch it to its headset profile (HSP/HFP) in the system's "
"sound settings; the sound in the headset is of lower quality while it is."
msgstr ""
"%1 "
"はマイクのない再生用のプロファイル（A2DP）になっているため、何も録音されていません。システムのサウンド設定でヘッドセットプロファイル（HSP/HFP）に切り替えてください。その間、ヘッドセットの音質は下がります。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchControl.qml:42
msgctxt "@item the Input Switch's first input, as a letter"
msgid "A"
msgstr "A"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchControl.qml:43
msgctxt "@item the Input Switch's second input, as a letter"
msgid "B"
msgstr "B"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchControl.qml:47
msgctxt "@info the Input Switch is fading from one input to the other"
msgid "Crossfading…"
msgstr "クロスフェード中…"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchControl.qml:49
msgctxt "@info the Input Switch passes its second input"
msgid "Input B passing"
msgstr "入力 B を通過中"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchControl.qml:50
msgctxt "@info the Input Switch passes its first input"
msgid "Input A passing"
msgstr "入力 A を通過中"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:18
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"Lets one of two sources through, A or B, and fades smoothly from one to the "
"other when you switch."
msgstr "2 つの音源 A と B のうち一方を通し、切り替えるときは一方からもう一方へ滑らかにフェードします。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"The block has two inputs on its tile, A and B, and one output. Wire a source "
"into each. Only one of them is heard at a time; a new block lets A through."
msgstr ""
"このブロックのタイルには、A と B の 2 つの入力と、1 "
"つの出力があります。それぞれに音源を配線してください。一度に聞こえるのはどちらか一方だけで、新しいブロックは A を通します。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"When you switch, the block does not cut from one to the other. It fades the "
"one out while it fades the other in, over half a second, or two seconds with "
"Shift held. The two are balanced so that the sound stays as loud all the way "
"across, with no dip in the middle."
msgstr ""
"切り替えるとき、ブロックは一方からもう一方へいきなり切り替えません。0.5 秒かけて（Shift を押しながらなら 2 "
"秒かけて）一方をフェードアウトしながら、もう一方をフェードインします。2 "
"つの音量のバランスが取られているので、切り替えの間ずっと音の大きさが変わらず、途中で落ち込むこともありません。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"Switch back before a fade has finished, and it turns round where it is and "
"goes back the way it came."
msgstr "フェードが終わる前に切り替え直すと、その位置で向きを変え、来た道を戻ります。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid "The block adds no delay."
msgstr "このブロックは遅延を加えません。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:36
#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchPanel.qml:49
msgctxt ""
"@title:group the Input Switch's two inputs and the switch between them"
msgid "Which input passes"
msgstr "通過させる入力"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:38
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"The two inputs are named one above the other, and the knob of the switch "
"beside them sits next to the one that passes. The line beside them says which"
" one you hear."
msgstr ""
"2 つの入力の名前が上下に並び、その横にあるスイッチのつまみが、通過している入力の隣に来ます。その横の行には、どちらが聞こえているかが表示されます。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:39
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"Click the switch, or press Space while it has the focus, to fade over to the "
"other input in half a second. Hold Shift as you do to fade over two seconds "
"instead. While the session runs, the knob moves along with the fade."
msgstr ""
"スイッチをクリックするか、スイッチにフォーカスがある状態で Space を押すと、0.5 秒かけてもう一方の入力にフェードします。そのとき Shift "
"を押していると、2 秒かけてフェードします。セッションの実行中は、フェードに合わせてつまみが動きます。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:40
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"The block's tile has an A and a B button too: click one to fade over to it, "
"with Shift for two seconds."
msgstr "ブロックのタイルにも A と B のボタンがあります: クリックするとその入力へフェードし、Shift を押しながらなら 2 秒かけます。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:47
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"You want to go back and forth between two microphones, or between a "
"microphone and music."
msgstr "2 本のマイクの間や、マイクと音楽の間を行き来したいとき。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:48
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"You compare two versions of the same sound, such as before and after an "
"effect, and want to hear the difference at a click."
msgstr "エフェクトの前と後など、同じ音の 2 つのバージョンを比べていて、クリック 1 つで違いを聞きたいとき。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:49
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"A show needs a smooth change from one source to another, without stopping "
"either."
msgstr "番組などで、どちらの音源も止めずに、一方からもう一方へ滑らかに切り替える必要があるとき。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:56
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"Give it a global shortcut to switch without looking at the window: Input "
"Switch: play A and play B, in System Settings, under Keyboard, Shortcuts, "
"Reverblabr. They switch every Input Switch in the session the main window "
"shows."
msgstr ""
"グローバルショートカットを割り当てると、ウィンドウを見ずに切り替えられます: システム設定の「キーボード › ショートカット › "
"Reverblabr」にある「入力切替: A を再生」と「入力切替: B "
"を再生」です。これらは、メインウィンドウに表示されているセッション内のすべての「入力切替」を切り替えます。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:57
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"To switch from a script, use the command line: reverblabr-ctl switch, then "
"the session's name and A or B."
msgstr ""
"スクリプトから切り替えるには、コマンドラインを使います: reverblabr-ctl switch の後に、セッション名と A または B "
"を指定します。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:58
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid ""
"For a fair comparison of two sources, make them about as loud as each other "
"first, with a Volume block before one of them."
msgstr "2 つの音源を公平に比べるには、まず一方の前に「音量」ブロックを置いて、両者の大きさをほぼそろえてください。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchHelp.qml:59
msgctxt "@info help page of the Input Switch block"
msgid "Ctrl+Z takes a switch back, like any other change."
msgstr "他の変更と同じように、Ctrl+Z で切り替えを元に戻せます。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchPanel.qml:111
msgctxt "@action:button switch the Input Switch to its other input"
msgid "Switch to %1"
msgstr "%1 に切り替え"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchPanel.qml:119
msgctxt "@info what the Input Switch does now"
msgid "Sound from input B goes through; input A is not heard."
msgstr "入力 B の音が通ります。入力 A は聞こえません。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchPanel.qml:120
msgctxt "@info what the Input Switch does now"
msgid "Sound from input A goes through; input B is not heard."
msgstr "入力 A の音が通ります。入力 B は聞こえません。"

#: blocks/inputswitch/ui/InputSwitchPanel.qml:130
msgctxt "@info how the Input Switch switches"
msgid "Click to crossfade over half a second; with Shift, over two seconds."
msgstr "クリックすると 0.5 秒でクロスフェードします。Shift を押しながらだと 2 秒かけます。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:20
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"Puts two lanes back together as one stereo pair: the left side from one lane,"
" the right side from the other. With it, each ear can have a lane of blocks "
"of its own."
msgstr ""
"2 本のレーンを 1 つのステレオペアにまとめ直します: "
"左側は一方のレーンから、右側はもう一方のレーンから取ります。これを使うと、耳ごとに専用のブロックのレーンを持てます。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"Every lane in Reverblabr carries a stereo pair: a left side for the left ear "
"and a right side for the right ear. The blocks in the Hearing group work on "
"one ear each and pass the other side through."
msgstr ""
"Reverblabr "
"のレーンはどれも、ステレオペア（左耳用の左側と右耳用の右側）を運びます。「聴覚」グループのブロックは、それぞれ片方の耳だけに働き、もう片方はそのまま通します。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"When the two ears need quite different help, it is clearer to give each ear a"
" lane of its own. Wire the source to two lanes, put the left ear's blocks on "
"one and the right ear's on the other, and bring both lanes into Join L/R. "
"What comes out is one stereo pair again, ready for your headphones or another"
" block."
msgstr ""
"左右の耳で必要な補助が大きく違う場合は、耳ごとに専用のレーンを用意するほうがわかりやすくなります。音源を 2 "
"本のレーンに配線し、一方に左耳用のブロック、もう一方に右耳用のブロックを置いて、両方のレーンを「L/R 結合」に入れます。出てくるのは再び 1 "
"つのステレオペアで、ヘッドホンや別のブロックにそのまま送れます。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:27
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"Join L/R takes the left side of the lane on its Left input, and the right "
"side of the lane on its Right input. The other two sides, the ones each lane "
"only passed through, are left out."
msgstr ""
"「L/R 結合」は、「左」入力のレーンからは左側を、「右」入力のレーンからは右側を取ります。残りの 2 "
"つの側（各レーンがそのまま通しただけの側）は使いません。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:28
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"The blocks on the two lanes may hold the sound back by different amounts. "
"Reverblabr makes the quicker lane wait for the slower one where they meet, so"
" both ears hear the sound at the same moment. The block adds no delay of its "
"own, and the whole is only as late as the slower lane."
msgstr ""
"2 本のレーンのブロックは、それぞれ異なる時間だけ音を遅らせることがあります。Reverblabr は、2 "
"本が合流する地点で速いレーンを遅いレーンに合わせて待たせるので、両耳には同じ瞬間に音が届きます。このブロック自体は遅延を加えず、全体の遅れは遅いほうのレーンと同じです。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:29
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"A quick way to set it up: select the source and add a hearing block, which "
"starts on the left ear. Select the source again and add a second block of the"
" same kind, which starts on the right ear and gets a lane of its own. Select "
"the left one and add Join L/R, which takes it on its Left input, then wire "
"the right one into its Right input."
msgstr ""
"手早く設定する方法: 音源を選択して聴覚ブロックを追加すると、そのブロックは左耳から始まります。もう一度音源を選択して同じ種類のブロックを追加すると、2 "
"つ目は右耳から始まり、専用のレーンができます。左耳のブロックを選択して「L/R "
"結合」を追加すると、それが「左」入力につながります。続けて右耳のブロックを「右」入力に配線します。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:30
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid "The block has nothing to set."
msgstr "このブロックには設定項目がありません。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:35
msgctxt "@title a part of the Join L/R block's help page"
msgid "Its two inputs"
msgstr "2 つの入力"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:37
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"To wire a lane to an input, hold Ctrl and drag from the output connector on "
"the right edge of the lane's last block to the input connector on the left "
"edge of Join L/R. The connectors that would take the wire light up while you "
"drag."
msgstr ""
"レーンを入力に配線するには、Ctrl を押しながら、レーンの最後のブロックの右端にある出力コネクターから、「L/R "
"結合」の左端にある入力コネクターまでドラッグします。ドラッグ中は、配線を受け付けるコネクターが光ります。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:45
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"Wire the left ear's lane here. Only its left side is used, so the hearing "
"blocks on that lane should be the ones for the left ear: Ear set to Left in "
"their settings, and an L on their tile."
msgstr ""
"左耳のレーンをここに配線します。使われるのは左側だけなので、そのレーンの聴覚ブロックは左耳用にしてください: 設定の「耳」が「左」で、タイルに L "
"が表示されているものです。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:53
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"Wire the right ear's lane here. Only its right side is used, so the hearing "
"blocks on that lane should be the ones for the right ear: Ear set to Right in"
" their settings, and an R on their tile."
msgstr ""
"右耳のレーンをここに配線します。使われるのは右側だけなので、そのレーンの聴覚ブロックは右耳用にしてください: 設定の「耳」が「右」で、タイルに R "
"が表示されているものです。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:60
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"Each ear needs several blocks of its own, and one lane with all of them for "
"both ears is hard to follow."
msgstr "耳ごとに複数の専用ブロックが必要で、両耳分をすべて 1 本のレーンに並べるとわかりにくいとき。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:61
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"One ear needs a block that holds the sound back a long time, such as "
"Frequency Raising, and the other does not. On one lane, the delays of all the"
" blocks add up; on two lanes joined here, only the slower lane counts."
msgstr ""
"一方の耳には「周波数引き上げ」のように音を長く遅らせるブロックが必要で、もう一方には必要ないとき。1 "
"本のレーンではすべてのブロックの遅延が足し合わされますが、2 本のレーンをここで結合すれば、遅いほうのレーンの遅延だけで済みます。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:68
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"Name the two lanes' blocks, or look at the L and R on their tiles, so you can"
" tell at a glance which lane is for which ear."
msgstr "2 本のレーンのブロックに名前を付けるか、タイルの L と R を見れば、どのレーンがどちらの耳用かが一目でわかります。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:69
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid ""
"If one ear hears nothing changed, check that its lane goes into the right "
"input: a lane of left-ear blocks wired to Right passes on only the side it "
"did not change."
msgstr ""
"片方の耳で何も変化が聞こえない場合は、そのレーンが正しい入力につながっているか確認してください: "
"左耳用ブロックのレーンを「右」に配線すると、変更していない側だけが渡されます。"

#: blocks/joinlr/ui/JoinLrHelp.qml:70
msgctxt "@info help page of the Join L/R block"
msgid "Put a meter after Join L/R to check that both sides arrive."
msgstr "「L/R 結合」の後にメーターを置いて、左右の両方が届いているか確認してください。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterFace.qml:51
msgctxt "@label what the number on a running Limiter tile is"
msgid "reduction"
msgstr "低減"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterFace.qml:52
msgctxt "@label a Limiter's ceiling, as a true peak, on its tile"
msgid "TP ceiling"
msgstr "TP 上限"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterFace.qml:53
msgctxt "@label a Limiter's ceiling, as a sample peak, on its tile"
msgid "ceiling"
msgstr "上限"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterFace.qml:56
msgctxt ""
"@info:tooltip a Limiter's settings, 'Ceiling -1.0 dBTP, release 100 ms'"
msgid "Ceiling %1, release %2"
msgstr "上限 %1、リリース %2"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterFace.qml:68
msgctxt "@info what a Limiter tile says, 'reduction -3.2 dB'"
msgid "%1 %2"
msgstr "%1 %2"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:18
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"Keeps the sound under a level you choose, the ceiling, and never lets it "
"past. Use it at the end of a lane to stop the sound from clipping."
msgstr "音を、選んだレベル（上限）より下に保ち、決して超えさせません。レーンの最後に置いて、音のクリッピングを防ぐのに使います。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"While the sound stays below the ceiling, the Limiter leaves it exactly as it "
"is. When a loud moment would go over, it turns the sound down just enough, "
"and lets it come back up once the moment has passed."
msgstr ""
"音が上限より下にある間、「リミッター」は音にまったく手を加えません。大きな瞬間が上限を超えそうになると、必要な分だけ音を下げ、その瞬間が過ぎると元に戻します。"

#. i18n: "full scale" is the highest level digital sound can have; the sentence
#. explains it.
#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"The ceiling is counted down from full scale, the loudest a digital signal can"
" be. Sound pushed past full scale is clipped: the tops of its waves are cut "
"off, and it crackles. A limiter turns those moments down instead, which is "
"far harder to hear."
msgstr ""
"上限は、フルスケール（デジタル信号が出せる最大の大きさ）から下へ数えます。フルスケールを超えた音はクリップします。波の頂点が切り取られ、バリバリという音になります。リミッターはそうした瞬間を代わりに下げるので、ずっと気付かれにくくなります。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"It listens a little ahead, one and a half thousandths of a second, so it is "
"already turning down when a sudden peak arrives and nothing slips through. To"
" do that it holds the whole lane back by about that much, far too little to "
"hear."
msgstr ""
"1.5 "
"ミリ秒だけ先を聞いているので、急なピークが来たときにはすでに音を下げ始めていて、何もすり抜けません。そのためにレーン全体をそれくらい遅らせますが、聞いてわかるほどではありません。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:27
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"It turns both sides down together, so a loud sound on one side does not shift"
" the sound towards the other."
msgstr "左右を一緒に下げるので、片側の大きな音のせいで、音がもう片側へ寄ることはありません。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:37 blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterPanel.qml:58
msgctxt "@label:slider the level a Limiter never lets the sound past"
msgid "Ceiling"
msgstr "上限"

#. i18n: dB stands for decibels; dBTP and dBFS stay as they are, the next
#. paragraph explains them.
#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:40
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"The highest the sound may go, in decibels (dB) below full scale, from −12 dB "
"to 0 dB in tenths. A new block starts at −1 dB, which leaves a little room "
"for whatever comes after it."
msgstr ""
"音が達してよい最大のレベルで、フルスケールより下のデシベル（dB）で表し、−12 dB〜0 dB の範囲を 0.1 刻みで設定します。新しいブロックは "
"−1 dB から始まり、後に続く処理のために少し余裕を残します。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:41
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"The number is written in dBTP while Catch peaks between samples is on, and in"
" dBFS while it is off: the same scale, measured in the two ways the switch "
"describes."
msgstr ""
"数値は、「サンプル間のピークを捉える」がオンのときは dBTP、オフのときは dBFS で表示されます。どちらも同じ目盛りで、このスイッチが説明する 2 "
"つの方法で測ったものです。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:42
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"A new ceiling glides in over a fiftieth of a second, so moving the slider "
"while the sound plays makes no click."
msgstr "新しい上限は 50 分の 1 秒かけて滑らかに切り替わるので、音の再生中にスライダーを動かしてもクリック音は出ません。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:48 blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterPanel.qml:104
msgctxt "@label:slider how quickly a Limiter lets go"
msgid "Release"
msgstr "リリース"

#. i18n: ms stands for milliseconds, s for seconds.
#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:51
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"How quickly the sound comes back up after a loud moment, from 10 milliseconds"
" (ms) to 1 second. A new block uses 100 ms."
msgstr "大きな瞬間の後、音がどれだけ速く戻るかで、10 ミリ秒（ms）〜1 秒です。新しいブロックは 100 ms を使います。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:52
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"A short release brings the sound back at once, which keeps it loud but can "
"make it pump or crackle when the Limiter works often. A long release is "
"smoother, but quiet sounds right after a loud one stay turned down for a "
"while."
msgstr ""
"リリースが短いと音はすぐに戻るので大きさは保たれますが、「リミッター」が頻繁に働くと、音が波打ったりバリバリしたりすることがあります。リリースが長いと滑らかですが、大きな音の直後の小さな音が、しばらく下がったままになります。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:58 blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterPanel.qml:147
msgctxt "@option:check a Limiter detects true peaks"
msgid "Catch peaks between samples"
msgstr "サンプル間のピークを捉える"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:60
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"Digital sound is a row of measurements, called samples. The wave they "
"describe can rise higher between two of them than either of them is. A "
"player, a converter or an encoder that later rebuilds the wave can then clip,"
" although no sample went over."
msgstr ""
"デジタル音声は、サンプルと呼ばれる測定値の並びです。それらが描く波は、2 "
"つのサンプルの間で、どちらのサンプルよりも高くなることがあります。そのため、後で波を組み立て直すプレーヤー、変換器、エンコーダでは、どのサンプルも上限を超えていないのにクリップすることがあります。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:61
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"With this on, the Limiter works out where the wave goes between the samples "
"and keeps that under the ceiling too. These are called true peaks. It is on "
"for a new block; leave it on unless you need every last bit of level."
msgstr ""
"これをオンにすると、「リミッター」はサンプル間で波がどこまで上がるかを計算し、それも上限より下に保ちます。これをトゥルーピークといいます。新しいブロックではオンです。レベルを最後の一滴まで使い切る必要がない限り、オンのままにしてください。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:62
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"Switching it does not change how late the sound comes out, so you can try "
"both while the session runs."
msgstr "切り替えても音の遅れは変わらないので、セッションの実行中に両方を試せます。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:68 blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterPanel.qml:173
msgctxt "@label how much gain a Limiter is taking off now"
msgid "Gain reduction"
msgstr "ゲインリダクション"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:70
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"Not a setting but a reading: how far the Limiter is turning the sound down "
"right now, in decibels. 0.0 dB means it is doing nothing. While the session "
"is stopped, it shows a dash."
msgstr ""
"設定ではなく測定値で、「リミッター」がいま音をどれだけ下げているかをデシベルで示します。0.0 dB "
"は何もしていないことを意味します。セッションの停止中は横線が表示されます。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:71
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"The block's tile shows the same while the session runs, as a number and a "
"bar. While it is stopped, the tile shows the ceiling."
msgstr "セッションの実行中は、ブロックのタイルにも同じ値が数値とバーで表示されます。停止中は、タイルに上限が表示されます。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:78
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid "A recording or a stream must never clip, whatever happens in it."
msgstr "何が起きても、録音や配信を決してクリップさせたくないとき。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:79
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"Sudden loud sounds, such as a laugh, a cough or a door, jump out of an "
"otherwise even level."
msgstr "笑い声、せき、ドアの音のような突然の大きな音が、ほかは安定したレベルの中で飛び出すとき。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:80
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid "You have turned a source up and its loudest moments now go too high."
msgstr "音源を上げたら、最も大きな瞬間が高くなりすぎるようになったとき。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:87
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"Put the Limiter last in a lane, after everything that can make the sound "
"louder."
msgstr "「リミッター」は、音を大きくする可能性のあるものすべての後、レーンの最後に置いてください。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:88
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"Watch Gain reduction. A few decibels now and then is fine. If it hardly ever "
"reads 0.0 dB, the sound arriving is too loud: turn it down earlier in the "
"lane rather than letting the Limiter do all the work."
msgstr ""
"「ゲインリダクション」を見てください。ときどき数デシベルなら問題ありません。0.0 dB "
"になることがほとんどない場合は、届く音が大きすぎます。「リミッター」にすべてを任せず、レーンのもっと前で音を下げてください。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:89
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"For a recording or a stream, a ceiling of −1 dB with Catch peaks between "
"samples on is a safe start."
msgstr "録音や配信では、上限 −1 dB で「サンプル間のピークを捉える」をオンにするのが、安全な出発点です。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterHelp.qml:90
msgctxt "@info help page of the Limiter block"
msgid ""
"The Volume block already ends with a limiter at −1 dB. Add this block when "
"you want to choose the ceiling or see how hard it works."
msgstr ""
"「音量」ブロックの最後には、すでに −1 dB "
"のリミッターがあります。上限を自分で選びたいときや、どれだけ強く働いているかを見たいときに、このブロックを追加してください。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterPanel.qml:81
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Ceiling"
msgstr "上限"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterPanel.qml:125
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Release"
msgstr "リリース"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterPanel.qml:163
msgctxt "@info what true-peak limiting is for"
msgid ""
"A signal can rise between its samples higher than any of them. Catching those"
" peaks keeps a converter or an encoder further down from clipping."
msgstr ""
"信号はサンプルの間で、どのサンプルよりも高くなることがあります。そうしたピークを捉えると、後段の変換器やエンコーダでのクリッピングを防げます。"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterPanel.qml:182
msgctxt "@info no reading while the session is stopped"
msgid "—"
msgstr "—"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterWords.qml:34
msgctxt "@info a ceiling as a true peak, '-1.0 dBTP'"
msgid "%1 dBTP"
msgstr "%1 dBTP"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterWords.qml:35
msgctxt "@info a ceiling as a sample peak, '-1.0 dBFS'"
msgid "%1 dBFS"
msgstr "%1 dBFS"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterWords.qml:40
msgctxt "@info a level in decibels, '-1.0 dB'"
msgid "%1 dB"
msgstr "%1 dB"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterWords.qml:48
msgctxt "@info the gain taken off, '-3.2 dB'"
msgid "%1 dB"
msgstr "%1 dB"

#: blocks/limiter/ui/LimiterWords.qml:50
msgctxt "@info no gain taken off"
msgid "0.0 dB"
msgstr "0.0 dB"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerFace.qml:49
msgctxt "@info how many of the Mixer's five inputs are in use"
msgid "%1 of 5 inputs"
msgid_plural "%1 of 5 inputs"
msgstr[0] "入力 %1/5"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerFace.qml:51
msgctxt ""
"@info:tooltip the Mixer's master volume and inputs, '100 %, 3 of 5 inputs'"
msgid "Master %1 %, %2"
msgstr "マスター %1%、%2"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerFace.qml:77 blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:217
#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:181
msgctxt "@info a volume as a percentage"
msgid "%1 %"
msgstr "%1%"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerFace.qml:110 blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:55
#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:201
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Master volume"
msgstr "マスター音量"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:18
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"Brings up to five sources together into one, each with its own volume, mute, "
"solo and balance, and one master volume over them all."
msgstr "最大 5 つの音源を 1 つにまとめます。それぞれに音量、ミュート、ソロ、バランスがあり、全体に 1 つのマスター音量がかかります。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"The block has five inputs on its tile and one output. Each input has a strip "
"of its own in the settings, numbered 1 to 5 from the top, with the name of "
"what is wired into it. A strip with nothing wired in says No source and is "
"drawn faded; it costs nothing."
msgstr ""
"このブロックのタイルには 5 つの入力と 1 つの出力があります。設定では各入力に専用のチャンネルストリップがあり、上から 1〜5 "
"の番号と、配線されているものの名前が付いています。何も配線されていないストリップには「音源なし」と表示されて薄く描かれ、処理の負荷はかかりません。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"What comes out is all the strips added together, each at its own volume, then"
" turned up or down by the master."
msgstr "出力は、すべてのストリップをそれぞれの音量で足し合わせ、マスターで上げ下げしたものです。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"Every change glides rather than jumps, so nothing clicks: a slider in a "
"fiftieth of a second, a fade in half a second or two."
msgstr ""
"どの変更も急に跳ばず滑らかに移るので、クリック音は出ません。スライダーは 50 分の 1 秒、フェードは 0.5 秒か 2 秒かけて変わります。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid "The block adds no delay."
msgstr "このブロックは遅延を加えません。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:36 blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:170
msgctxt "@title:group the Mixer's five strips, one an input"
msgid "Inputs"
msgstr "入力"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:38
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid "Each strip has, from left to right:"
msgstr "各チャンネルストリップには、左から順に次のものがあります:"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:41
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block, a control of a Mixer strip"
msgid ""
"↘ 0 %: fades the input out to silence over half a second, or two seconds with"
" Shift held."
msgstr "↘ 0%: 0.5 秒（Shift を押しながらなら 2 秒）かけて、入力を無音までフェードアウトします。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:42
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block, a control of a Mixer strip"
msgid ""
"The speaker button: mutes the input, and unmutes it when pressed again. The "
"volume stays where it was."
msgstr "スピーカーボタン: 入力をミュートし、もう一度押すとミュートを解除します。音量はそのままです。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:43
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block, a control of a Mixer strip"
msgid ""
"The volume slider: from 0 % to 200 %, as a percentage of how loud the input "
"arrives. A new block starts every strip at 100 %, which leaves the input as "
"it is. The number beside it says where it is."
msgstr ""
"音量スライダー: 届いた入力の大きさに対する割合で、0%〜200% です。新しいブロックではすべてのストリップが 100% "
"から始まり、入力はそのままです。横の数値が現在の位置を示します。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:44
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block, a control of a Mixer strip"
msgid ""
"↗ 100 %: fades the input to 100 % over half a second, or two seconds with "
"Shift held."
msgstr "↗ 100%: 0.5 秒（Shift を押しながらなら 2 秒）かけて、入力を 100% までフェードします。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:45
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block, a control of a Mixer strip"
msgid ""
"Solo: while any strip is soloed, you hear only the soloed ones. Solo several "
"to hear them together. Hold Alt as you click to solo this one alone. A muted "
"strip stays silent even when soloed."
msgstr ""
"ソロ: どれかのストリップがソロのときは、ソロにしたストリップだけが聞こえます。複数をソロにすると一緒に聞けます。Alt "
"を押しながらクリックすると、そのストリップだけをソロにします。ミュートしたストリップは、ソロにしても無音のままです。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:46
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block, a control of a Mixer strip"
msgid ""
"The balance slider, between L and R: towards L turns the right side of the "
"input down, towards R the left. In the middle, where a new block starts, both"
" sides are as they arrive."
msgstr ""
"バランススライダー（L と R の間）: L に寄せると入力の右側が、R "
"に寄せると左側が小さくなります。新しいブロックの初期位置である中央では、左右とも届いたままです。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:49
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"In a narrow window a strip folds onto three lines, with the same controls."
msgstr "ウィンドウが狭いときは、ストリップが同じ操作のまま 3 行に折り返されます。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:57
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"The volume of everything together, from 0 % to 200 %. A new block starts at "
"100 %."
msgstr "すべてをまとめた音量で、0%〜200% です。新しいブロックは 100% から始まります。"

#. i18n: "full scale" is the highest level digital sound can have; the sentence
#. explains it.
#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:59
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"Several sources added together can be louder than full scale, the loudest a "
"digital signal can be, and the Mixer does not hold them back. If a meter "
"after the block reaches the red, turn the master down."
msgstr ""
"複数の音源を足し合わせると、フルスケール（デジタル信号が出せる最大の大きさ）を超えることがありますが、「ミキサー」はそれを抑えません。ブロックの後ろのメーターが赤に達したら、マスターを下げてください。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:65 blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:240
msgctxt "@title:group fading every Mixer strip at once"
msgid "Fade all"
msgstr "一括フェード"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:67 blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:255
msgctxt "@action:button fade every Mixer strip to silence"
msgid "Fade All to 0 %"
msgstr "すべて 0% へフェード"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:68 blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:265
msgctxt "@action:button fade every Mixer strip up to its full level"
msgid "Fade All to 100 %"
msgstr "すべて 100% へフェード"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:71
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"Fades every strip at once: Fade All to 0 % to silence, Fade All to 100 % to "
"full. Each takes half a second, or two seconds with Shift held. The master "
"stays where it is."
msgstr ""
"すべてのストリップを一度にフェードします。「すべて 0% へフェード」で無音に、「すべて 100% へフェード」で元の大きさにします。どちらも 0.5 "
"秒（Shift を押しながらなら 2 秒）かかります。マスターはそのままです。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:77 blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:283
#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:286
msgctxt "@title:group saved sets of the Mixer's volumes"
msgid "Scenes"
msgstr "シーン"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:79
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"A scene keeps the five strips' volumes, to bring them back later with one "
"click. There are five, A to E."
msgstr "シーンは 5 つのストリップの音量を記憶し、後でワンクリックで呼び戻せるようにします。シーンは A〜E の 5 つです。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:80
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"Save Scene, then a scene in its list, keeps the volumes as they are now. "
"Click the scene's letter to bring them back: every strip glides to its saved "
"volume over a second. A letter nobody has saved yet cannot be clicked."
msgstr ""
"「シーンを保存」を押してから一覧のシーンを選ぶと、現在の音量が記憶されます。シーンの文字をクリックすると呼び戻され、すべてのストリップが 1 "
"秒かけて保存した音量へ滑らかに移ります。まだ保存されていない文字はクリックできません。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:81
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"A scene keeps the volumes only, not the mute, the solo or the balance. Scenes"
" are saved with the session and with a preset of the block."
msgstr "シーンが記憶するのは音量だけで、ミュート、ソロ、バランスは含みません。シーンは、セッションやブロックのプリセットと一緒に保存されます。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:88
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"You stream or record several sources at once, such as a microphone, a game, "
"music and a call, and want each at the right level."
msgstr "マイク、ゲーム、音楽、通話など、複数の音源を同時に配信または録音し、それぞれを適切なレベルにしたいとき。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:89
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"A show has parts, such as an intro, talking and music, each with its own "
"balance of sources: save each as a scene."
msgstr "番組にオープニング、トーク、音楽などの部分があり、それぞれ音源のバランスが違うとき。それぞれをシーンとして保存してください。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:90
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"You need to hear one source alone for a moment, with Solo, without changing "
"any volume."
msgstr "音量を変えずに、「ソロ」で 1 つの音源だけを少しの間聞きたいとき。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:97
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"Give the blocks you wire in names of your own, so each strip says what it "
"carries: select a block on the canvas and press F2."
msgstr ""
"配線するブロックに自分で名前を付けておくと、各ストリップに何が流れているかがわかります。キャンバスでブロックを選択して F2 キーを押してください。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:98
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"Put a Peak/RMS meter after the Mixer: with several sources together, the sum "
"can reach the red even when each source alone does not."
msgstr ""
"「ミキサー」の後ろに「ピーク/RMS」メーターを置いてください。複数の音源を合わせると、どの音源も単独では赤に届かなくても、合計が赤に達することがあります。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:99
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid ""
"Turn a source down rather than the others up when you can. It leaves more "
"room before the sum gets too loud."
msgstr "できるだけ、ほかの音源を上げるのではなく、1 つの音源を下げるようにしてください。合計が大きくなりすぎるまでの余裕が増えます。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerHelp.qml:100
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mixer block"
msgid "Ctrl+Z takes back a fade or a scene in one step."
msgstr "Ctrl+Z を押すと、フェードやシーンの呼び出しを 1 回で元に戻せます。"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:189
msgctxt "@label:slider the Mixer's volume over all its inputs"
msgid "Master"
msgstr "マスター"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:256 blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:266
msgctxt "@info:tooltip"
msgid "Over half a second; with Shift, two seconds"
msgstr "0.5 秒かけて変わります。Shift を押しながらなら 2 秒です"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:307
msgctxt "@action:button bring a saved set of volumes back"
msgid "Recall scene %1"
msgstr "シーン %1 を呼び出す"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:319
msgctxt "@action:button keep the volumes as a scene"
msgid "Save Scene"
msgstr "シーンを保存"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerPanel.qml:332
msgctxt "@action:inmenu keep the volumes as one of five scenes"
msgid "Save as Scene %1"
msgstr "シーン %1 として保存"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:91
msgctxt "@info a Mixer strip nothing is wired into"
msgid "No source"
msgstr "音源なし"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:119
msgctxt "@action:button fade this Mixer strip to silence"
msgid "↘ 0 %"
msgstr "↘ 0%"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:121
msgctxt "@action:button"
msgid "Fade input %1 to 0 %"
msgstr "入力 %1 を 0% へフェード"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:122
msgctxt "@info:tooltip"
msgid "Fade to 0 % over half a second; with Shift, two seconds"
msgstr "0.5 秒かけて 0% へフェードします。Shift を押しながらなら 2 秒です"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:137
msgctxt "@action:button silence one Mixer strip"
msgid "Mute input %1"
msgstr "入力 %1 をミュート"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:160
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Volume of input %1"
msgstr "入力 %1 の音量"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:197
msgctxt "@action:button fade this Mixer strip up to its full level"
msgid "↗ 100 %"
msgstr "↗ 100%"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:199
msgctxt "@action:button"
msgid "Fade input %1 to 100 %"
msgstr "入力 %1 を 100% へフェード"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:200
msgctxt "@info:tooltip"
msgid "Fade to 100 % over half a second; with Shift, two seconds"
msgstr "0.5 秒かけて 100% へフェードします。Shift を押しながらなら 2 秒です"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:217
msgctxt "@action:button hear only this Mixer strip and any others soloed"
msgid "Solo"
msgstr "ソロ"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:219
msgctxt "@action:button"
msgid "Solo input %1"
msgstr "入力 %1 をソロ"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:220
msgctxt "@info:tooltip"
msgid "Hear this input and any others soloed; with Alt, only this one"
msgstr "この入力と、ソロにしたほかの入力を聞きます。Alt を押しながらなら、この入力だけを聞きます"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:241
msgctxt "@label the left end of a balance slider"
msgid "L"
msgstr "L"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:259
msgctxt "@label:slider"
msgid "Balance of input %1"
msgstr "入力 %1 のバランス"

#: blocks/mixer/ui/MixerStrip.qml:279
msgctxt "@label the right end of a balance slider"
msgid "R"
msgstr "R"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:18
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"Sends the sound through a trained model from a folder you choose, and plays "
"what the model makes of it: for example with the noise taken out, or spoken "
"in another voice."
msgstr "選択したフォルダにある学習済みモデルに音を通し、モデルが作り出した音を再生します。たとえば、ノイズを取り除いた音や、別の声で話した音です。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"A model is a file made by training a program on many examples. This block "
"runs one while the sound plays. The model runs in a separate process, so a "
"model that is slow or crashes cannot stop the session or the other lanes."
msgstr ""
"モデルとは、プログラムに多くの例を学習させて作ったファイルです。このブロックは、音の再生中にモデルを実行します。モデルは別のプロセスで動くので、モデルが遅かったりクラッシュしたりしても、セッションや他のレーンが止まることはありません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"Reverblabr includes no models and never downloads one. You choose a folder "
"that you already have, and the terms of that model are yours to read."
msgstr ""
"Reverblabr "
"にはモデルが含まれておらず、モデルをダウンロードすることもありません。手元にあるフォルダを選んでください。そのモデルの利用条件は、各自で確認してください。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"Sound only leaves this block after the model has processed it. In every other"
" case the block is silent, and the sound does not reach the next block "
"either. That holds when no model is chosen, while one loads, when one cannot "
"be loaded, when it falls behind, when its process stops and restarts, when it"
" gives back something that is not sound, and when the block is switched off. "
"The card says why it is silent."
msgstr ""
"音は、モデルが処理した後にだけこのブロックから出ます。それ以外の場合、ブロックは無音になり、次のブロックにも音は届きません。モデルが選択されていないとき、読み込み中、読み込めないとき、処理が遅れたとき、プロセスが停止して再起動するとき、音ではないものを返したとき、ブロックがオフのときがこれに当たります。無音の理由は設定パネルに表示されます。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:35
#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:166
msgctxt "@title:group the folder a Model block runs"
msgid "Model Folder"
msgstr "モデルフォルダ"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:37
#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:195
msgctxt "@action:button choose the folder that holds a model"
msgid "Choose Folder…"
msgstr "フォルダを選択…"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:38
#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:205
msgctxt "@action:button stop using the model folder"
msgid "Remove Folder"
msgstr "フォルダを外す"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:39
#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:280
msgctxt "@action:button read a model's licence file"
msgid "Open Licence"
msgstr "ライセンスを開く"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:42
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"Choose Folder… picks the folder that holds the model. The line under it says "
"what kind of model it found, or why it cannot use the folder. Remove Folder "
"stops using it."
msgstr ""
"「フォルダを選択…」で、モデルが入っているフォルダを選びます。その下の行に、見つかったモデルの種類、またはフォルダを使えない理由が表示されます。「フォルダを外す」で、そのフォルダの使用をやめます。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:43
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"This version runs a streaming DeepFilterNet model, for noise cleanup, a voice"
" conversion model, and any ONNX model whose folder has a file called "
"reverblabr-model.json that says how to call it. The Model section of the "
"blocks guide lists what that file holds."
msgstr ""
"このバージョンで実行できるのは、ノイズ除去用のストリーミング型 DeepFilterNet モデル、声質変換モデル、そして呼び出し方を記述した "
"reverblabr-model.json というファイルがフォルダにある任意の ONNX "
"モデルです。このファイルに書く内容は、ブロックガイドの「モデル」の節に記載されています。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:44
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"A voice conversion model is three ONNX files in one folder: the voice, a "
"content encoder that hears what is said, and a pitch estimator that hears how"
" high it is. The last two are the same for many voices, and the card says "
"which one is missing."
msgstr ""
"声質変換モデルは、1 つのフォルダに入った 3 つの ONNX ファイルでできています: "
"声そのもの、話している内容を聞き取るコンテンツエンコーダ、声の高さを聞き取るピッチ推定器です。後の 2 "
"つは多くの声で共通で、足りないものがあれば設定パネルに表示されます。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:45
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"If the folder has a licence file, the card names it and Open Licence shows "
"it. If it has none, the card says so."
msgstr ""
"フォルダにライセンスファイルがあれば、設定パネルにそのファイル名が表示され、「ライセンスを開く」で内容を表示できます。ない場合は、設定パネルにそう表示されます。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:46
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"Files that can run code when they are opened, such as .pt, .pth, .ckpt and "
".pkl, are never opened. Use an ONNX version of the model."
msgstr ""
".pt、.pth、.ckpt、.pkl など、開くとコードを実行できてしまうファイルは決して開きません。ONNX 版のモデルを使ってください。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:52
#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:304
msgctxt "@label:spinbox how far a voice is moved up or down, in semitones"
msgid "Pitch shift"
msgstr "ピッチシフト"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:54
#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:294
msgctxt "@title:group the settings of a voice in a Model block"
msgid "Voice"
msgstr "声"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:57
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"Shown for a voice. How many semitones higher or lower the voice speaks than "
"you do, from 24 down to 24 up. A voice sounds most like itself near its own "
"pitch, so a man using a woman's voice may want about 12 up, and the other way"
" round about 12 down. The change takes effect within a moment and the sound "
"does not stop."
msgstr ""
"声のモデルのときに表示されます。声を自分の声より何半音高く、または低くするかを、24 半音下から 24 "
"半音上までの範囲で設定します。声は本来の高さに近いほど、その声らしく聞こえます。そのため、男性が女性の声を使う場合は約 12 半音上げ、逆の場合は約 12"
" 半音下げるとよいでしょう。変更はすぐに反映され、音が途切れることはありません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:58
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"A voice always runs once, on the two sides mixed, and both sides play it."
msgstr "声のモデルは常に、左右を混ぜた音に対して 1 回だけ実行され、その結果を左右の両方で再生します。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:59
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid "Use only voices you have the right to use."
msgstr "使用する権利のある声だけを使ってください。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:65
#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:323
msgctxt "@label:listbox the time a Model block allows a model for each run"
msgid "Spare time"
msgstr "猶予時間"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:67
#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:315
msgctxt "@title:group how a Model block runs its model"
msgid "Running"
msgstr "実行"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:70
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"How much time the model is given, from 20 to 250 thousandths of a second. A "
"new block starts at 50. It is part of the delay: less is a shorter delay, and"
" more gives a slow model room. Reverblabr keeps the other lanes in step with "
"that delay."
msgstr ""
"モデルに与える時間を、20〜250 ミリ秒の範囲で設定します。新しいブロックでは 50 です。この時間は遅延の一部です: "
"短くすると遅延が短くなり、長くすると遅いモデルにも余裕ができます。Reverblabr は、他のレーンをこの遅延に合わせます。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:71
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"A voice takes far longer than a cleanup model, so its delay holds time for "
"that as well, and Delay on the card says what the whole of it comes to, "
"usually about 0.4 seconds."
msgstr ""
"声のモデルはノイズ除去モデルよりはるかに時間がかかるため、その分の時間も遅延に含まれます。合計は設定パネルの「遅延」に表示され、通常は約 0.4 秒です。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:72
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"If the block says it cannot keep up, choose a longer time. If the model's "
"Time used is above 100 %, it is too slow for this computer at any setting."
msgstr ""
"処理が追いつかないとブロックに表示された場合は、より長い時間を選んでください。モデルの「使用時間」が 100% "
"を超える場合、どの設定でもこのコンピュータには遅すぎます。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:78
#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:334
msgctxt "@label:listbox what a mono model does with a stereo lane"
msgid "Mono models"
msgstr "モノラルモデル"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:80
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"Most models take one channel. Once a side runs the model twice, which keeps "
"the stereo picture and takes twice the work. On the sides mixed runs it once "
"on the two sides together, and both sides then play the result."
msgstr ""
"ほとんどのモデルは 1 チャンネルを受け取ります。「片側ずつ」はモデルを 2 回実行するので、ステレオ感が保たれますが、処理は 2 "
"倍になります。「左右を混ぜて」は、左右を合わせた音に対して 1 回だけ実行し、その結果を左右の両方で再生します。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:86 blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:86
msgctxt "@label what a Model block is doing"
msgid "State"
msgstr "状態"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:88
#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:129
msgctxt "@label how late a Model block's output is"
msgid "Delay"
msgstr "遅延"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:89
#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:150
msgctxt "@label how much of the available time a Model block's model uses"
msgid "Time used"
msgstr "使用時間"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:90
#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:115
msgctxt "@action:button start a Model block's model again after it failed"
msgid "Try Again"
msgstr "再試行"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:93
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"Not a setting: what the block is doing, how late the sound is, and how much "
"of the time it has the model is using."
msgstr "設定ではありません: ブロックの動作状況、音の遅れ、与えられた時間のうちモデルが使っている割合を示します。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:94
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"A process that crashes is started again by itself. After three crashes in a "
"minute the block stays silent and says Failed, and Try Again starts it once "
"more."
msgstr ""
"クラッシュしたプロセスは自動的に再起動します。1 分間に 3 "
"回クラッシュすると、ブロックは無音のままになって「失敗」と表示されます。「再試行」で、もう一度起動できます。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:101
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"You have a noise cleanup model, and want it on your microphone or on a call."
msgstr "ノイズ除去モデルがあり、マイクや通話に使いたいとき。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:102
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"You have a voice conversion model, and want to speak in that voice. The delay"
" is too long to hear yourself comfortably while you talk."
msgstr "声質変換モデルがあり、その声で話したいとき。ただし遅延が長いため、話しながら自分の声を快適に聞くことはできません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:103
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"You have an ONNX model that takes sound and gives sound, and want to hear it "
"live."
msgstr "音を受け取って音を返す ONNX モデルがあり、それをリアルタイムで聞きたいとき。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:110
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid "If the sound drops out, look at the card first: it says why."
msgstr "音が途切れたら、まず設定パネルを見てください: 理由が表示されています。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelHelp.qml:111
msgctxt "@info help page of the Model block"
msgid ""
"Keep a second lane around the block if you need to hear the original while "
"you try a model."
msgstr "モデルを試しながら元の音も聞きたい場合は、このブロックを迂回する 2 本目のレーンを用意してください。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:137
msgctxt "@info a delay in milliseconds, '63.0 ms'"
msgid "%1 ms"
msgstr "%1 ms"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:158
msgctxt "@info a share of the time a model has, '34 %'"
msgid "%1 %"
msgstr "%1%"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:178
msgctxt "@info a Model block with no folder chosen"
msgid "No folder chosen"
msgstr "フォルダ未選択"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:222
msgctxt ""
"@info what a Model block's folder holds: the kind of model, its file, its "
"sample rate and channels, 'DeepFilterNet noise cleanup, model.onnx, 48000 Hz,"
" 1 channel'"
msgid "%1, %2, %3 Hz, %4"
msgstr "%1、%2、%3 Hz、%4"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:224
msgctxt "@info how many channels a model takes"
msgid "%1 channel"
msgid_plural "%1 channels"
msgstr[0] "%1 チャンネル"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:238
msgctxt ""
"@info the two files a voice uses beside its own, 'Content encoder: a.onnx. "
"Pitch estimator: b.onnx.'"
msgid "Content encoder: %1. Pitch estimator: %2."
msgstr "コンテンツエンコーダ: %1。ピッチ推定器: %2。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:266
msgctxt "@info the file that says on what terms a model may be used"
msgid "Licence file: %1"
msgstr "ライセンスファイル: %1"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:269
msgctxt "@info a model's folder has no licence file"
msgid ""
"No licence file in this folder. Check the model's terms where you got it."
msgstr "このフォルダにはライセンスファイルがありません。モデルの入手元で利用条件を確認してください。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:287
msgctxt "@info what a Model block's folder has to hold"
msgid ""
"A folder with an ONNX model. Reverblabr never downloads a model and includes "
"none."
msgstr "ONNX モデルが入ったフォルダです。Reverblabr はモデルをダウンロードせず、同梱もしていません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:309
msgctxt "@info what the pitch shift of a Model block means"
msgid ""
"How many semitones higher or lower the voice speaks than you do. Twelve is an"
" octave; try that when the voice is much higher or lower than yours."
msgstr ""
"声を自分の声より何半音高く、または低くするかです。12 半音で 1 オクターブです。声が自分の声よりずっと高いか低い場合は、12 を試してください。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:339
msgctxt "@info what a Model block does when it has nothing to give"
msgid ""
"Sound only leaves this block after the model has processed it. In every other"
" case the block is silent, even when it is switched off."
msgstr "音は、モデルが処理した後にだけこのブロックから出ます。それ以外の場合は、オフのときも含めて無音になります。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelPanel.qml:346
msgctxt "@title:window"
msgid "Choose a Model Folder"
msgstr "モデルフォルダを選択"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:68
msgctxt "@info a Model block switched off"
msgid "Off"
msgstr "オフ"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:71
msgctxt "@info a Model block with no folder chosen"
msgid "No model"
msgstr "モデルなし"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:75
msgctxt "@info a Model block whose model is loading"
msgid "Loading"
msgstr "読み込み中"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:77
msgctxt "@info a Model block processing sound"
msgid "Running"
msgstr "実行中"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:79
msgctxt "@info a Model block whose model is too slow"
msgid "Cannot keep up"
msgstr "処理が追いつかない"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:81
msgctxt "@info a Model block whose model will not run"
msgid "Failed"
msgstr "失敗"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:83
msgctxt "@info a Model block whose model's process is starting again"
msgid "Restarting"
msgstr "再起動中"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:85
msgctxt "@info a Model block whose model gave back something that is not sound"
msgid "Bad output"
msgstr "不正な出力"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:87
msgctxt "@info a Model block in a session that is not running"
msgid "Not running"
msgstr "停止中"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:92
msgctxt ""
"@info a Model block running, and how late the sound is, 'Running, 63 ms'"
msgid "Running, %1 ms"
msgstr "実行中、%1 ms"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:104
msgctxt "@info why a Model block is silent"
msgid "Silent: this block is switched off. No sound passes through it."
msgstr "無音: このブロックはオフです。音は通りません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:108
msgctxt "@info why a Model block is silent"
msgid ""
"Silent: no model is chosen. Sound only leaves this block after a model has "
"processed it."
msgstr "無音: モデルが選択されていません。音は、モデルが処理した後にだけこのブロックから出ます。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:112
msgctxt "@info why a Model block is silent"
msgid "Silent: the model is still loading."
msgstr "無音: モデルを読み込み中です。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:116
msgctxt "@info why a Model block is silent"
msgid ""
"Silent: the session's cycle is longer than Spare time allows. Choose a longer"
" Spare time."
msgstr "無音: セッションのオーディオサイクルが、「猶予時間」で許される長さを超えています。「猶予時間」をもっと長くしてください。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:118
msgctxt "@info why a Model block is silent"
msgid ""
"Silent for now: the model is not finishing in time, and nothing else may "
"leave this block."
msgstr "一時的に無音: モデルの処理が間に合っておらず、それ以外の音はこのブロックから出せません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:121
msgctxt ""
"@info why a Model block is silent, then the reason, 'Silent: the folder is "
"not there.'"
msgid "Silent: %1"
msgstr "無音: %1"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:124
msgctxt "@info why a Model block is silent"
msgid "Silent: the model's process stopped, and it is being started again."
msgstr "無音: モデルのプロセスが停止したため、再起動しています。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:127
msgctxt "@info why a Model block is silent"
msgid "Silent: the model gave back something that is not sound."
msgstr "無音: モデルが音ではないものを返しました。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:129
msgctxt "@info why a Model block is silent"
msgid "Silent: the session is not running."
msgstr "無音: セッションが実行されていません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:136
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid "The folder is not there, or cannot be read."
msgstr "フォルダが存在しないか、読み取れません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:138
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid "The folder holds no model this version can read."
msgstr "このバージョンで読み込めるモデルが、フォルダにありません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:140
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid "reverblabr-model.json cannot be read, or a value in it is out of range."
msgstr "reverblabr-model.json を読み取れないか、範囲外の値が含まれています。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:142
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid "The model file is larger than 2 GiB."
msgstr "モデルファイルが 2 GiB を超えています。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:144
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid "The file is damaged, or is not a model."
msgstr "ファイルが壊れているか、モデルではありません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:146
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid ""
"The folder only holds files that can run code when opened (.pt, .pth, .ckpt, "
".pkl). They are never opened. Use an ONNX version of the model."
msgstr ""
"フォルダには、開くとコードを実行できてしまうファイル（.pt、.pth、.ckpt、.pkl）しかありません。これらは決して開きません。ONNX "
"版のモデルを使ってください。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:148
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid "The model asks for a file outside its folder, and that is refused."
msgstr "モデルがフォルダ外のファイルを要求したため、拒否しました。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:150
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid "This kind of model is recognised, but this version cannot run it yet."
msgstr "この種類のモデルは認識できますが、このバージョンではまだ実行できません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:152
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid "The model's inputs and outputs are not what its description says."
msgstr "モデルの入力と出力が、記述された内容と一致しません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:154
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's model cannot be run"
msgid "The model could not be loaded."
msgstr "モデルを読み込めませんでした。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:156
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's model cannot be run"
msgid "The model's process crashed three times in a minute."
msgstr "モデルのプロセスが 1 分間に 3 回クラッシュしました。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:158
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's model cannot be run"
msgid "The program that runs models could not be started."
msgstr "モデルを実行するプログラムを起動できませんでした。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:160
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's model cannot be run"
msgid "The model took more than two minutes to load."
msgstr "モデルの読み込みに 2 分以上かかりました。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:162
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid ""
"This model is of an unknown kind. Add a reverblabr-model.json to its folder "
"to describe it."
msgstr "このモデルは種類が不明です。フォルダに reverblabr-model.json を追加して、モデルを記述してください。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:164
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's model cannot be run"
msgid "The model's sample rate cannot be converted from the session's."
msgstr "セッションのサンプルレートを、モデルのサンプルレートに変換できません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:166
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid ""
"This voice also needs a content encoder in the same folder: an ONNX file such"
" as vec-768-layer-12.onnx."
msgstr "この声には、同じフォルダにコンテンツエンコーダも必要です: vec-768-layer-12.onnx のような ONNX ファイルです。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:168
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid ""
"This voice also needs a pitch estimator in the same folder: an ONNX file such"
" as rmvpe.onnx."
msgstr "この声には、同じフォルダにピッチ推定器も必要です: rmvpe.onnx のような ONNX ファイルです。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:170
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid ""
"This folder has a content encoder or a pitch estimator, but no voice. Add the"
" voice as an ONNX file. A .pth file is never opened."
msgstr ""
"このフォルダにはコンテンツエンコーダかピッチ推定器はありますが、声がありません。声を ONNX ファイルとして追加してください。.pth "
"ファイルは決して開きません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:172
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's folder cannot be used"
msgid ""
"The content encoder in this folder was made for another kind of voice. This "
"voice needs the encoder it was trained with."
msgstr "このフォルダのコンテンツエンコーダは、別の種類の声用に作られたものです。この声には、学習時に使ったエンコーダが必要です。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:174
msgctxt "@info why a Model block's model cannot be run"
msgid "The model will not run."
msgstr "モデルを実行できません。"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:181
msgctxt "@info a kind of model"
msgid "Model described by its configuration"
msgstr "設定ファイルで記述されたモデル"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:183
msgctxt "@info a kind of model"
msgid "DeepFilterNet noise cleanup"
msgstr "DeepFilterNet ノイズ除去"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:185
msgctxt "@info a kind of model"
msgid "Noise cleanup"
msgstr "ノイズ除去"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:187
msgctxt "@info a kind of model"
msgid "Voice conversion"
msgstr "声質変換"

#: blocks/modelblock/ui/ModelState.qml:189
msgctxt "@info a kind of model"
msgid "Speech through a language model"
msgstr "言語モデルを介した音声"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerFace.qml:43
msgctxt "@info:tooltip a Mono Enhancer's setting, 'Width above 500 Hz'"
msgid "Width above %1"
msgstr "%1 以上を広げる"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerFace.qml:90
msgctxt "@label what the number on a Mono Enhancer tile is"
msgid "crossover"
msgstr "クロスオーバー"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerFace.qml:107
msgctxt "@label:slider where a Mono Enhancer's width starts"
msgid "Crossover"
msgstr "クロスオーバー"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:17
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"Makes a mono recording sound wider in stereo, and still sounds just as it did"
" when it is played in mono."
msgstr "モノラル録音をステレオで広がりのある音にします。モノラルで再生したときは元のままに聞こえます。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:22
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"A mono recording has one channel. Played on two speakers, the same sound "
"comes out of both, so it seems to come from a single point between them."
msgstr "モノラル録音のチャンネルは 1 つです。2 つのスピーカーで再生すると両方から同じ音が出るので、その間の 1 点から聞こえるように感じます。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"This block makes the two sides a little different from each other above a "
"frequency you choose. It adds a copy of the higher sounds, twelve thousandths"
" of a second late, to one side, and takes the same copy away from the other. "
"That is far too short to hear as an echo; the ear hears it as width."
msgstr ""
"このブロックは、選んだ周波数より上で左右を少しだけ違う音にします。高い音のコピーを 1000 分の 12 "
"秒遅らせて片側に加え、同じコピーをもう片側から差し引きます。これはエコーとして聞こえるにはあまりに短く、耳には広がりとして聞こえます。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"Because one side gains what the other loses, the two sides always add back up"
" to the sound that went in. Played on one speaker, or mixed down to mono "
"later, it sounds exactly as it did."
msgstr ""
"片側が得た分をもう片側が失うので、左右を足し合わせると常に入ってきた音に戻ります。1 "
"つのスピーカーで再生しても、後でモノラルにまとめても、元のままに聞こえます。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"Below the chosen frequency nothing is added, so the bass stays in the middle,"
" where it sounds firm."
msgstr "選んだ周波数より下には何も加えないので、低音は中央にとどまり、しっかりと聞こえます。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"A stereo source is first made mono, by averaging its two sides, so its own "
"stereo is replaced by the block's width."
msgstr "ステレオの音源は、まず左右を平均してモノラルにするので、元のステレオはこのブロックの広がりに置き換わります。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:36
#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerPanel.qml:54
#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerPanel.qml:78
msgctxt "@label:slider where a Mono Enhancer's width starts"
msgid "Crossover frequency"
msgstr "クロスオーバー周波数"

#. i18n: Hz stands for hertz, kHz for kilohertz.
#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:39
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"Where the width starts, in hertz (Hz), from 100 Hz to 2 kHz. Everything above"
" it is spread out; everything below it stays in the middle. A new block "
"starts at 500 Hz."
msgstr ""
"広がりが始まる周波数で、単位はヘルツ（Hz）、100 Hz から 2 kHz "
"までです。これより上はすべて広げられ、下はすべて中央にとどまります。新しいブロックは 500 Hz から始まります。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:40
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"Lower spreads more of the sound, including the body of a voice. Higher "
"spreads only the brighter part and keeps more of the sound in the middle."
msgstr "低くすると、声の芯も含めて音のより多くの部分が広がります。高くすると明るい部分だけが広がり、音の多くが中央に残ります。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:41
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"The slider gives each octave, a doubling of the frequency, the same room. The"
" change glides in, so you can drag it while you listen."
msgstr ""
"スライダーでは、オクターブ（周波数が 2 倍になる幅）ごとに同じ幅が割り当てられています。変化は滑らかに反映されるので、聞きながらドラッグできます。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:48
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"An old recording, a radio show or a phone call is in mono and sounds narrow "
"on headphones."
msgstr "古い録音、ラジオ番組、電話の音声がモノラルで、ヘッドホンで聞くと狭く感じるとき。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:49
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"A mono microphone should feel less flat, and the result must still work for "
"listeners in mono."
msgstr "モノラルのマイクの音をもっと立体的にしたいが、モノラルで聞く人にも問題なく聞こえるようにしたいとき。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:56
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"Listen on headphones or with the speakers apart while you set it: that is "
"where the width is heard."
msgstr "設定するときは、ヘッドホンか、離して置いたスピーカーで聞いてください: 広がりが聞こえるのはその環境です。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:57
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"Start at 500 Hz. If a voice starts to sound hollow, raise the crossover."
msgstr "500 Hz から始めてください。声がうつろに聞こえ始めたら、クロスオーバーを上げてください。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerHelp.qml:58
msgctxt "@info help page of the Mono Enhancer block"
msgid ""
"Do not use it on a recording that is already stereo: its own left and right "
"would be lost."
msgstr "すでにステレオの録音には使わないでください: 元の左右が失われてしまいます。"

#: blocks/monoenhancer/ui/MonoEnhancerPanel.qml:99
msgctxt "@info what the Mono Enhancer does"
msgid ""
"Spreads a mono recording across the two sides above this frequency, and "
"leaves the bass in the middle. Played in mono it sounds as it did."
msgstr "この周波数より上でモノラル録音を左右に広げ、低音は中央に残します。モノラルで再生すると元のままに聞こえます。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorFace.qml:60
msgctxt "@info accessible name of a multiband compressor's tile"
msgid "Multiband Compressor, %1"
msgstr "マルチバンドコンプレッサー、%1"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:19
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"Three compressors side by side: one for the low sounds, one for the middle "
"and one for the high. Each evens out its own part of the sound, so one part "
"cannot pull the others down with it."
msgstr ""
"3 つのコンプレッサーを並べたものです: 低い音用、中ほどの音用、高い音用が 1 "
"つずつあります。それぞれが自分の受け持つ部分の音量をならすので、ある部分につられて他の部分まで下がることがありません。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"A compressor turns the sound down when it gets louder than a set level, the "
"threshold, and so brings loud and quiet closer together. An ordinary "
"compressor turns everything down at once: a loud drum or bass note makes the "
"voice above it duck too."
msgstr ""
"コンプレッサーは、音が設定したレベル（スレッショルド）より大きくなると音量を下げ、大きい音と小さい音の差を縮めます。通常のコンプレッサーはすべてを一度に下げるので、大きなドラムやベースの音が鳴ると、その上に乗っている声まで引っ込んでしまいます。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"This block first splits the sound by frequency, from low to high, into three "
"bands: Low, Mid and High. Each band goes through a compressor of its own, "
"with its own settings, and the three are then added back together."
msgstr ""
"このブロックはまず、音を周波数によって、低いほうから「低域」「中域」「高域」の 3 "
"つのバンドに分けます。各バンドは、独自の設定を持つ専用のコンプレッサーを通り、その後 3 つが再び足し合わされます。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"The split itself changes nothing you can hear: with every ratio at 1:1, the "
"sound comes out as it went in. A new block does compress, gently, from −24 dB"
" at 3:1 in every band."
msgstr ""
"分割そのものは、聞こえる音を何も変えません: すべてのレシオが 1:1 なら、音は入ったとおりに出てきます。新しいブロックでは、すべてのバンドで −24 "
"dB から 3:1 の穏やかな圧縮がかかります。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:27
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"Each band is turned down on both sides together, so the stereo picture does "
"not move. The sound is not delayed."
msgstr "各バンドは左右を一緒に下げるので、ステレオの定位は動きません。音は遅れません。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:37
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorPanel.qml:193
msgctxt "@info accessible name of a multiband compressor's bands"
msgid "Bands"
msgstr "バンド"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:39
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandWords.qml:32
msgctxt "@label the lowest of a multiband compressor's three bands"
msgid "Low"
msgstr "低域"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:40
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandWords.qml:34
msgctxt "@label the middle of a multiband compressor's three bands"
msgid "Mid"
msgstr "中域"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:41
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandWords.qml:36
msgctxt "@label the highest of a multiband compressor's three bands"
msgid "High"
msgstr "高域"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:44
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"The strip at the top shows the three bands across the frequencies, from the "
"lowest on the left to the highest on the right. While the session runs, a bar"
" hangs from the top of each band as far as that band is being turned down, "
"and the band shows how many decibels."
msgstr ""
"上部の帯には、3 "
"つのバンドが周波数順に、左端の最も低いものから右端の最も高いものまで並びます。セッションの実行中は、各バンドの上端から、そのバンドが下げられている分だけバーが垂れ下がり、何デシベル下げているかがバンドに表示されます。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:45
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"The two lines between the bands are the splits. Drag one to move where two "
"bands meet."
msgstr "バンドの間にある 2 本の線が境界です。ドラッグすると、2 つのバンドが接する位置を動かせます。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:46
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"Click a band in the strip, or choose Low, Mid or High under it, to pick the "
"band whose curve and settings are shown below. The words beside the buttons "
"say which frequencies the band holds. The panel opens on Mid."
msgstr ""
"帯の中のバンドをクリックするか、その下の「低域」「中域」「高域」を選ぶと、下にカーブと設定を表示するバンドを選べます。ボタンの横の文字は、そのバンドが受け持つ周波数を示します。パネルを開いたときは「中域」が選択されています。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:47
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"The curve shows what the picked band does: how loud the sound goes in, along "
"the bottom, against how loud it comes out, up the side. The dashed line is "
"the sound left alone; where the curve bends below it, the band is turning the"
" sound down. While the session runs, a dot shows where the band's sound is on"
" its curve."
msgstr ""
"カーブは、選択したバンドの働きを示します: "
"横軸が入力の大きさ、縦軸が出力の大きさです。破線は何も処理しない場合の音で、カーブがその下に曲がっているところでは、バンドが音を下げています。セッションの実行中は、そのバンドの音がカーブ上のどこにあるかを点で示します。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:53
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorPanel.qml:126
msgctxt "@label where a band's compressor starts working"
msgid "Threshold"
msgstr "スレッショルド"

#. i18n: dB stands for decibels.
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:56
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"The level where the picked band starts to be turned down, in decibels (dB) "
"below full scale, from −60 dB to 0 dB. Lower means it works on more of the "
"sound. Every band starts at −24 dB."
msgstr ""
"選択したバンドが下げられ始めるレベルを、フルスケールを基準としたデシベル（dB）で、−60 dB〜0 dB "
"の範囲で設定します。低くするほど、より多くの音に働きます。どのバンドも −24 dB から始まります。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:62
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorPanel.qml:128
msgctxt "@label how much of what goes over the threshold comes out"
msgid "Ratio"
msgstr "レシオ"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:64
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"How hard the band is held back above the threshold, from 1:1 to 20:1. At 3:1,"
" where every band starts, a sound 3 dB over the threshold comes out only 1 dB"
" over. At 1:1 the band is left alone."
msgstr ""
"スレッショルドを超えた部分をどれだけ強く抑えるかを、1:1〜20:1 の範囲で設定します。どのバンドも最初は 3:1 で、このときスレッショルドを 3 "
"dB 超えた音は、1 dB 超えるだけになります。1:1 では、バンドに何もしません。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:70
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorPanel.qml:130
msgctxt "@label how fast a band's compressor reacts to the band getting louder"
msgid "Attack"
msgstr "アタック"

#. i18n: ms stands for milliseconds.
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:73
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"How quickly the band is turned down when it gets loud, from a tenth of a "
"millisecond (ms) to 200 ms. A short attack catches sudden sounds; a longer "
"one lets the start of each sound through, which keeps it lively."
msgstr ""
"バンドが大きくなったときに、どれだけ速く下げるかを、0.1 ミリ秒（ms）〜200 ms "
"の範囲で設定します。短いアタックは突然の音を捉え、長いアタックは各音の出だしを通すので、生き生きとした音が保たれます。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:74
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"The bands start at different times: 20 ms for Low, 10 ms for Mid and 3 ms for"
" High. Low sounds are slow waves, and turning them down too quickly would "
"distort them; high sounds can be caught at once."
msgstr ""
"バンドごとに初期値が異なります: 「低域」は 20 ms、「中域」は 10 ms、「高域」は 3 ms "
"です。低い音はゆっくりした波なので、急に下げすぎるとひずんでしまいますが、高い音はすぐに捉えられます。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:80
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorPanel.qml:132
msgctxt "@label how fast a band's compressor lets go once the band is quieter"
msgid "Release"
msgstr "リリース"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:82
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"How quickly the band comes back up once it is quieter, from 10 ms to 3 "
"seconds. The bands start at 250 ms for Low, 150 ms for Mid and 80 ms for "
"High."
msgstr ""
"バンドが小さくなった後、どれだけ速く元に戻すかを、10 ms〜3 秒の範囲で設定します。初期値は「低域」が 250 ms、「中域」が 150 "
"ms、「高域」が 80 ms です。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:83
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"Too short, and the band can flutter with every beat; too long, and it stays "
"turned down after the loud part has passed."
msgstr "短すぎると、ビートのたびにバンドの音量が揺れることがあります。長すぎると、大きな部分が過ぎた後も下がったままになります。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:89
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorPanel.qml:134
msgctxt "@label gain added to a band after it has been held back"
msgid "Makeup"
msgstr "メイクアップ"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:91
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"Turns the band up or down after it has been compressed, from −20 dB to +20 "
"dB, to give back the level compressing took away or to change the balance "
"between the bands. Every band starts at 0 dB."
msgstr ""
"圧縮した後のバンドを −20 dB〜+20 dB の範囲で上げ下げし、圧縮で失われたレベルを取り戻したり、バンド間のバランスを変えたりします。どのバンドも"
" 0 dB から始まります。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:97
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorPanel.qml:136
msgctxt "@label how wide the bend around every band's threshold is"
msgid "Knee"
msgstr "ニー"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:99
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"How gradually compressing starts around the threshold, from 0 dB, a sharp "
"corner, to 24 dB, a wide gentle bend. One knee serves all three bands. A new "
"block uses 6 dB."
msgstr ""
"スレッショルドの付近で圧縮がどれだけ緩やかに始まるかを、0 dB（鋭い角）〜24 dB（広く緩やかな曲線）の範囲で設定します。ニーは 3 "
"つのバンドすべてに共通です。新しいブロックでは 6 dB です。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:100
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"A wider knee eases in, which is harder to hear; a sharp one holds the level "
"more exactly."
msgstr "ニーを広くすると圧縮が徐々にかかるので目立ちにくく、鋭くするとレベルをより正確に抑えられます。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:106
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorPanel.qml:138
msgctxt "@label where the low band ends and the middle begins"
msgid "Low split"
msgstr "低域の境界"

#. i18n: Hz stands for hertz, kHz for kilohertz.
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:109
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"Where the Low band ends and the Mid band begins, in hertz (Hz), from 30 Hz to"
" 2 kHz. A new block splits at 200 Hz."
msgstr ""
"「低域」が終わり「中域」が始まる位置を、ヘルツ（Hz）で、30 Hz〜2 kHz の範囲で設定します。新しいブロックでは 200 Hz で分割します。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:115
#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorPanel.qml:140
msgctxt "@label where the middle band ends and the high begins"
msgid "High split"
msgstr "高域の境界"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:117
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"Where the Mid band ends and the High band begins, from 500 Hz to 16 kHz. A "
"new block splits at 3 kHz."
msgstr "「中域」が終わり「高域」が始まる位置を、500 Hz〜16 kHz の範囲で設定します。新しいブロックでは 3 kHz で分割します。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:118
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"The high split always stays at least one and a half times the low one, so the"
" Mid band never gets too narrow to hold anything. Dragging a split stops "
"there."
msgstr ""
"高域の境界は常に低域の境界の 1.5 倍以上に保たれるので、「中域」が狭くなりすぎることはありません。境界をドラッグしても、そこで止まります。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:125
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid "Music with heavy bass makes the voices in it duck and swell."
msgstr "低音の強い音楽で、声が引っ込んだり膨らんだりするとき。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:126
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid "A voice has sharp, hissing “s” sounds that stand out."
msgstr "声の「s」の音（歯擦音）が鋭く、耳につくとき。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:127
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"You want a loud, even sound for a stream or a podcast, and a single "
"compressor makes it pump."
msgstr "配信やポッドキャスト用に大きく均一な音にしたいのに、コンプレッサー 1 つだと音量が不自然に波打つとき。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:134
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"If you just want an even level, the Simple Compressor is easier. Use this "
"block when one part of the sound is the problem."
msgstr "レベルを均一にしたいだけなら、「簡易コンプレッサー」のほうが簡単です。このブロックは、音の一部分に問題があるときに使ってください。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:135
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid "To work on one band only, set the other two to a ratio of 1:1."
msgstr "1 つのバンドだけを処理するには、他の 2 つのレシオを 1:1 にしてください。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:136
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"To tame sharp “s” sounds, pick High, lower its threshold until its bar moves "
"only on the “s”, and raise its ratio."
msgstr "鋭い「s」の音を抑えるには、「高域」を選び、バーが「s」の音でだけ動くまでスレッショルドを下げてから、レシオを上げてください。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorHelp.qml:137
msgctxt "@info help page of the Multiband Compressor block"
msgid ""
"Watch the bars while the session runs. A band that is always being turned "
"down a lot is set too low: raise its threshold."
msgstr "セッションの実行中はバーを見てください。いつも大きく下げられているバンドは、設定が低すぎます: スレッショルドを上げてください。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorPanel.qml:195
msgctxt "@info a band, where it is, and how much it holds back now"
msgid "%1, %2, %3"
msgstr "%1、%2、%3"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorPanel.qml:379
msgctxt "@info accessible name of a band's compressor curve; the band's name"
msgid "%1 band's curve"
msgstr "%1のカーブ"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandCompressorPanel.qml:461
msgctxt "@info what the Multiband Compressor block does"
msgid ""
"Holds the low, the middle and the high range back each by its own amount, so "
"a loud bass does not pull the voice down with it and a sharp \"s\" can be "
"tamed without dulling the rest. With every ratio at 1:1 the sound comes out "
"as it went in."
msgstr ""
"低域、中域、高域をそれぞれ別の量だけ抑えるので、大きな低音につられて声が下がることがなく、他の部分をこもらせずに鋭い「s」の音を抑えられます。すべてのレシオが"
" 1:1 なら、音は入ったとおりに出てきます。"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandWords.qml:45
msgctxt "@info the frequencies of a multiband compressor's low band"
msgid "Below %1"
msgstr "%1 以下"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandWords.qml:48
msgctxt "@info the frequencies of a multiband compressor's middle band"
msgid "%1 to %2"
msgstr "%1〜%2"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandWords.qml:51
msgctxt "@info the frequencies of a multiband compressor's high band"
msgid "Above %1"
msgstr "%1 以上"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandWords.qml:59
msgctxt "@info a multiband compressor's two split frequencies, low first"
msgid "%1 · %2"
msgstr "%1 · %2"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandWords.qml:67
msgctxt ""
"@info:tooltip a multiband compressor band that does nothing; band name, then "
"its range"
msgid "%1, %2: left alone"
msgstr "%1、%2: 処理なし"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandWords.qml:70
msgctxt ""
"@info:tooltip a multiband compressor band; its name, its range, its threshold"
" and ratio"
msgid "%1, %2: from %3 at %4"
msgstr "%1、%2: %3 から %4 で圧縮"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandWords.qml:78
msgctxt "@info a compressor taking nothing off"
msgid "0 dB"
msgstr "0 dB"

#: blocks/multibandcompressor/ui/MultibandWords.qml:80
msgctxt "@info how much a compressor is taking off; the number has its minus"
msgid "%1 dB"
msgstr "%1 dB"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelFace.qml:41
msgctxt "@info Night Level is switched on"
msgid "On"
msgstr "オン"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelFace.qml:42
msgctxt "@info Night Level is switched off"
msgid "Off"
msgstr "オフ"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelFace.qml:44
msgctxt "@label what a Night Level tile says when the program declares music"
msgid "program says music"
msgstr "プログラムによると音楽"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelFace.qml:50
msgctxt ""
"@info:tooltip what Night Level is set to, 'Loud sounds 100 %, quiet sounds 50"
" %'"
msgid "Loud sounds %1 %, quiet sounds %2 %"
msgstr "大きな音 %1%、小さな音 %2%"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelFace.qml:51
msgctxt "@info:tooltip"
msgid "Set to nothing: passes the sound through"
msgstr "設定なし: 音をそのまま通します"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelFace.qml:69
msgctxt "@info:status spoken, Night Level found a level, 'Speech at -27 LUFS'"
msgid "Speech at %1"
msgstr "話し声 %1"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelFace.qml:73
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:52
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelWords.qml:164
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelWords.qml:191
msgctxt "@info:status Night Level"
msgid "No speech yet"
msgstr "まだ話し声なし"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelGraph.qml:64
msgctxt "@info:whatsthis Night Level's graph"
msgid ""
"Level going out against level coming in, both from the speech level. The "
"numbers are in the line below and in the table."
msgstr "入力レベルに対する出力レベルのグラフで、どちらも話し声のレベルを基準にしています。数値は下の行と表にあります。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelGraph.qml:150
msgctxt "@label an axis of Night Level's graph"
msgid "Level coming in, LU from speech"
msgstr "入力レベル（話し声基準の LU）"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelGraph.qml:157
msgctxt "@label an axis of Night Level's graph"
msgid "Level going out, LU from speech"
msgstr "出力レベル（話し声基準の LU）"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelGraph.qml:200
msgctxt "@label the part of Night Level's graph under its floor"
msgid "not lifted"
msgstr "持ち上げない"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelGraph.qml:212
msgctxt "@label on Night Level's graph"
msgid ""
"speech\n"
"left alone -5 to +3"
msgstr ""
"話し声\n"
"-5〜+3 はそのまま"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelGraph.qml:246
msgctxt "@label the dashed line on Night Level's graph"
msgid "dashed: unchanged"
msgstr "破線: 変化なし"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:17
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"Finds the level of speech in what is playing. Sounds near it stay as they "
"are, louder ones come down, quieter ones come up. Until it hears speech it "
"changes nothing. It can't know what comes next, so a sudden sound can start "
"loud."
msgstr ""
"再生中の音から話し声のレベルを見つけます。それに近い音はそのまま、それより大きい音は下げ、小さい音は持ち上げます。話し声が聞こえるまでは何も変えません。次に何が来るかはわからないため、突然の音は最初だけ大きく聞こえることがあります。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:22
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"A new block is set to nothing. Press Light, Night or Strong on its card to "
"start. Put it after the Application block of the program that plays the film."
" Use one leveller on a lane: this block or Auto Level, not both."
msgstr ""
"新しいブロックは何も設定されていません。設定パネルの「軽め」「夜間」「強め」のいずれかを押して始めてください。映画を再生するプログラムの「アプリケーション」ブロックの後に置いてください。1"
" つのレーンで使うレベル調整は 1 つだけにしてください: このブロックか「オートレベル」のどちらかで、両方は使いません。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:23
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"The block listens for a voice. After about three seconds of speech it has a "
"level, and the tile says it. The level then follows the speech slowly, "
"counting only the time a voice is heard, so one shouted line moves it little."
" With no voice the level stays where it is, and after half a minute the tile "
"says it is held. After 15 minutes of sound with no voice the level is let go,"
" and the block goes back to changing nothing."
msgstr ""
"ブロックは声を探して聞き取ります。約 3 "
"秒間話し声が続くとレベルが決まり、タイルに表示されます。その後レベルは、声が聞こえている時間だけを数えてゆっくりと話し声に追従するので、1 "
"回叫んだくらいではほとんど動きません。声がないとレベルはそのまま保たれ、30 秒たつとタイルに保持中と表示されます。声のない音が 15 "
"分続くとレベルは解除され、ブロックは何も変えない状態に戻ります。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:24
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"The level comes from a voice detector, and it can be wrong. While people talk"
" it reads the voices and everything under them, so it may be the level of the"
" mix more than of the voices. Singing counts as a voice. If the level looks "
"wrong, type one."
msgstr ""
"レベルは声の検出器から得られるもので、誤ることがあります。人が話している間は声とその下にあるすべての音を読み取るので、声のレベルというよりミックス全体のレベルになることがあります。歌声も声として数えられます。レベルがおかしいと思ったら、値を入力してください。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:25
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"Sound from 5 LU under the speech level to 3 LU over it is left alone. Louder "
"sound comes down within a tenth of a second or so. Quieter sound comes up "
"after about four seconds, by at most 10 dB, and never past the speech level. "
"Sound more than 30 LU under speech is not lifted. A line shorter than about "
"three seconds is not lifted either."
msgstr ""
"話し声のレベルより 5 LU 低いところから 3 LU 高いところまでの音はそのままです。それより大きな音は約 0.1 "
"秒以内に下がります。それより小さな音は約 4 秒後に、最大 10 dB まで、話し声のレベルを超えない範囲で持ち上げられます。話し声より 30 LU "
"以上小さい音は持ち上げられません。約 3 秒より短いセリフも持ち上げられません。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:26
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"When a loud sound stops, the gain comes back over a second or two and no "
"faster than 12 dB a second, so a line right after a bang stays a little "
"quiet."
msgstr "大きな音が止むと、ゲインは 1〜2 秒かけて、毎秒 12 dB 以下の速さで戻ります。そのため、大きな音の直後のセリフは少し小さいままです。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:27
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"A limit stops peaks at a level tied to the speech level, or at -1 dBFS with "
"no level found. It is a digital limit, not a level at your ears. It holds the"
" sound back by less than two thousandths of a second, far too little to hear,"
" and that delay stays even with the block set to nothing."
msgstr ""
"制限により、ピークは話し声のレベルに連動したレベルで、レベルが見つかっていない場合は -1 dBFS "
"で止められます。これはデジタル上の制限で、耳に届くレベルではありません。音は 1000 分の 2 "
"秒未満だけ遅れますが、聞き取れないほどわずかです。この遅延は、ブロックを何も設定していないときも残ります。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:28
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"It presses music too, so turn it off for music. Music with no voice finds no "
"level on a new session. After a film, music is pressed around the film's "
"level for up to 15 minutes. If a program declares that it plays music, the "
"tile and the card say so. A program that declares nothing tells the block "
"nothing."
msgstr ""
"音楽も圧縮してしまうので、音楽ではオフにしてください。新しいセッションでは、声のない音楽からはレベルが見つかりません。映画の後は最大 15 "
"分間、音楽が映画のレベルを基準に圧縮されます。プログラムが音楽を再生していると通知すると、タイルと設定パネルにそう表示されます。何も通知しないプログラムからは、ブロックは何も知ることができません。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:29
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"It uses the voice model where the build has one and the session runs at 48 "
"kHz, and Level and rhythm otherwise, which finds levels less often. The card "
"says which."
msgstr ""
"ビルドに音声モデルが含まれ、セッションが 48 kHz "
"で動作している場合は音声モデルを使い、それ以外の場合は「レベルとリズム」を使います。こちらはレベルが見つかる頻度が低くなります。どちらを使っているかは設定パネルに表示されます。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:30
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"The card shows the lowest and highest change of the last minute as a line of "
"numbers. Nothing else is kept, and the level found is not saved."
msgstr ""
"設定パネルには、直近 1 分間の変化量の最小値と最大値が 1 行の数値で表示されます。それ以外は記録されず、見つかったレベルも保存されません。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:37
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"For a film or a show, when the loud parts are too loud for the voices. Put it"
" after the Application block of the program that plays it, before One Ear "
"Mix. For voices on a call use Voice Evener, and for music use neither."
msgstr ""
"映画や番組で、声に比べて大きな場面がうるさすぎるとき。再生するプログラムの「アプリケーション」ブロックの後、「片耳ミックス」の前に置いてください。通話の声には「声量均一化」を使い、音楽にはどちらも使わないでください。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:47
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:188
msgctxt "@label Night Level's choice of amounts"
msgid "How much"
msgstr "強さ"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:49
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelWords.qml:217
msgctxt "@item:inlistbox how much Night Level does"
msgid "Light"
msgstr "軽め"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:50
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelWords.qml:219
msgctxt "@item:inlistbox how much Night Level does"
msgid "Night"
msgstr "夜間"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:51
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelWords.qml:221
msgctxt "@item:inlistbox how much Night Level does"
msgid "Strong"
msgstr "強め"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:54
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"Light sets Loud sounds to 50 % and Quiet sounds to 0 %. Night sets 100 % and "
"50 %. Strong sets 100 % and 100 %. Nothing is picked once you set other "
"amounts."
msgstr ""
"「軽め」は「大きな音」を 50%、「小さな音」を 0% にします。「夜間」は 100% と 50%、「強め」は 100% と 100% "
"です。ほかの値に設定すると、どれも選択されていない状態になります。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:60
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:254
msgctxt "@label where Night Level's speech level comes from"
msgid "Speech level"
msgstr "話し声のレベル"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:62
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelWords.qml:230
msgctxt "@item:inlistbox where Night Level's speech level comes from"
msgid "Found"
msgstr "自動検出"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:63
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelWords.qml:232
msgctxt "@item:inlistbox where Night Level's speech level comes from"
msgid "Typed"
msgstr "手動指定"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:64
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:297
msgctxt "@label:slider Night Level's speech level, typed"
msgid "Typed level"
msgstr "指定レベル"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:67
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"Found uses the level the block heard. Typed uses a level you give it from the"
" first second and never lets it go. It starts from the level found, or from "
"-28 LUFS with none. The block goes on listening, so going back to Found is "
"immediate."
msgstr ""
"「自動検出」は、ブロックが聞き取ったレベルを使います。「手動指定」は、指定したレベルを最初の 1 "
"秒から使い、決して手放しません。初期値は見つかったレベルで、見つかっていない場合は -28 LUFS "
"です。ブロックは聞き取りを続けているので、「自動検出」に戻すとすぐに反映されます。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:73
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:344
msgctxt "@label:slider how far Night Level turns loud sounds down"
msgid "Loud sounds"
msgstr "大きな音"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:75
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"How far sound over the speech level comes down. At 100 % a sound 20 LU over "
"speech ends 9.8 LU over it."
msgstr "話し声のレベルを超える音をどれだけ下げるかです。100% では、話し声より 20 LU 大きい音が 9.8 LU 大きい音になります。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:81
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:359
msgctxt "@label:slider how far Night Level lifts quiet sounds"
msgid "Quiet sounds"
msgstr "小さな音"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:83
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"How far sound under the speech level comes up. At 100 % a sound 20 LU under "
"speech ends 14 LU under it."
msgstr "話し声のレベルを下回る音をどれだけ持ち上げるかです。100% では、話し声より 20 LU 小さい音が 14 LU 小さい音になります。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:88
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:308
msgctxt "@title:group Night Level's graph"
msgid "Level in and out"
msgstr "入出力レベル"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:89
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:412
msgctxt "@title:group Night Level's graph as numbers"
msgid "Graph as a table"
msgstr "グラフを表で表示"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:91
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"Both axes count from the speech level, so 0 is the speech and +10 is 10 LU "
"louder than voices. The shaded strip is left alone. The dot is the last 400 "
"ms and the change made now, so it leaves the curve while the change is on its"
" way. The same figures are in the table."
msgstr ""
"どちらの軸も話し声のレベルを基準にしているので、0 が話し声、+10 は声より 10 LU 大きい音です。影の付いた帯の範囲はそのままです。点は直近 "
"400 ms と現在の変化量を示すので、変化の途中ではカーブから外れます。同じ数値が表にもあります。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:98
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"Start with Light. It lifts nothing, so the quiet parts stay as they are."
msgstr "まずは「軽め」から始めてください。何も持ち上げないので、静かな部分はそのままです。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:99
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"If speech seems to be turned down, the level found may be too low. Type a "
"level a little higher."
msgstr "話し声が下げられているように感じる場合は、見つかったレベルが低すぎる可能性があります。少し高めのレベルを入力してください。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelHelp.qml:100
msgctxt "@info help page of the Night Level block"
msgid ""
"Set the volume for the voices as you always would. The first moment of a bang"
" still comes through, so don't rely on the block to hold it."
msgstr ""
"音量はいつもどおり、声に合わせて設定してください。大きな音の最初の瞬間はそのまま出てしまうので、このブロックが抑えてくれると当てにしないでください。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:55
msgctxt "@info under Night Level's typed level"
msgid "Typed. The block goes by this and never lets it go"
msgstr "手動指定。ブロックはこの値に従い、決して手放しません"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:58
msgctxt "@info under Night Level's level"
msgid "Nothing changes until it hears speech"
msgstr "話し声が聞こえるまでは何も変わりません"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:61
msgctxt "@info under Night Level's found level"
msgid "Found on this lane. From a voice detector, it can be wrong."
msgstr "このレーンで検出しました。声の検出器によるもので、誤ることがあります。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:66
msgctxt ""
"@info which detector Night Level uses and why, 'Level and rhythm is "
"listening. This build has no voice model'"
msgid "%1 is listening. %2"
msgstr "「%1」で検出中。%2"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:80
msgctxt "@label the live row of Night Level's table, 'Now -10'"
msgid "Now %1"
msgstr "現在 %1"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:95
msgctxt ""
"@info the sound coming in and going out of Night Level, 'In -30 LUFS · Out "
"-27 LUFS · Change +3 dB'"
msgid "In %1 · Out %2 · Change %3"
msgstr "入力 %1 · 出力 %2 · 変化量 %3"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:298
msgctxt "@label the unit of Typed level"
msgid "LUFS"
msgstr "LUFS"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:345
msgctxt "@label the unit of Loud sounds"
msgid "%"
msgstr "%"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:346
#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:361
msgctxt "@info an amount, '100 %'"
msgid "%1 %"
msgstr "%1%"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:360
msgctxt "@label the unit of Quiet sounds"
msgid "%"
msgstr "%"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:373
msgctxt "@info what Night Level does"
msgid ""
"Keeps speech where it is and brings louder and quieter sounds towards it. For"
" films and shows. It presses music too, so turn it off for music. The speech "
"level comes from a voice detector, and it can be wrong"
msgstr ""
"話し声はそのままに、それより大きい音と小さい音を話し声に近づけます。映画や番組向けです。音楽も圧縮してしまうので、音楽ではオフにしてください。話し声のレベルは声の検出器から得られるもので、誤ることがあります"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:394
msgctxt "@info Night Level when the program in front of it declares music"
msgid ""
"This lane's program says music. This block presses the loud and soft of it. "
"Turn it off, or move the program to a lane of its own."
msgstr ""
"このレーンのプログラムは音楽を再生中と通知しています。このブロックは音楽の強弱も圧縮してしまいます。オフにするか、プログラムを専用のレーンに移してください。"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:413
msgctxt "@info the columns of Night Level's table"
msgid "In, Out, Change"
msgstr "入力、出力、変化量"

#: blocks/nightlevel/ui/NightLevelPanel.qml:421
